{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_7a15e31a7f5644d084437fca","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"echo \"$TALLY_BRIEF\" && cat \"$TALLY_BRIEF\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/96f44cad4fc8a04dcbd2e3c767139e140c6ad57f64ed62037af1a35ac0ec868f.json\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task proxy-tooling: Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\\\",\\\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:ac0ef77b2d4a46a6afa4c3d4d139976417738f45445cfdcbe71883417b22482b\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.\",\"id\":\"proxy-scripts-clean\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"The admitted kernel path and the ported table path execute on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Write scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh per spec claim 4.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4). make-proxy.sh runs inside the container and builds a tiny synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy: the same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, a small lookup table with the shard tensor naming the mmap path expects — reuse the fork's own test scaffolding under tests/models/ inside the fork checkout wherever possible instead of inventing generators. run-proxy.sh serves it single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json. Boundaries: touch only scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/.\",\"id\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:e5bea94a618c21673e727d80dc72777cd31604d0c28385bf83f7b349c10d0bfd\",\"title\":\"Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/proxy-tooling-e5bea94a618c2167\",\"taskId\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"worktreePath\":\"/