{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_4290fa10f72344e8b25b42cd","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && grep -rn \"ngram_vocab_size\\|ple_embed\\|heads_per_ngram\\|layer_types\\|linear_attention\\|num_experts\\|weight_block_size\" specs/flashnext/evidence/*.md docs handoff README.md 2>/dev/null | head -30"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md:343:**[M] 38 of 131 shards present; 57 G on disk; mtimes 21:25–22:06 today; owner `tom:users` (library-fetch chowns to `tom:users`, `hosts/nas/models.nix:146` — but this dir was created BEFORE any catalog row exists, so it was NOT placed by library-fetch).** The download is in flight or partial. `config.json` reads `\"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"]`, `\"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\"`, with `layer_types` alternating `linear_attention` ×3 / `full_attention`, `full_attention_interval: 4`, `hidden_size: 2560`, `head_dim: 256`, `indexer_budget: 2048` **[S]**.\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/innovation-ledger.md:325:6. `layer_types` full-attention count (12 expected from `full_attention_interval: 4`)\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:59:- `from_config()` reads `weight_block_size` from the HF `quantization_config` at\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:64:163:        weight_block_size = cls.get_from_keys_or(config, [\"weight_block_size\"], None)\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:71:This is exactly the checkpoint's shape: `weight_block_size [128,128]` + a 943-entry\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:80:- `block_quant` is set from the presence of `weight_block_size`:\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:143:85:        padded_num_experts = (moe_config.num_experts + 31) // 32 * 32\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:144:86:        if padded_num_experts >= 1024:\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:150:512 experts → `padded_num_experts = 512` → `512 < 1024` → **passes**. **[S]**\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:424:`copy_ple_embedding_shard_`, `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/common/ple.py:71-75` **[S]**:\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:643:  geometry is config-driven (`ngram_vocab_size_base`, `heads_per_ngram`,\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md:644:  `ple_embed_dim`, `make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by` — read at\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md:148:- Matches tensor **names** with `_SHARD_RE = re.compile(r\"layers\\.(\\d+)\\.ple\\.ple_embedding\\.ngram_embedding\\.shard_(\\d+)\\.weight$\")`, `ple_mmap.py:94-96`. [S]\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md:153:**`shard_0` / `shard_1` are NOT TP shards. Confirmed.** [S] Precisely: `shard_i` is the *i*-th **row block of the logical table as stored under its own checkpoint tensor name**, produced by the checkpoint's `split_ngram_parts` split (default 512, `nvidia/ple_layer.py:241`). The mapping is `shard_size = (org_vocab_size + split_ngram_parts - 1) // split_ngram_parts; checkpoint_start = shard_index * shard_size` — written twice, verbatim, at `nvidia/ple_layer.py:502-509` (loader) and `ple_mmap.py:869-891` (`_attach_table`), with a comment at `ple_mmap.py:866-868` calling them \"two self-consistent halves of the same mapping\". [S] The runtime lookup is `shard = uniq // self.shard_size` (`ple_mmap.py:367`) — pure row arithmetic, no `tp_rank` anywhere. TP sharding in the stock path is an *orthogonal* second split applied by `VocabParallelEmbedding` (`vocab_parallel_embedding.py:313-314`), and `copy_ple_embedding_shard_` is what intersects the two (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:534-540`, `tp_start=/tp_end=` from `shard_indices`). [S]\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md:308:embeddings = self.ple_embedding(input_ids, query_start_loc, ngram_context)\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md:323:embeddings = self.ple_embedding(input_ids, query_start_loc, ngram_context)\nspecs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md:329:Therefore the AMD port is **either**: (i) port the whole nvidia FP8 embedding stack too (`Qwen4ExpPLEFp8EmbeddingMethod` `nvidia/ple_layer.py:142-181`, `_get_ple_embedding_quant_method` `:184-207`, `_get_embedding_weight_scale`/`_dequantize_embeddings` `:632-648`, the `quant_config=`/`params_dtype=` plumbing at `:580-589`, and the `:1194` call) — roughly **+80 further lines**; **or** (ii) port only the mmap-specific dequant: read `weight_scale` off the placeholder and multiply, ~10 lines, accepting that env-off AMD FP8 PLE stays unsupported. Either way, **the \"~15-line port\" figur"}],"details":{}}}
