{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note: `test_worklist_shape_and_hygiene` forbids things like \"qwen\" inside the worklist byte string. My scripts also need to avoid banned model family names? That lint applies only to the worklist byte string. But naming F.5: \"Don't put model family names in spec or worklist byte strings\" — only spec/worklist. Scripts may reference the architecture identifier (run-smoke.sh references Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration). Architecture identifiers are not the same as family names like \"qwen\"? \"Qwen4Exp\" contains \"Qwen\"... run-smoke.sh already has it, and the test only scans the worklist. No problem — follow the run-smoke precedent.\n\nNext, add a test file tests/test_proxy_tooling.py modeled after claim 6.4's style: syntax-clean scripts (already covered by test_scripts_are_syntax_clean), plus proxy-specific assertions:\n- run-proxy.sh references results/receipts/proxy.json\n- run-proxy.sh sets VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1\n- run-proxy.sh does NOT pass --enforce-eager together with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 (the fork's guard refuses this; ruling P10) — a good pin!\n- run-proxy.sh runs in PIECEWISE cudagraph mode\n- make-proxy.sh builds under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy, uses weight_block_size 128×128 and 8 experts... (grep for \"weight_block_size\", shard naming `ngram_embedding.shard_`, number of experts).\n- neither script exports env vars that are the target of is-set probes (F.9): assert absence of VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_MOE_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER.\n\nThese mirror the \"package assertions\" style.\n\nNext — details of the config template for the fallback. Let me define the proxy geometry (fallback template when there's no staged config):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],\n  \"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\",\n  \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\",\n  \"hidden_size\": 2560,\n  \"num_hidden_layers\": 8,\n  \"layer_types\": [3×linear, full]×2,\n  \"full_attention_interval\": 4,\n  \"num_attention_heads\": 32? \n```\nHmm hidden 2560, head_dim 256 → num_attention_heads = hidden/head_dim = 10 for a normal model, but qwen3_next uses head_dim independent of hidden (head_dim 256 with num_attention_heads 16, etc.). From the evidence: hidden_size 2560, head_dim 256. Qwen3Next style: q_size = num_heads*head_dim can differ from hidden. I don't know the actual heads count. Keep hidden_size 2560, head_dim 256, num_attention_heads 16 (q dim 4096), num_key_value_heads 2? Arbitrary... for the proxy, only matters for weight shapes. vLLM builds shapes from the config, and my weights must match. Since my fallback writer derives shapes from the same config I write, they'll be consistent.\n\nBut — the bigger risk is config schema completeness for the qwen4_exp config class (indexer, qsa, ple fields, mtp...). If the staged config exists, reuse it and only shrink: safest. Fallback template: include only fields I know + what the config class requires; the fork's config class has defaults (the config must have defaults since HF config.json is the sole source). Shrink the staged config:\n- num_hidden_layers → 8; rebuild layer_types from the pattern\n- num_experts → 8, num_experts_per_tok → 2\n- moe_intermediate_size → round to multiple of 128 and shrink → e.g. 256\n- intermediate_size (dense) → 512?\n- vocab_size → keep? embed_tokens vocab ~150k → embed 150k×2560×2B = 770 MB bf16. Hmm, that's big for \"tiny\". Shrink vocab to 4096. But the tokenizer I copy from the workload has the full vocab; lm_head/embed of 4096 vs tokenizer vocab 152k — vLLM pads vocab to tp/divisor; tokenizer ids > vocab → runtime error on tokenize? Greedy completion from a short ASCII prompt: qwen tokenizer encodes common text with ids less than 4096? No guarantee (byte-fallback ids for common words might be higher). Safer: vocab_size = 32768 (embed 32k×2560×2 = 160 MB, fine), and most common token ids fall under 32k. Also the ngram/PLE padded vocab is derived from org_vocab... shrink ngram_vocab_size_base if present. Hmm, org_vocab for PLE ≠ text vocab? \"The 51.2B-parameter hash-lookup embedding... reads one layer per token\" — the ngram vocab is its own thing (ngram_vocab_size_base etc.). If base config has those fields, shrink them: e.g. ngram_vocab_size_base → 1024, keep heads_per_ngram/ple_embed_dim (small). Table bytes = ngram_vocab × heads × ple_embed_dim... with fp8 row_bytes = heads_per_ngram*ple_embed_dim bytes. Keeping real dims (unknown to me) — shrink base if the field exists.\n\nHonestly, can't perfectly determine this without seeing the real config. The shrink path preserves the field names (copies the actual config and then overrides known keys) — so whatever the real config contains, it stays valid. The fallback template is a last resort, marked as such in output.\n\nAlso `tie_word_embeddings`: false; provide lm_head separately.\n\nQuantization: add quantization_config to the proxy config. Note: the real config.json likely already has a quantization_config — override with {\"quant_method\":\"fp8\",\"weight_block_size\":[128,128]} and drop modules_to_not_convert (so all linears are quantized... wait, I decided earlier to quantize all linears; but hmm — embedding-adjacent modules: VocabParallelEmbedding is unaffected. PLE's key_proj/value_proj linear layers would be fp8-quantized — the PLE FP8 stack handles fp8 embeddings, but are its projections quantized? In the real model they're in modules_to_not_convert (943 entries — the vast majority of modules are not converted; only experts are quantized!). Real model: only mlp.experts.* is quantized. Quantizing everything is a divergence; risk: fp8 path in PLE projection quant — Fp8LinearMethod on key_proj/value_proj is a normal linear; the 0012 patch permits block-fp8 linear on gfx1151. Should work. But a subtle risk remains.\n\n  Alternative that mirrors the workload exactly: generate modules_to_not_convert programmatically: everything except `mlp.experts`. Can I enumerate? Format of the modules_to_not_convert entries in the real checkpoint is unknown (names like \"model.layers.0.mlp.gate\"? \"re:.*linear_attn.*\"?). Fp8Config just does `ignore = lambda prefix: any(re.match(ignore_pattern, prefix)...`? In vLLM's Fp8Config, ignored_layers is a list of regex/strings matched against the module prefix. So I can write modules_to_not_convert as a regex covering all non-expert linears: does vLLM use `re.match(pattern, module_name)` per pattern? Let me recall: Fp8Config.from_config reads modules_to_not_convert; `self.ignored_layers` is used in get_quant_method via `if self.ignore(layer prefix)`. The check is `any(re.match(layer, ...) ...)`? In vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/fp8.py:\n```python\ndef ignore(self, layer_name): return any(re.match(ignore_pattern, layer_name) for ignore_pattern in self.ignored_layers)\n```\nHmm, is re.match pattern→layer or layer→pattern... I think: `any(re.search(pattern, layer_name) ...)`. If patterns are regexes, one entry like `^(?!.*mlp\\.experts).*` is fragile across versions.\n\n  Decision: don't set modules_to_not_convert at all (quantize everything). This is a proxy; its role is to exercise the permitted kernel path and the mmap table path with finite outputs. Quantizing all linears exercises more of the permitted surface (both the 0008 MoE permission and the 0012 linear permission). Document this choice in the script comment.\n\nWait, another consideration: with block_quant and all lineals quantized, `Fp8LinearMethod` needs the TritonFp8BlockScaledMMKernel (permitted by 0012; FN_FP8_LINEAR defaults on). OK.\n\nBut note: qwen3_next linear-attention modules contain Conv1d and other non-Linear modules — automatically not quantized. GatedDeltaNet's A_log/dt_bias are buffers — fine.\n\nNow weight tensor generation details (fallback writer). Shape derivation from config:\n- H = hidden_size; HD = head_dim; NH = num_attention_heads; NKV = num_key_value_heads\n- V = vocab_size (proxy), L layers, E