id in stacked_params_mapping: ...\n    ...\n    param = params_dict[name]\n```\nIf an unknown name comes in → KeyError → loud failure. That's the risk I flagged. So the fallback writer should only emit names guaranteed to exist. Confidence list:\n- model.embed_tokens.weight ✓ (standard)\n- model.norm.weight ✓\n- lm_head.weight ✓\n- Full-attn layers: model.layers.{i}.self_attn.{q_proj,k_proj,v_proj,o_proj}.weight, .self_attn.{q_norm,k_norm}.weight — qwen3 family naming ✓ (qwen3_next follows qwen3 naming with q_norm/k_norm).\n  Hmm — but does Qwen4Exp's full_attention layer use `self_attn` prefix? qwen4_exp/amd/model.py imports Qwen3NextAttention etc. Yes.\n- MoE every layer: model.layers.{i}.mlp.gate.weight [E, H]; experts: model.layers.{i}.mlp.experts.{e}.{gate_proj,up_proj}.weight [M, H] fp8 + weight_scale_inv [ceil(M/128), ceil(H/128)] fp32; down_proj.weight [H, M] + scale.\n  Shared experts if config has shared_expert_intermediate_size>0: mlp.shared_experts.{gate,up,down}_proj... quantize these too? These are linears — the fp8-block path handles them; or bf16? If quantization_config has no ignore list, shared experts are also quantized (they are Linear modules). Emit in fp8+scale for consistency.\n  mlp.gate.weight is not quantized (it's a router, excluded from quant by vLLM's Fp8Config? Router is a ReplicatedLinear; Fp8Config.get_quant_method for the FusedMoE router... router remains unquantized by vLLM convention (the router weight stays in params_dtype). Emit gate.weight bf16.\n- Per-layer PLE: model.layers.{i}.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_{j:05d}.weight (fp8, uint8 rows?) + ...ngram_embedding.weight_scale (fp32 scalar per layer).\n\nShard tensor details: dtype must be one of _FP8_DTYPES (safetensors dtype \"F8_E4M3\"), shape (rows, row_bytes) where row_bytes = heads_per_ngram * ple_embed_dim? From dossier: MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, head_dim) — hmm, embedding_dim = head_dim? row_bytes = head_dim? Table: rows × row_bytes uint8 view of fp8