from /opt/flashnext/build-info.json (read in-container? run-proxy is host-side; grab via podman exec/logs — simpler: include in the serve container's startup command? Just record what's available on host: image name. Fork commit: `podman run --rm $IMAGE cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json` once — cheap, include fork_commit in receipt. Nice touch tying engine identity to the receipt (spec: build receipt names the lane; proxy receipt is graded by receipts-verify's general form).\n\nNow make-proxy.sh structure (host bash):\n- PROXY_DIR host default: \"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint}\"\n- MODEL_DIR host: \"${FN_MODEL_DIR:-/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8}\" (for tokenizer + optional base config)\n- If MODEL_DIR exists, mount: -v \"$MODEL_DIR:/models:ro\"\n- -v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\"\n- ENV: FN_PROXY_LAYERS default 8, FN_PROXY_EXPERTS default 8\n- podman run --rm (no GPU needed for generation! no --device needed) $IMAGE python3 - <<'PY'\n\nInside python:\n```python\nimport json, math, os, re, sys, time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nOUT = Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nMODELS = Path(\"/models\")  # read-only mount if present\nlayers = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_LAYERS\", \"8\"))\nexperts = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_EXPERTS\", \"8\"))\n```\nSteps:\n1. Base config: if MODELS/config.json exists → load; source=\"workload\"; else → template; source=\"template\".\n2. Shrink:\n```python\ncfg[\"architectures\"]  # keep, assert it contains Qwen4Exp id\ncfg[\"num_hidden_layers\"] = layers\n# layer pattern:\ninterval = cfg.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4)\ncfg[\"layer_types\"] = [\"linear_attention\"]*(interval-1)+[\"full_attention\"]  # times\nrepeat to num_hidden_layers\ncfg[\"num_experts\"] = experts\nif \"num_experts_per_tok\" in cfg: cfg[\"num_experts_per_tok\"] = min(cfg[\"num_experts_per_tok\"], experts)\nelse set 2\ncfg[\"moe_intermediate_size\"] = max(128, round to 128, maybe shrink)  # set 256\nif \"intermediate