{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Pair service uses `--network host`. Do the same in the proxy runner too (simpler, no port mapping issues; only bind the port via the serve CLI). Note: `--network host` exposes the port directly on the host.\n\nAlso, mirror the container flags: --ipc host, devices, seccomp, group-add keep-groups, ulimit memlock.\n\nOK let's write the script. run-smoke.sh mounts `-v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\"`, so receipts are written inside the container to /results/receipts/... . run-proxy.sh does the same: mount results at /results, write receipts inside the python heredoc at /results/receipts/proxy.json, and also echo on the host side. Receipt writing is done in host-side python (simpler: host writes receipt after data collection). Collect data in bash variables + podman outputs, then at the end write the receipt via a host python heredoc. Cleaner approach: host python orchestrates the entire API interaction + receipt writing, calling podman via subprocess? run-tp2.sh uses host-side python heredocs that use urllib against FN_API — the host reaches the container port via --network host. ✓ Follow that: bash orchestrates the container lifecycle, and a host python heredoc does polling + completion + assertions + receipt writing.\n\nNow — engagement grep: on the host side do `podman logs $CTR`. ✓\n\nFork commit: `podman run --rm $IMAGE cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json` (cheap) → parse fork_commit. ✓\n\nClean shutdown: vllm serve launched via `podman exec -d` inside a sleep-infinity container? Or a detached container running serve directly? With serve directly: `podman run -d --name CTR ... IMAGE bash -lc \"exec vllm serve ...\"` → container's main process = serve; podman stop → SIGTERM to serve → clean exit → exit code obtainable via inspect ✓. Simpler than sleep-infinity + exec.\n\nNow let's write make-proxy.sh. A complete python generator. Let me draft it carefully.\n\n```python\nimport importlib\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport traceback\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport torch\n\nOUT = Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nMODELS = Path(\"/models\")           # staged workload, ro-mounted if present\nLAYERS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_LAYERS\", \"8\"))\nEXPERTS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_EXPERTS\", \"8\"))\nTOPK = 2\nMOE_INTER = 256                    # multiple of the 128 block size\nBLOCK = 128\nSEED = 42\nwarnings = []\nscaffold = {\"fork_scaffold_candidates\": [], \"reused\": None,\n            \"validation\": []}\n\ndef note(msg):\n    print(f\"make-proxy: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    warnings.append(msg)\n```\n\nStage 1 config:\n\n```python\ndef load_base_config():\n    p = MODELS / \"config.json\"\n    if p.is_file():\n        return json.loads(p.read_text()), f\"workload:{p}\"\n    tmpl = {\n        \"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],\n        \"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\",\n        \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\",\n        \"hidden_size\": 2560,\n        \"head_dim\": 256,\n        \"num_attention_heads\": 16,\n        \"num_key_value_heads\": 2,\n        \"num_hidden_layers\": LAYERS,\n        \"full_attention_interval\": 4,\n        \"layer_types\": [],\n        \"vocab_size\": 4096,\n        \"max_position_embeddings\": 4096,\n        \"rms_norm_eps\": 1e-6,\n        \"tie_word_embeddings\": False,\n        \"use_qk_norm\": True,\n        \"decoder_sparse_step\": 1,\n        \"num_experts\": EXPERTS,\n        \"num_experts_per_tok\": TOPK,\n        \"moe_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"indexer_budget\": 2048,\n        \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 512,\n        \"heads_per_ngram\": 1,\n        \"ple_embed_dim\": 256,\n        \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 128,\n        \"split_ngram_parts\": 2,\n    }\n    return tmpl, \"template:evidence-dotfiles-observed-3.3\"\n```\n\nShrink handling:\n\n```python\ndef shrink(cfg):\n    edits = {}\n    def set_(k, v):\n        edits[k] = [cfg.get(k), v]\n        cfg[k] = v\n    archs = cfg.get(\"architectures\") or []\n    if not any(\"Qwen4Exp\" in a for a in archs):\n        raise SystemExit(f\"make-proxy: base config architectures {archs} carry no Qwen4Exp identifier; refusing to relabel a foreign model as the proxy\")\n    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    interval = cfg.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4)\n    pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\n    set_(\"num_experts\", EXPERTS)\n    set_(\"num_experts_per_tok\", min(int(cfg.get(\"num_experts_per_tok\", TOPK)), EXPERTS))\n    if \"decoder_sparse_step\" in cfg or True:\n        set_(\"decoder_sparse_step\", 1)   # every layer routed-MoE: the admitted kernel runs on every decode\n    set_(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"intermediate_size\", 2 * BLOCK)\n    set_(\"max_position_embeddings\", min(int(cfg.get(\"max_position_embeddings\", 4096)), 4096))\n    # Keep the workload's vocab_size + tokenizer as a pair\n    if not (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file():\n        set_(\"vocab_size\", 4096)\n    # quantization: block-FP8 everywhere a Linear lives; embed/lm_head stay bf16 by loader rule\n    set_(\"quantization_config\", {\"quant_method\": \"fp8\", \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]})\n    # small PLE table\n    for k in list(cfg):\n        if \"ngram\" in k.lower() and re.search(r\"(size|base|vocab)\", k.lower()):\n            v = cfg[k]\n            if isinstance(v, int) and v > 512:\n                set_(k, 512)\n    split_key = next((k for k in cfg if \"split\" in k.lower() and \"ngram\" in k.lower()), None)\n    if split_key:\n        set_(split_key, 2)\n    return edits\n```\n\nHmm wait, \"set_('decoder_sparse_step', 1) or True\" — sloppy; just write set_ unconditionally.\n\nNote: if the workload config has its own quantization_config with modules_to_not_convert — drop it (replaced with the new dict) → quantize all Linears. Then the unknown name problem: linear-attn's Linears are quantized but not provided by fallback writer → uninitialized fp8 → NaN risk. In the introspection path, resolve the name. In fallback... need mitigation.\n\nMitigation idea for fallback: empirically probe the ignore semantics and if regex is accepted use a modules_to_not_convert that covers everything except the expert prefix:\n\n```python\ndef probe_ignore_semantics():\n    try:\n        from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 import Fp8Config\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"Fp8Config probe unavailable: {e}\")\n        return None\n    expert = \"model.layers.3.mlp.experts.4.gate_proj\"\n    other = \"model.layers.3.linear_attn.in_proj_qkvz\"\n    for patterns in (\n        [r\"(?!(.*mlp\\.experts)).*\"],          # negative lookahead regex\n        [r\"^(?!.*mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"],\n    ):\n        try:\n            qc = Fp8Config(weight_block_size=[BLOCK, BLOCK], ignored_layers=list(patterns))\n            # Probe how the skip predicate reads the layer:\n            from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 import Fp8Config as _C\n            # Build a dummy module? get_quant_method needs a layer instance...\n        except Exception as e:\n            ...\n```\nget_quant_method(layer, prefix) needs a layer object with isinstance checks (FusedMoE/LinearBase/EmbeddingBase...). Can we make a fake? `types.SimpleNamespace`? First isinstance(layer, FusedMoEBase)... complicated. Alternative probe target: find the skip helper function itself:\n\n```python\nimport vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 as fp8mod\nimport inspect\nsrc = inspect.getsource(fp8mod)\n```\nAnd grep the source for how ignored_layers is consumed (search for \"ignored_layers\" usages). Then decide the pattern format empirically from the source text (regex or membership). Clever but fragile across versions — still better than guessing. If source shows `prefix in ignored` → literal prefix required → can't enumerate without instantiation → fall back to quantize-all + curated names + NaN risk flag. If `re.match/search(pattern, prefix)` → use lookahead regex or simpler: patterns = [r\"^model\\.layers\\.\\d+\\.(?!mlp\\.experts).*\"] hmm need to cover all top-level non-expert Linears too.\n\nA simpler regex that works under re.match against all non-expert Linears: `r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"` — any prefix not containing .mlp.experts. → skip (unquantized). Expert prefix doesn't match → quantized ✓. If semantics is re.search(pattern, prefix): the pattern is anchored with ^...$ — still works.\n\nLet's go with this empirical probe: source-inspect how ignored_layers is consumed, then validate that our patterns give the desired predicate with re directly (mirror the observed semantics locally), and further if instantiable do a live get_quant_method probe.\n\nAnd last-resort fallback if none of that works: quantize-all + curated writer + honestly manifest the risk + run-proxy's finite-logits assertion grades it anyway.\n\nStage 2 fork scaffolding probe for the PLE writer:\n\n```python\ndef probe_fork_ple_scaffold():\n    \"\"\"Prefer the fork's own tests/models scaffolding over inventing writers\n    (task goal). Tests of the mmap path construct fixture checkpoints with the\n    exact shard naming discover_shards accepts, so any shard writer exposed\n    there is reused as-is.\"\"\"\n    sys.path.insert(0, \"/opt/vllm/tests\")\n    cand = []\n    for modname in (\"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap_amd\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple\"):\n        try:\n            mod = importlib.import_module(modname)\n        except Exception as e:\n            cand.append({\"module\": modname, \"import\": f\"FAIL {e.__class__.__name__}: {e}\"})\n            continue\n        writers = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                   if callable(getattr(mod, n))\n                   and re.search(r\"(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|ckpt|checkpoint|fixture)|fixture.*shard\", n, re.I)]\n        cand.append({\"module\": modname, \"writers\": writers})\n        scaffold[\"fork_scaffold_candidates\"].append(cand[-1])\n    ...\n```\nActually calling an unknown fixture is too risky (pytest fixture objects, kwargs). Limit actual reuse to: importing the module and reading its fixture naming convention? Hmm. Honestly: reuse = (a) validate against the fork's own ple_mmap (_SHARD_RE, discover_shards, dtype map), (b) match the fixture file naming `model-ple-{layer}-{shard:05d}.safetensors`, (c) if a fork test exposes a module-level writer that takes a directory argument, use it. Implement (c) opportunistically: only call if `inspect.signature` has exactly one positional param with default or named path/dir/out/tmp; wrap in try; validate the output via discover_shards; on validation failure delete and use own writer. OK.\n\nStage 3 geometry computation:\n\n```python\ndef ngram_geometry(cfg):\n    base = int(cfg.get(\"ngram_vocab_size_base\", 512))\n    heads = int(cfg.get(\"heads_per_ngram\", 1))\n    div = int(cfg.get(\"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\", 1) or 1)\n    split = int(cfg.get(\"split_ngram_parts\", 512))\n    total = base * heads\n    padded = math.ceil(total / div) * div if div > 1 else total\n    shard_rows = math.ceil(padded / split)\n    return {\"base\": base, \"heads\": heads, \"divisible_by\": div,\n            \"split\": split, \"padded_rows\": padded, \"rows_per_shard\": shard_rows}\n```\nNote in manifest: mirror of the loader's mapping `(org + split - 1)//split`; residual mismatch fails loudly via the discover check.\n\nRow byte width: head_dim? PLE embedding dim: the nvidia side builds MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim) → row = head_dim elements fp8. Use cfg.get(\"head_dim\", cfg.get(\"ple_embed_dim\", 256))... but heads_per_ngram>1 might widen embedding_dim = heads*ple_embed_dim... the VocabParallelEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim) says head_dim. Use head_dim. Validate at runtime if fork importable: if ple_mmap._validate_layer_shards exists, introspect its expected row_bytes? validate_shards_for(model_config, layer_name, head_dim)... the third arg head_dim is passed in → so row_bytes == head_dim. ✓ Confirmed by dossier signature.\n\nStage 4 weight writing. Write a small safetensors serializer + tensor factories. Then a curated writer:\n\n```python\ndef curated_weights(cfg, geom):\n    H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E = EXPERTS; M = MOE_INTER\n    layer_types = cfg[\"layer_types\"]\n    tensors = {}\n    # bf16 factories...\n    emb = randn_bf16((V, H), scale=0.02)\n    tensors[\"model.embed_tokens.weight\"] = emb\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = emb  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    for i, lt in enumerate(layer_types):\n        p = f\"model.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(H)\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(H)\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((NH*HD, H))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((NKV*HD, H))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.v_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((NKV*HD, H))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.o_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((H, NH*HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(HD)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(HD)\n            + scale_inv for each fp8\n        moe block: gate bf16 zeros (E,H); experts fp8 zeros + scales; shared experts fp8 zeros + scales if the config has shared_expert_intermediate_size\n    tensors[\"model.norm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(H)\n```\nfp8 zeros → scale_inv ones. All zeros → finite forward (analyzed earlier). Attention zeros → uniform softmax over seq → OK.\n\nWait, one hazard: if layer_types has linear_attention and we skip its tensors entirely — those Linears are quantized (quantize-all config) → uninitialized fp8 NaN risk. Covered by the ignore-regex probe (then unquantized → init by vLLM's own init? unquantized Linears init via the model's init_weights → finite ✓). So if the ignore probe succeeds, linear-attn stays bf16-init → safe. Attention/experts are quantized and provided → safe. embed/lm_head unquantized by loader rule ✓. So the ignore-regex success → fully safe. Ignore probe failure + quantize-all + unknown names → risk persists (flag it).\n\nHmm — furthermore, with ignore regex active, what about the curated full-attn tensors I write in fp8? If the prefix matches the ignore regex → vLLM expects bf16 unquantized weights but I'm providing fp8 + scale_inv → loader mismatch (dtype/shape error, unknown scale_inv name!). Consistency required: if ignore is active → write full-attn in bf16 and don't emit scale_inv for them; experts are always block-fp8. So parameterize the writer by ignore_active: linear is fp8+scale only when quantized. Experts are quantized in either mode ✓ (regex excludes only non-experts).\n\nStage 5 fork-introspection writer (upgrade path): after config.json exists, attempt model construction; enumerate parameters; derive names. Given the complexity, implement as \"best effort\":\n\n```python\ndef fork_introspect_weights():\n    try:\n        from vllm.config import ModelConfig, VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config\n        from vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry\n        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))   # may need tokenizer ✓ present\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]\n            with torch.device(\"meta\"):\n                model = cls(vllm_config=vc)\n        params = [(n, tuple(p.shape), str(p.dtype)) for n, p in model.named_parameters()]\n        stacked = getattr(model, \"stacked_params_mapping\", [])\n        return params, stacked\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"fork model introspection unavailable: ...\")\n        return None\n```\nModelConfig(model=str(OUT)) signature: ModelConfig(model=..., tokenizer=...?) default tokenizer=model path ✓. The constructor may require more (revision defaults OK). Might error on platform/memory? ModelConfig mostly parses config. Try it; broad except.\n\nIf params obtained → write the tensor list precisely: for each param name:\n- Mapping via stacked: vllm fused name → per-shard HF names (need mapping of shard_id→(hf suffix, slice)). stacked_params_mapping entries: (vllm_suffix, hf_suffix, shard_id). Derivation: vllm name = base + vllm_suffix; HF name = base + hf_suffix (+ .weight). Per-shard shape: slice along dim0 — need slice boundaries... complex for gate_up (equal halves), qkv (per head count). Feasible: compute from config NH/NKV/HD/M. But this introspection upgrade is a bonus path; if shape slicing is wrong → wrong bytes but right names → numerically fine (zeros anyway!). Even with wrong slice size, tensor total size matches the parameter so loader weight_loader errors out? vllm's weight_loader validates shard shape. Zeros everywhere so... slicing must be correct shape-wise. Doable but more code (~60 lines).\n\nTime/complexity budget — introspection upgrade implemented pragmatically:\n- Names: use introspected params;\n- Fused qkv/gate_up: use stacked mapping and config dims to emit HF-split names;\n- Everything else: emit under parameter name (vllm name ≈ usually HF name for non-fused);\n- dtype/quant: name contains \".mlp.experts.\" and is a weight (not scale) → fp8 block + scale_inv; other weights bf16; norms are ones; embeds randn-small; gate is zero;\n- Skip params that look like buffers (rotary inv_freq usually is a buffer so not in named_parameters).\nIf introspection is active, ignore-regex is unnecessary... names are exact → quantize-all is safe only if all quantized Linears are provided. Introspection provides all Linear param names ✓ So with introspection: quantize-all config OK; write fp8+scale for each quantized linear: which are quantized? All Linears except embed/lm_head/router. Parameter name tells us the module kind only heuristically... use ignore probe anyway: quantize-only-experts (ignore regex) + write bf16 for all non-expert params + fp8 for experts → consistent and safe under either semantics... but regex semantics must be verified ✓ (probe). If regex not verified → fall back to quantize-all + fp8 all Linear params + provide all → also consistent! Because introspection lists everything. So:\n\n- Introspection + verified regex → experts fp8, others bf16 (ignore list = the regex).\n- Introspection + regex unverified → quantize-all (no ignore), all Linear/Embedding method params fp8? Embedding is unquantized by loader rule; provide fp8 to params that are quantized Linear (fp8 e4m3 + scale_inv), provide bf16 to others. Which params are quantized Linears? Without the ignore predicate... assume all weight tensors under Linear-ish modules: heuristic on name excluding (embed_tokens, lm_head, norm, gate (router? name mlp.gate.weight — router is Linear! Fp8Config.get_quant_method is FusedMoE router... FusedMoE router: vLLM treats the router weight specially as unquantized (Fp8MoEMethod handles experts; router's ReplicatedLinear gets Fp8LinearMethod?? In FusedMoE the gate/router is created with `self.gate = ReplicatedLinear(..., bias=False)` without quant_method? Hmm FusedMoE creates `self.gate` unquantized (params_dtype) — yes, standard vLLM: router stays in compute dtype). Provide router as bf16 ✓.\n\nEnough already. This adaptive design covers most branches. One more simplification: always quantize all linears except when regex verified (drop ignore); and when introspection is unavailable, curated writer + quantize-all + ignore probe.\n\nOK also handle: what if get_config rejects my synthesized config (unknown extra keys are usually tolerated). If ModelConfig() can't parse (template mode), make-proxy fails loudly — acceptable typed failure.\n\nPLE shard writer:\n\n```python\ndef write_ple(cfg, geom):\n    rows = geom[\"rows_per_shard\"]; rb = head_dim; split = geom[\"split\"]\n    count = 0\n    for layer in range(LAYERS):\n        for s in range(split):\n            name = f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_{s:05d}.weight\"\n            t = fp8_zeros((rows, rb))\n            save_safetensors(OUT / f\"model-ple-{layer}-{s:05d}.safetensors\", {name: t})\n            count += 1\n        scale = f32 ones [1] name ...weight_scale → put in main file? The loader intercepts by (stripped) name; put in main safetensors alongside others.\n```\nWait — does every layer have PLE? If only some layers have a ple module, unknown checkpoint names → ValueError from AutoWeightsLoader per layer... risk either way. Per-layer PLE structure is this model family's signature (PLE = every-layer ngram lookup per dossier §2 \"per lookup, per PLE layer, per forward\"). Emit for all layers; note residual risk in manifest. Hmm... but if wrong → loud failure at serve weight-load (~5 min), typed error, fail receipt — acceptable failure mode for a synthetic campaign.\n\nTokenizer:\n\n```python\ndef stage_tokenizer():\n    copied = []\n    for f in (\"tokenizer.json\", \"tokenizer_config.json\", \"special_tokens_map.json\",\n              \"vocab.json\", \"merges.txt\", \"generation_config.json\", \"chat_template.jinja\"):\n        src = MODELS / f\n        if src.is_file():\n            shutil.copy2(src, OUT / f); copied.append(f)\n    if any(c.startswith(\"tokenizer\") for c in copied): return copied\n    # fallback synthetic WordLevel tokenizer paired with vocab_size 4096\n    ...write tokenizer_config.json + tokenizer.json...\n```\nWordLevel tokenizer.json structure:\n```json\n{\"version\":\"1.0\",\"truncation\":null,\"padding\":null,\"added_tokens\":[{\"id\":0,\"content\":\"<pad>\",\"single_word\":false,\"lstrip\":false,\"rstrip\":false,\"normalized\":false,\"special\":true},... bos1 eos2 unk3],\"normalizer\":{\"type\":\"NFC\"},\"pre_tokenizer\":{\"type\":\"Whitespace\"},\"post_processor\":null,\"decoder\":{\"type\":\"WordLevel\"},\"model\":{\"type\":\"WordLevel\",\"vocab\":{...},\"unk_token\":\"<unk>\"}}\n```\nvocab: special 0-3, then printable ASCII singles, then a few words. Tokenize splits on whitespace; unknown word → unk. Deterministic-ish greedy output will be mostly unk... output text quality irrelevant; finiteness of logits matters. OK.\n\nValidation stage:\n```python\ndef validate_with_fork():\n    try:\n        from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common import ple_mmap\n    except ImportError:\n        try: from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia import ple_mmap\n    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))\n    per_layer counts; compare against split; rows per shard vs geom; dtype map\n    record in scaffold[\"validation\"]\n    mismatch → SystemExit with detail\n```\nReturn found to confirm engagement. discover_shards is functools.cache'd — single call fine.\n\nManifest write + main flow with try/except → traceback to stderr, exit 1 (host bash adds its own message). Manifest always written (best-effort) so run-proxy can report provenance even on failure.\n\nNow host-side bash wrapper details for make-proxy.sh:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Header comment with doctrine\nset -euo pipefail\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nPROXY_DIR=\"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-${FN_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext}/proxy-checkpoint}\"\nMODEL_DIR=\"${FN_MODEL_DIR:-/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8}\"\n\nlog() { echo \"make-proxy: $*\" >&2; }\nmkdir -p \"$PROXY_DIR\"\nfind \"$PROXY_DIR\" -mindepth 1 -delete   # rebuild clean: the proxy is disposable by construction\n\nMOUNTS=(-v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nif [ -f \"$MODEL_DIR/config.json\" ]; then\n  log \"staged workload config present at $MODEL_DIR — shrinking it as the base\"\n  MOUNTS+=(-v \"$MODEL_DIR:/models:ro\")\nfi\n\npodman run --rm \\\n  -e FN_PROXY_LAYERS=\"${FN_PROXY_LAYERS:-8}\" \\\n  -e FN_PROXY_EXPERTS=\"${FN_PROXY_EXPERTS:-8}\" \\\n  \"${MOUNTS[@]}\" \"$IMAGE\" python3 - <<'PY'\n...\nPY\n\nlog \"checkpoint ready at $PROXY_DIR ($(find \"$PROXY_DIR\" -name '*.safetensors' | wc -l) safetensors files)\"\n```\n\nNow run-proxy.sh:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Header: claim 4.1, ruling P10 note, receipt path\nset -euo pipefail\nREPO_ROOT=...\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nPROXY_DIR=\"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-${FN_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext}/proxy-checkpoint}\"\nPORT=\"${FN_PROXY_PORT:-1235}\"\nCTR=\"flashnext-proxy-serve\"\nOUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/proxy.json\"\nBOOT_TIMEOUT=\"${FN_PROXY_BOOT_TIMEOUT:-3600}\"\nAPI=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\"\nmkdir -p \"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\n\nlog() ...\nfail_receipt() { python heredoc to write fail receipt with reason \"$1\"; exit 1; }\n```\nCareful: write_receipt via python reading env vars (mirror build.sh pattern). Write one python receipt writer reused for pass/fail with env: FN_STATUS, FN_DATA_JSON (json string collected). Simpler: build receipt in the final python step; also write fail receipt in traps.\n\nFlow:\n1. Check checkpoint exists: [ -f \"$PROXY_DIR/config.json\" ] || fail \"no checkpoint at $PROXY_DIR — run scripts/make-proxy.sh first\"\n2. Cleanup leftovers: podman rm -f $CTR 2>/dev/null || true\n3. fork/build-info: BUILD_INFO=\"$(podman run --rm \"$IMAGE\" cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json 2>/dev/null || echo '{}')\"\n4. Launch:\n```bash\npodman run -d --name \"$CTR\" \\\n  --network host --ipc host \\\n  --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri \\\n  --security-opt seccomp=unconfined \\\n  --group-add keep-groups --ulimit memlock=-1:-1 \\\n  -v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy:ro\" \\\n  -e VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 \\\n  -e HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 -e VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1 -e VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK=1 \\\n  -e PYTHONHASHSEED=0 \\\n  -e HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1 \\\n  -e PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=\"expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85\" \\\n  \"$IMAGE\" bash -lc \"exec vllm serve /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy \\\n    --served-model-name flashnext-proxy \\\n    --host 127.0.0.1 --port $PORT \\\n    --tensor-parallel-size 1 \\\n    --max-model-len 4096 \\\n    --gpu-memory-utilization 0.6 \\\n    --disable-log-requests \\\n    -cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE\"\n```\nNote: no --enforce-eager; comment explains: the fork's check_cudagraph_safety (per ruling P10) rejects both full-graph capture and bare eager when VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1; piecewise capture with the mmap op as split boundary is the approved first-light mode. Avoid the literal \"--enforce-eager\" inside a comment for my tests? My tests assert absence of that string — keep it absent everywhere, comment uses the \"plain-eager mode\" phrasing.\n\nNote fn-cluster-up.sh warned: don't put comments inside backslash-continuations — leave none.\n\nHmm `--host 127.0.0.1` with --network host: host-side python binds to localhost and reaches it fine.\n\n5. Poll loop in bash or python? Python heredoc for poll + request + assert + receipt (mirrors run-tp2 style):\n```python\nimport json, math, os, subprocess, sys, time, urllib.request, urllib.error\nAPI=os.environ[\"FN_API\"]; CTR=os.environ[\"FN_CTR\"]; ...\ndef podman_logs(): return subprocess.run([\"podman\",\"logs\",CTR],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout+stderr\ndeadline = time.time()+BOOT\nready=False\nwhile time.time()<deadline:\n    if container not running → break fail with log tail\n    try GET /v1/models → if served name present ready=True break\n    sleep 5\n```\nThen completion:\n```python\nbody={\"model\":\"flashnext-proxy\",\"prompt\":\"First light on the proxy: \",\"max_tokens\":16,\"temperature\":0,\"logprobs\":5}\nr=post /v1/completions\ntext=choices[0][\"text\"]; tokens=usage[\"completion_tokens\"]\nlps=[]\nfor ch in choices: \n  tl=ch[\"logprobs\"][\"token_logprobs\"] → extend with non-None\n  top=ch[\"logprobs\"][\"top_logprobs\"] → values of dicts\nfinite = len(lps)>0 and all(math.isfinite(x))\n```\nAssert finite → status.\nEngagement: logs = podman logs; mmap_mentions = count of \"ple_mmap\"; engaged = mentions>0. If VLLM_PLE_MMAP didn't engage → fail (claim requires engagement).\n6. Shutdown (bash after python? keep inside same python via subprocess): podman stop -t 120 CTR; inspect ExitCode; rm. clean = exit==0.\n7. Receipt data: {checkpoint, manifest (from PROXY_DIR/proxy-manifest.json if present), engine:{image, fork_commit, torch}, serve:{port, cudagraph_mode:\"PIECEWISE\", vllm_ple_mmap:1, boot_seconds, tp:1}, completion:{prompt,text,tokens,finish_reason}, logits:{finite, values_checked}, mmap:{engaged, log_mentions}, shutdown:{clean, exit_code}}.\nstatus = pass iff ready & finite & engaged & clean.\nWrite OUT; also print.\n\nReceipt written inside python (python receives OUT via env). Exit code 0/1 → bash exits accordingly. Cleanup trap: on bash error before python completes, ensure container removed + fail receipt written. Simplify: trap 'on_err $LINENO' ERR → podman rm -f, write fail receipt with \"aborted at line N\" via inline python, exit 1. But careful: python heredoc exit 1 → ERR trap fires → overwrites receipt with fail — acceptable (same fail). But don't double-write: if python wrote a fail receipt already, trap rewrite is harmless (same status). But pass case: python exits 0, no trap.\n\nHmm — but if python exits 1 after writing fail receipt, bash `set -e` triggers ERR trap → rewrite receipt \"aborted\" losing detail. Let python exit 0 even on status fail after writing receipt? No — script should exit non-zero on step failure (overnight ladder grades). Compromise: trap checks if OUT already exists with valid JSON → don't overwrite. Implement write_receipt_once semantics in the trap's python: only write if file missing or unparseable. Good.\n\nEnv F.9 check for the run-proxy -e list: VLLM_PLE_MMAP is bool(int(os.getenv)) ✓ safe to export (fn-env does it too). HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT is not an engine probe. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF is fine. PYTHONHASHSEED is fine.\n\nNow tests/test_proxy_tooling.py — write as planned. Also mirror the run-tp2 header comment convention and keep script comment quality high.\n\nOne more check: does `results/receipts` dir exist and is it committed? results/receipts exists with build.json etc. ✓ git-tracked.\n\nAlso README/docs mention? out of boundary (only scripts/ + tests/). Fine.\n\nLet's write the files. Start with make-proxy.sh.\n\nAnother detail — inside the make-proxy container's python, we need `import shutil` for tokenizer copy, and numpy for randn? Use torch for randn (deterministic seed), then convert. bf16 bytes: t.to(torch.bfloat16).view(torch.int16).numpy().tobytes() — view requires contiguous ✓ .numpy on int16 ✓.\n\nfp8 zeros: torch.zeros(shape, dtype=torch.float8_e4m3fn) → view torch.uint8 → bytes. For nonzero small values: (torch.rand×2a−a).to(fp8). Keep mostly zeros + small randn embed for safety.\n\ne4m3 scale_inv: per-block [128,128] → shape (ceil(rows/128), ceil(cols/128)) fp32 ones.\n\nSafetensors serializer padding: format has no per-tensor alignment requirement? Spec: data_offsets absolute; alignment recommended 8-byte for zero-copy — my offsets: accumulate; pad each blob to 8 for safety (pad after each blob, not included in offsets). Implement pad after each tensor blob.\n\nEdge: empty header dict when no tensors — not applicable.\n\n\"__metadata__\" optional — add {\"format\":\"pt\"}. vLLM doesn't care; discover parses name→spec entries; must skip \"__metadata__\" — does discover's code handle it? parse_safetensors_header probably ignores metadata (header entries without data_offsets). Their parser reads the tensor entries — metadata entries lack dtype/shape; a strict parser could choke. Actual checkpoints don't carry format metadata? HF write adds {\"format\":\"pt\"}. Upstream parse_safetensors_header (ple_mmap.py:125-170) — unknown handling. Safest: omit __metadata__. ✓ Omit.\n\nFile naming: single main file `model-00001-of-00001.safetensors` + per-shard ple files `model-ple-{layer}-{shard:05d}.safetensors` (mirror fixture naming from dossier).\n\nNow — subtle point about discover_shards globbing: globs `*.safetensors` in model_path (flat). All files flat under OUT ✓.\n\nTime to write. Also don't forget acceptance: run-proxy.sh must contain literal `results/receipts/proxy.json` — my OUT= line contains it ✓.\n\nPython heredoc inside bash: use quoted 'PY' to avoid expansion. Pass variables via -e env.\n\nAlso decide FN_SERVED name for the proxy: \"flashnext-proxy\".\n\nOK let's write make-proxy.sh in full now."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"I now have the full picture. Key facts:\n\n- Fork is at `/opt/vllm` in the container; its mmap module lives at `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/common/ple_mmap.py` (patch 0009), with fixture naming `model-ple-{layer}-{shard:05d}.safetensors` and shard tensor names `layers.{i}.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_{j}.weight`.\n- The fork's `check_cudagraph_safety` guard **refuses plain-eager and full-graph capture** under `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1`; ruling P10 sanctions piecewise mode. So `run-proxy.sh` must run `-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE`, not eager.\n- Receipt shape: `{\"step\",\"status\",\"ts\",\"data\"}`; run-smoke.sh is the style reference; fn-env.sh gives env doctrine (no is-set-probe exports).\n- Workload config facts from evidence: `Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration`, `model_type qwen4_exp`, `layer_types` 3×linear+1×full, `hidden_size 2560`, `head_dim 256`.\n\nNow writing `scripts/make-proxy.sh`:\n\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7db45de74a904edfb3d5852f","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# scripts/make-proxy.sh — the proxy checkpoint builder (prep for spec claim 4.1).\n#\n# Builds a tiny synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy with the\n# vocabulary contract of spec.md (\"proxy checkpoint\"): the same architecture\n# identifier and expert format as the workload — a handful of layers, 8 routed\n# experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size [128, 128], a small engram/PLE\n# lookup table under exactly the shard tensor naming the mmap path's\n# discover_shards expects, plus a tokenizer so the server never reaches for a\n# hub (spec F.6). The result proves the admitted kernel path and the ported\n# table path on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded.\n#\n# Fork-scaffold reuse doctrine (task goal: reuse, do not invent):\n#   - The base config is the staged workload config shrunk, whenever\n#     /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8/config.json is present, so every\n#     field the fork's config class reads keeps its exact shape.\n#   - The PLE table naming is validated against the fork's own mmap module\n#     (vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common.ple_mmap: _SHARD_RE, discover_shards),\n#     and the fork's tests/models/qwen4_exp scaffolding is probed for a\n#     shard-writer before the built-in writer is used.\n#   - Weight tensor names are derived from the fork's own model class by\n#     meta-device instantiation whenever that is possible; the curated\n#     qwen3-next-family naming below is the fallback only.\n#\n# The checkpoint directory is disposable by construction: it is rebuilt from\n# scratch on every run. Host-side default location keeps it OUTSIDE the repo\n# (compare container/build.sh's cache doctrine); override with FN_PROXY_DIR.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nPROXY_DIR=\"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-${FN_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext}/proxy-checkpoint}\"\nMODEL_DIR=\"${FN_MODEL_DIR:-/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8}\"\n\nlog() { echo \"make-proxy: $*\" >&2; }\n\nmkdir -p \"$PROXY_DIR\"\nfind \"$PROXY_DIR\" -mindepth 1 -delete\nlog \"building the proxy checkpoint at $PROXY_DIR\"\n\nMOUNTS=(-v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nif [ -f \"$MODEL_DIR/config.json\" ]; then\n    log \"staged workload config present at $MODEL_DIR — shrinking it as the base\"\n    MOUNTS+=(-v \"$MODEL_DIR:/models:ro\")\nelse\n    log \"no staged workload config at $MODEL_DIR — falling back to the evidence template\"\nfi\n\npodman run --rm \\\n    -e FN_PROXY_LAYERS=\"${FN_PROXY_LAYERS:-8}\" \\\n    -e FN_PROXY_EXPERTS=\"${FN_PROXY_EXPERTS:-8}\" \\\n    \"${MOUNTS[@]}\" \\\n    \"$IMAGE\" python3 - <<'PY'\n\"\"\"Build /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy: config + tokenizer + weights + PLE shards.\n\nEvery stage is loud: a stage that cannot complete raises with a typed message,\nand a manifest (proxy-manifest.json) records what was reused, what was\nfallback, and every residual risk, so run-proxy.sh and the morning ledger can\ngrade provenance rather than narrate it.\n\"\"\"\nimport importlib\nimport inspect\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport traceback\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport torch\n\nOUT = Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nMODELS = Path(\"/models\")  # read-only mount of the staged workload, if present\nLAYERS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_LAYERS\", \"8\"))\nEXPERTS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_EXPERTS\", \"8\"))\nTOPK = 2\nMOE_INTER = 256  # multiple of the 128 block size\nBLOCK = 128\nSEED = 42\n\nMANIFEST = {\n    \"built_by\": \"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\n    \"ts\": time.strftime(\"%FT%T\"),\n    \"geometry\": {\"layers\": LAYERS, \"experts\": EXPERTS,\n                 \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]},\n    \"base_config_source\": None,\n    \"config_edits\": {},\n    \"tokenizer_source\": None,\n    \"scaffold\": {\"fork_modules_probed\": [], \"reused\": [], \"validation\": []},\n    \"weight_source\": None,\n    \"files\": [],\n    \"warnings\": [],\n}\n\n\ndef note(msg):\n    print(f\"make-proxy: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    MANIFEST[\"warnings\"].append(msg)\n\n\ndef die(msg):\n    raise SystemExit(f\"make-proxy: FATAL: {msg}\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 1 — config: shrink the workload config, else the evidence template\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef load_base_config():\n    p = MODELS / \"config.json\"\n    if p.is_file():\n        return json.loads(p.read_text()), \"workload:%s\" % p\n    # Typed fallback: field values observed in the workload config per\n    # specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 3.3, completed\n    # with the PLE geometry names per specs/flashnext/evidence/\n    # moe-dispatch.md section 5. Only used when staging has not landed.\n    tmpl = {\n        \"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],\n        \"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\",\n        \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\",\n        \"hidden_size\": 2560,\n        \"head_dim\": 256,\n        \"num_attention_heads\": 16,\n        \"num_key_value_heads\": 2,\n        \"num_hidden_layers\": LAYERS,\n        \"full_attention_interval\": 4,\n        \"layer_types\": [],\n        \"vocab_size\": 4096,\n        \"max_position_embeddings\": 4096,\n        \"rms_norm_eps\": 1e-6,\n        \"tie_word_embeddings\": False,\n        \"use_qk_norm\": True,\n        \"decoder_sparse_step\": 1,\n        \"num_experts\": EXPERTS,\n        \"num_experts_per_tok\": TOPK,\n        \"moe_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"indexer_budget\": 2048,\n        \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 512,\n        \"heads_per_ngram\": 1,\n        \"ple_embed_dim\": 256,\n        \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 128,\n        \"split_ngram_parts\": 2,\n    }\n    return tmpl, \"template:evidence-dotfiles-observed-3.3+moe-dispatch-5\"\n\n\ndef shrink(cfg):\n    edits = {}\n\n    def set_(key, val):\n        edits[key] = [cfg.get(key), val]\n        cfg[key] = val\n\n    archs = cfg.get(\"architectures\") or []\n    if not any(\"Qwen4Exp\" in a for a in archs):\n        die(f\"base config architectures {archs} carry no Qwen4Exp identifier; \"\n            \"refusing to relabel a foreign model as the proxy\")\n    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    interval = int(cfg.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4))\n    pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\n    set_(\"num_experts\", EXPERTS)\n    set_(\"num_experts_per_tok\",\n         min(int(cfg.get(\"num_experts_per_tok\", TOPK)), EXPERTS))\n    # Every layer routed-MoE, so the admitted block-FP8 kernel runs on every\n    # decode step of the proxy serve.\n    set_(\"decoder_sparse_step\", 1)\n    set_(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"intermediate_size\", 2 * BLOCK)\n    set_(\"max_position_embeddings\",\n         min(int(cfg.get(\"max_position_embeddings\", 4096)), 4096))\n    if not (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file():\n        set_(\"vocab_size\", 4096)  # template tokenizer is paired with 4096\n    # Block-FP8 for the routed experts is the workload's expert format; the\n    # proxy quantizes every Linear so BOTH admitted paths run (the 0008 MoE\n    # admission and the 0012 linear twin). embed/lm_head stay bf16 by the\n    # loader's own rule.\n    set_(\"quantization_config\",\n         {\"quant_method\": \"fp8\", \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]})\n    # Small PLE table: shrink every large ngram-size field; keep heads/dims.\n    for key in list(cfg):\n        if \"ngram\" in key.lower() and re.search(r\"(size|base|vocab)\",\n                                                key.lower()):\n            val = cfg[key]\n            if isinstance(val, int) and val > 512:\n                set_(key, 512)\n    split_key = next((k for k in cfg\n                      if \"split\" in k.lower() and \"ngram\" in k.lower()), None)\n    if split_key is not None:\n        set_(split_key, 2)\n    return edits\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 2 — tokenizer: copy from the staged workload, else synthesize a pair\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef stage_tokenizer(cfg):\n    copied = []\n    for name in (\"tokenizer.json\", \"tokenizer_config.json\",\n                 \"special_tokens_map.json\", \"vocab.json\", \"merges.txt\",\n                 \"generation_config.json\", \"chat_template.jinja\"):\n        src = MODELS / name\n        if src.is_file():\n            shutil.copy2(src, OUT / name)\n            copied.append(name)\n    if any(n.startswith(\"tokenizer\") for n in copied):\n        return \"workload:\" + \",\".join(copied)\n    # Synthetic WordLevel tokenizer paired with the template vocab_size 4096.\n    specials = [\"<pad>\", \"<bos>\", \"<eos>\", \"<unk>\"]\n    vocab = {tok: i for i, tok in enumerate(specials)}\n    i = len(specials)\n    for c in (chr(x) for x in range(33, 127)):\n        vocab[c] = i\n        i += 1\n    for word in (\"the\", \"a\", \"of\", \"and\", \"to\", \"in\", \"is\", \"on\", \"for\",\n                 \"with\", \"that\", \"this\", \"night\", \"pair\", \"proxy\", \"light\"):\n        if i >= int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"]):\n            break\n        vocab[word] = i\n        i += 1\n    added = [{\"id\": n, \"content\": tok, \"single_word\": False, \"lstrip\": False,\n              \"rstrip\": False, \"normalized\": False, \"special\": True}\n             for tok, n in zip(specials, range(len(specials)))]\n    tok_json = {\n        \"version\": \"1.0\", \"truncation\": None, \"padding\": None,\n        \"added_tokens\": added,\n        \"normalizer\": {\"type\": \"NFC\"},\n        \"pre_tokenizer\": {\"type\": \"Whitespace\"},\n        \"post_processor\": None,\n        \"decoder\": {\"type\": \"WordLevel\"},\n        \"model\": {\"type\": \"WordLevel\", \"vocab\": vocab, \"unk_token\": \"<unk>\"},\n    }\n    (OUT / \"tokenizer.json\").write_text(json.dumps(tok_json))\n    (OUT / \"tokenizer_config.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\n        \"tokenizer_class\": \"PreTrainedTokenizerFast\",\n        \"model_max_length\": 4096,\n        \"pad_token\": \"<pad>\", \"bos_token\": \"<bos>\",\n        \"eos_token\": \"<eos>\", \"unk_token\": \"<unk>\",\n    }))\n    note(\"no staged workload tokenizer: synthesized a WordLevel pair \"\n         \"(proxy output text quality is not the claim; finite logits are)\")\n    return \"synthetic-wordlevel\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 3 — the fork's own scaffolding: probe, reuse where possible\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef probe_fork_scaffolds():\n    \"\"\"Probe the fork's tests/models/qwen4_exp tree for reusable writers and\n    import its ple_mmap module as the naming authority (_SHARD_RE).\"\"\"\n    ple_mmap = None\n    try:\n        from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common import ple_mmap as _pm\n        ple_mmap = _pm\n        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n            \"vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common.ple_mmap (naming authority)\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        try:\n            from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia import ple_mmap as _pm\n            ple_mmap = _pm\n            MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n                \"vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.ple_mmap (pre-0009 location)\")\n        except Exception as e2:\n            note(f\"ple_mmap not importable ({e!r}, {e2!r}); the serve itself \"\n                 \"remains the naming authority\")\n    sys.path.insert(0, \"/opt/vllm/tests\")\n    for modname in (\"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap_amd\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple\"):\n        entry = {\"module\": modname}\n        try:\n            mod = importlib.import_module(modname)\n            writers = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                       if callable(getattr(mod, n, None)) and re.search(\n                           r\"(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|ckpt|\"\n                           r\"checkpoint|fixture)\", n, re.I)]\n            entry[\"callable_writers\"] = writers\n            for wname in writers:\n                fn = getattr(mod, wname)\n                try:\n                    sig = inspect.signature(fn)\n                except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                    continue\n                # Reuse only a writer with a single path-like argument;\n                # anything else is a pytest fixture contract we must not guess.\n                pos = [p for p in sig.parameters.values()\n                       if p.kind in (p.POSITIONAL_ONLY, p.POSITIONAL_OR_KEYWORD)\n                       and p.default is p.empty]\n                if len(sig.parameters) == 1 and len(pos) <= 1:\n                    try:\n                        fn(str(OUT))\n                        entry[\"invoked\"] = wname\n                        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n                            f\"{modname}.{wname}\")\n                        break\n                    except Exception as e3:\n                        entry[f\"{wname}_error\"] = f\"{e3.__class__.__name__}\"\n        except Exception as e:\n            entry[\"import\"] = f\"FAIL {e.__class__.__name__}: {e}\"\n        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"fork_modules_probed\"].append(entry)\n    return ple_mmap\n\n\ndef ngram_geometry(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Mirror the loader's shard mapping (specs/flashnext/evidence/\n    ple-54129.md section 3): shard_size = ceil(org / split); the checkpoint\n    carries ceil(org / shard_size) row-block tensors per PLE layer.\"\"\"\n    base = int(cfg.get(\"ngram_vocab_size_base\", 512))\n    heads = int(cfg.get(\"heads_per_ngram\", 1))\n    div = int(cfg.get(\"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\", 1) or 1)\n    split = int(cfg.get(\"split_ngram_parts\", 512))\n    total = base * heads\n    padded = math.ceil(total / div) * div if div > 1 else total\n    return {\"base\": base, \"heads\": heads, \"divisible_by\": div,\n            \"split\": split, \"padded_rows\": padded,\n            \"rows_per_shard\": math.ceil(padded / split) if split else padded,\n            \"note\": \"mirror of (org + split - 1) // split; a mismatch is \"\n                    \"caught by the discover_shards validation below\"}\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 4 — weights: fork introspection first, curated naming as fallback\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef _bf16(t):\n    return (\"BF16\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous().view(torch.int16).numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef _fp8(t):\n    return (\"F8_E4M3\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.float8_e4m3fn).contiguous().view(torch.uint8).numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef _f32(t):\n    return (\"F32\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.float32).contiguous().numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef save_safetensors(path, tensors):\n    \"\"\"Minimal safetensors serializer (8-byte LE header length, JSON header,\n    packed blobs) so fp8 tensors never depend on library-version support.\"\"\"\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        pad = (8 - len(raw) % 8) % 8\n        blobs.append(raw + b\"\\x00\" * pad)\n        offset += len(raw) + pad\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    hpad = (8 - len(hjson) % 8) % 8\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\n        f.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)\n\n\ndef scale_inv_shape(shape):\n    return [math.ceil(d / BLOCK) for d in shape]\n\n\ndef try_fork_introspection(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Instantiate the fork's model class on the meta device and return the\n    exact parameter list, or None. When this works, weight names are the\n    fork's own, not the curated fallback's.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from vllm.config import ModelConfig, VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config\n        from vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry\n        torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]\n            with torch.device(\"meta\"):\n                model = cls(vllm_config=vc)\n        params = [(n, tuple(p.shape)) for n, p in model.named_parameters()]\n        stacked = list(getattr(model, \"stacked_params_mapping\", []))\n        if not params:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"model instantiated with zero parameters\")\n        return params, stacked\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"fork model introspection unavailable \"\n             f\"({e.__class__.__name__}: {e}); using the curated fallback \"\n             \"naming with its typed residual risks\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef probe_ignore_semantics():\n    \"\"\"Empirically determine how Fp8Config consumes modules_to_not_convert\n    (regex match vs literal membership) and, if regex, install a skip-list\n    that keeps every non-expert Linear UNQUANTIZED — an unprovided quantized\n    parameter is uninitialized fp8 memory, and NaN bits there would poison\n    the finite-logits claim. Returns True when the skip-list is active.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        import vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 as fp8mod\n        src = inspect.getsource(fp8mod)\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"Fp8Config source probe unavailable: {e!r}\")\n        return False\n    if re.search(r\"re\\.(match|search|fullmatch)\\s*\\([^)]*ignored\", src):\n        return True  # regex semantics: the negative-lookahead pattern works\n    note(\"Fp8Config appears to consume modules_to_not_convert by literal \"\n         \"membership; skipping the ignore-list (quantize-all mode)\")\n    return False\n\n\ndef curated_weights(cfg):\n    \"\"\"qwen3-next-family HF naming; the fallback path. Residual risks, typed:\n    (a) linear-attention module tensors are left to the fork's own init —\n    safe only when the ignore-list keeps them unquantized; (b) PLE shards are\n    written for EVERY layer on the family's per-layer PLE signature.\"\"\"\n    H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E, M = EXPERTS, int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n    S = int(cfg.get(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", 0) or 0)\n    gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n    tensors = {}\n    emb = torch.randn(V, H, generator=gen) * 0.02\n    tensors[\"model.embed_tokens.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    tensors[\"model.norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):\n        if quantized:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n            tensors[name + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n        else:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n\n    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n    for i, lt in enumerate(cfg[\"layer_types\"]):\n        p = f\"model.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            linear(f\"{a}.q_proj\", (NH * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.k_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.v_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.o_proj\", (H, NH * HD), quantize_linears)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n        # linear_attention layers: no checkpoint tensors are written — the\n        # fork's own init covers them when they stay unquantized (see above).\n        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        tensors[f\"{m}.gate.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(E, H))\n        for e in range(E):\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (M, H)), (\"up_proj\", (M, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, M))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.experts.{e}.{proj}\", shape, True)\n        if S > 0:\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (S, H)), (\"up_proj\", (S, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, S))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.shared_experts.{proj}\", shape, quantize_linears)\n    return tensors\n\n\ndef write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):\n    \"\"\"One row-block tensor per shard under the discover_shards naming, plus\n    the per-layer global weight_scale the load_weights interception keeps.\n    Values are fp8 zeros at scale 1.0: the PLE contribution is exactly zero,\n    which is finite by construction.\"\"\"\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    rows, split = geom[\"rows_per_shard\"], geom[\"split\"]\n    files = 0\n    scale = _f32(torch.ones(1))\n    main = {}\n    for layer in range(int(cfg[\"num_hidden_layers\"])):\n        for s in range(split):\n            name = (f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n                    f\"ngram_embedding.shard_{s:05d}.weight\")\n            save_safetensors(\n                OUT / f\"model-ple-{layer}-{s:05d}.safetensors\",\n                {name: _fp8(torch.zeros(rows, HD))})\n            files += 1\n        main[f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n             f\"ngram_embedding.weight_scale\"] = scale\n    return files, main\n\n\ndef validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom):\n    if ple_mmap is None:\n        note(\"skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)\")\n        return\n    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))\n    per_layer = {int(k): v for k, v in getattr(found, \"items\", lambda: found)()} \\\n        if isinstance(found, dict) else found\n    entry = {\"per_layer_shards\": {str(k): len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items()}}\n    expected = geom[\"split\"]\n    bad = {k: len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items() if len(v) != expected}\n    entry[\"expected_shards_per_layer\"] = expected\n    MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"validation\"].append(entry)\n    if bad:\n        die(f\"discover_shards found {bad} shards where the geometry expects \"\n            f\"{expected} per layer — the mmap path would refuse this table at \"\n            \"attach time; refusing to hand run-proxy.sh a doomed checkpoint\")\n    # Row-count cross-check against the mirror formula, via the first shard.\n    first = next(iter(per_layer.values()))[0]\n    rows = first[2] if isinstance(first, tuple) else None\n    if rows is not None and rows != geom[\"rows_per_shard\"]:\n        note(f\"discover_shards reports {rows} rows/shard vs the mirror's \"\n             f\"{geom['rows_per_shard']} — the serve is the tiebreaker\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# main\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef main():\n    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    cfg, source = load_base_config()\n    MANIFEST[\"base_config_source\"] = source\n    MANIFEST[\"config_edits\"] = shrink(cfg)\n\n    MANIFEST[\"tokenizer_source\"] = stage_tokenizer(cfg)\n\n    # Write config.json first: both fork introspection and the fork's config\n    # class read the checkpoint directory as the model path.\n    (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n\n    ple_mmap = probe_fork_scaffolds()\n    geom = ngram_geometry(cfg)\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ngram\"] = geom\n\n    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    if probe_ignore_semantics():\n        # Negative lookahead: skip every Linear except the routed experts.\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"]\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(\"modules_to_not_convert installed with regex semantics observed \"\n             \"in the fork's Fp8Config — non-expert linears stay unquantized\")\n\n    if introspected:\n        # Exact names from the fork's own class. Fused params are split back\n        # into their HF-side names; every other parameter is written under its\n        # own name, fp8-quantized iff it is an experts weight.\n        params, stacked = introspected\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n        V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n        tensors = {}\n        fused = {}  # vllm suffix -> (hf suffix, shard ids)\n        for vllm_sfx, hf_sfx, shard_id in stacked:\n            fused.setdefault(vllm_sfx, []).append((hf_sfx, shard_id))\n        for name, shape in params:\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and shape and len(shape) == 2:\n                base = name[:-len(\".weight\")]\n                hit = None\n                for vllm_sfx, entries in fused.items():\n                    if base.endswith(vllm_sfx):\n                        hit = (base[:-len(vllm_sfx)], entries)\n                        break\n                if hit:\n                    stem, entries = hit\n                    total_rows = shape[0]\n                    for hf_sfx, shard_id in entries:\n                        rows = total_rows // len(entries)\n                        sub = (rows, shape[1])\n                        hname = f\"{stem}{hf_sfx}\"\n                        if \".mlp.experts.\" in hname:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(sub))\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(sub)))\n                        else:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(sub))\n                    continue\n                if \".mlp.experts.\" in name and \"scale\" not in name:\n                    tensors[name] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n                    tensors[name[:-len(\".weight\")] + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = \\\n                        _f32(torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n                    continue\n            if \"embed_tokens\" in name and len(shape) == 2:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.randn(*shape, generator=gen) * 0.02)\n                continue\n            if \"norm\" in name and len(shape) == 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.ones(shape[0]))\n                continue\n            if len(shape) >= 1 and \"scale\" not in name:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n    else:\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"curated-fallback\"\n        tensors = curated_weights(cfg)\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n\n    shard_files, scale_tensors = write_ple_shards(cfg, geom)\n    if scale_tensors:\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-ple-scales.safetensors\", scale_tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-ple-scales.safetensors\")\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ple_shard_files\"] = shard_files\n    validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom)\n\n    manifest_path = OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\"\n    manifest_path.write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    total_bytes = sum(f.stat().st_size for f in OUT.iterdir() if f.is_file())\n    n_files = len(list(OUT.glob(\"*.safetensors\")))\n    print(f\"make-proxy: checkpoint complete: {n_files} safetensors files, \"\n          f\"{total_bytes / 2**20:.1f} MiB, weight_source=\"\n          f\"{MANIFEST['weight_source']}, base={source}\")\n    if MANIFEST[\"warnings\"]:\n        print(f\"make-proxy: {len(MANIFEST['warnings'])} warning(s) recorded \"\n              \"in proxy-manifest.json\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ntry:\n    main()\nexcept SystemExit as e:\n    try:\n        (OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    print(f\"{e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(1)\nexcept Exception:\n    traceback.print_exc()\n    try:\n        MANIFEST[\"warnings\"].append(\"unhandled exception; see container log\")\n        (OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    sys.exit(1)\nPY\n\nlog \"checkpoint ready at $PROXY_DIR: $(find \"$PROXY_DIR\" -name '*.safetensors' | wc -l) safetensors files\"\nlog \"next: scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Pair service uses `--network host`. Do the same in the proxy runner too (simpler, no port mapping issues; only bind the port via the serve CLI). Note: `--network host` exposes the port directly on the host.\n\nAlso, mirror the container flags: --ipc host, devices, seccomp, group-add keep-groups, ulimit memlock.\n\nOK let's write the script. run-smoke.sh mounts `-v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\"`, so receipts are written inside the container to /results/receipts/... . run-proxy.sh does the same: mount results at /results, write receipts inside the python heredoc at /results/receipts/proxy.json, and also echo on the host side. Receipt writing is done in host-side python (simpler: host writes receipt after data collection). Collect data in bash variables + podman outputs, then at the end write the receipt via a host python heredoc. Cleaner approach: host python orchestrates the entire API interaction + receipt writing, calling podman via subprocess? run-tp2.sh uses host-side python heredocs that use urllib against FN_API — the host reaches the container port via --network host. ✓ Follow that: bash orchestrates the container lifecycle, and a host python heredoc does polling + completion + assertions + receipt writing.\n\nNow — engagement grep: on the host side do `podman logs $CTR`. ✓\n\nFork commit: `podman run --rm $IMAGE cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json` (cheap) → parse fork_commit. ✓\n\nClean shutdown: vllm serve launched via `podman exec -d` inside a sleep-infinity container? Or a detached container running serve directly? With serve directly: `podman run -d --name CTR ... IMAGE bash -lc \"exec vllm serve ...\"` → container's main process = serve; podman stop → SIGTERM to serve → clean exit → exit code obtainable via inspect ✓. Simpler than sleep-infinity + exec.\n\nNow let's write make-proxy.sh. A complete python generator. Let me draft it carefully.\n\n```python\nimport importlib\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport traceback\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport torch\n\nOUT = Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nMODELS = Path(\"/models\")           # staged workload, ro-mounted if present\nLAYERS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_LAYERS\", \"8\"))\nEXPERTS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_EXPERTS\", \"8\"))\nTOPK = 2\nMOE_INTER = 256                    # multiple of the 128 block size\nBLOCK = 128\nSEED = 42\nwarnings = []\nscaffold = {\"fork_scaffold_candidates\": [], \"reused\": None,\n            \"validation\": []}\n\ndef note(msg):\n    print(f\"make-proxy: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    warnings.append(msg)\n```\n\nStage 1 config:\n\n```python\ndef load_base_config():\n    p = MODELS / \"config.json\"\n    if p.is_file():\n        return json.loads(p.read_text()), f\"workload:{p}\"\n    tmpl = {\n        \"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],\n        \"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\",\n        \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\",\n        \"hidden_size\": 2560,\n        \"head_dim\": 256,\n        \"num_attention_heads\": 16,\n        \"num_key_value_heads\": 2,\n        \"num_hidden_layers\": LAYERS,\n        \"full_attention_interval\": 4,\n        \"layer_types\": [],\n        \"vocab_size\": 4096,\n        \"max_position_embeddings\": 4096,\n        \"rms_norm_eps\": 1e-6,\n        \"tie_word_embeddings\": False,\n        \"use_qk_norm\": True,\n        \"decoder_sparse_step\": 1,\n        \"num_experts\": EXPERTS,\n        \"num_experts_per_tok\": TOPK,\n        \"moe_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"indexer_budget\": 2048,\n        \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 512,\n        \"heads_per_ngram\": 1,\n        \"ple_embed_dim\": 256,\n        \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 128,\n        \"split_ngram_parts\": 2,\n    }\n    return tmpl, \"template:evidence-dotfiles-observed-3.3\"\n```\n\nShrink handling:\n\n```python\ndef shrink(cfg):\n    edits = {}\n    def set_(k, v):\n        edits[k] = [cfg.get(k), v]\n        cfg[k] = v\n    archs = cfg.get(\"architectures\") or []\n    if not any(\"Qwen4Exp\" in a for a in archs):\n        raise SystemExit(f\"make-proxy: base config architectures {archs} carry no Qwen4Exp identifier; refusing to relabel a foreign model as the proxy\")\n    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    interval = cfg.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4)\n    pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\n    set_(\"num_experts\", EXPERTS)\n    set_(\"num_experts_per_tok\", min(int(cfg.get(\"num_experts_per_tok\", TOPK)), EXPERTS))\n    if \"decoder_sparse_step\" in cfg or True:\n        set_(\"decoder_sparse_step\", 1)   # every layer routed-MoE: the admitted kernel runs on every decode\n    set_(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"intermediate_size\", 2 * BLOCK)\n    set_(\"max_position_embeddings\", min(int(cfg.get(\"max_position_embeddings\", 4096)), 4096))\n    # Keep the workload's vocab_size + tokenizer as a pair\n    if not (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file():\n        set_(\"vocab_size\", 4096)\n    # quantization: block-FP8 everywhere a Linear lives; embed/lm_head stay bf16 by loader rule\n    set_(\"quantization_config\", {\"quant_method\": \"fp8\", \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]})\n    # small PLE table\n    for k in list(cfg):\n        if \"ngram\" in k.lower() and re.search(r\"(size|base|vocab)\", k.lower()):\n            v = cfg[k]\n            if isinstance(v, int) and v > 512:\n                set_(k, 512)\n    split_key = next((k for k in cfg if \"split\" in k.lower() and \"ngram\" in k.lower()), None)\n    if split_key:\n        set_(split_key, 2)\n    return edits\n```\n\nHmm wait, \"set_('decoder_sparse_step', 1) or True\" — sloppy; just write set_ unconditionally.\n\nNote: if the workload config has its own quantization_config with modules_to_not_convert — drop it (replaced with the new dict) → quantize all Linears. Then the unknown name problem: linear-attn's Linears are quantized but not provided by fallback writer → uninitialized fp8 → NaN risk. In the introspection path, resolve the name. In fallback... need mitigation.\n\nMitigation idea for fallback: empirically probe the ignore semantics and if regex is accepted use a modules_to_not_convert that covers everything except the expert prefix:\n\n```python\ndef probe_ignore_semantics():\n    try:\n        from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 import Fp8Config\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"Fp8Config probe unavailable: {e}\")\n        return None\n    expert = \"model.layers.3.mlp.experts.4.gate_proj\"\n    other = \"model.layers.3.linear_attn.in_proj_qkvz\"\n    for patterns in (\n        [r\"(?!(.*mlp\\.experts)).*\"],          # negative lookahead regex\n        [r\"^(?!.*mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"],\n    ):\n        try:\n            qc = Fp8Config(weight_block_size=[BLOCK, BLOCK], ignored_layers=list(patterns))\n            # Probe how the skip predicate reads the layer:\n            from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 import Fp8Config as _C\n            # Build a dummy module? get_quant_method needs a layer instance...\n        except Exception as e:\n            ...\n```\nget_quant_method(layer, prefix) needs a layer object with isinstance checks (FusedMoE/LinearBase/EmbeddingBase...). Can we make a fake? `types.SimpleNamespace`? First isinstance(layer, FusedMoEBase)... complicated. Alternative probe target: find the skip helper function itself:\n\n```python\nimport vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 as fp8mod\nimport inspect\nsrc = inspect.getsource(fp8mod)\n```\nAnd grep the source for how ignored_layers is consumed (search for \"ignored_layers\" usages). Then decide the pattern format empirically from the source text (regex or membership). Clever but fragile across versions — still better than guessing. If source shows `prefix in ignored` → literal prefix required → can't enumerate without instantiation → fall back to quantize-all + curated names + NaN risk flag. If `re.match/search(pattern, prefix)` → use lookahead regex or simpler: patterns = [r\"^model\\.layers\\.\\d+\\.(?!mlp\\.experts).*\"] hmm need to cover all top-level non-expert Linears too.\n\nA simpler regex that works under re.match against all non-expert Linears: `r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"` — any prefix not containing .mlp.experts. → skip (unquantized). Expert prefix doesn't match → quantized ✓. If semantics is re.search(pattern, prefix): the pattern is anchored with ^...$ — still works.\n\nLet's go with this empirical probe: source-inspect how ignored_layers is consumed, then validate that our patterns give the desired predicate with re directly (mirror the observed semantics locally), and further if instantiable do a live get_quant_method probe.\n\nAnd last-resort fallback if none of that works: quantize-all + curated writer + honestly manifest the risk + run-proxy's finite-logits assertion grades it anyway.\n\nStage 2 fork scaffolding probe for the PLE writer:\n\n```python\ndef probe_fork_ple_scaffold():\n    \"\"\"Prefer the fork's own tests/models scaffolding over inventing writers\n    (task goal). Tests of the mmap path construct fixture checkpoints with the\n    exact shard naming discover_shards accepts, so any shard writer exposed\n    there is reused as-is.\"\"\"\n    sys.path.insert(0, \"/opt/vllm/tests\")\n    cand = []\n    for modname in (\"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap_amd\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple\"):\n        try:\n            mod = importlib.import_module(modname)\n        except Exception as e:\n            cand.append({\"module\": modname, \"import\": f\"FAIL {e.__class__.__name__}: {e}\"})\n            continue\n        writers = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                   if callable(getattr(mod, n))\n                   and re.search(r\"(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|ckpt|checkpoint|fixture)|fixture.*shard\", n, re.I)]\n        cand.append({\"module\": modname, \"writers\": writers})\n        scaffold[\"fork_scaffold_candidates\"].append(cand[-1])\n    ...\n```\nActually calling an unknown fixture is too risky (pytest fixture objects, kwargs). Limit actual reuse to: importing the module and reading its fixture naming convention? Hmm. Honestly: reuse = (a) validate against the fork's own ple_mmap (_SHARD_RE, discover_shards, dtype map), (b) match the fixture file naming `model-ple-{layer}-{shard:05d}.safetensors`, (c) if a fork test exposes a module-level writer that takes a directory argument, use it. Implement (c) opportunistically: only call if `inspect.signature` has exactly one positional param with default or named path/dir/out/tmp; wrap in try; validate the output via discover_shards; on validation failure delete and use own writer. OK.\n\nStage 3 geometry computation:\n\n```python\ndef ngram_geometry(cfg):\n    base = int(cfg.get(\"ngram_vocab_size_base\", 512))\n    heads = int(cfg.get(\"heads_per_ngram\", 1))\n    div = int(cfg.get(\"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\", 1) or 1)\n    split = int(cfg.get(\"split_ngram_parts\", 512))\n    total = base * heads\n    padded = math.ceil(total / div) * div if div > 1 else total\n    shard_rows = math.ceil(padded / split)\n    return {\"base\": base, \"heads\": heads, \"divisible_by\": div,\n            \"split\": split, \"padded_rows\": padded, \"rows_per_shard\": shard_rows}\n```\nNote in manifest: mirror of the loader's mapping `(org + split - 1)//split`; residual mismatch fails loudly via the discover check.\n\nRow byte width: head_dim? PLE embedding dim: the nvidia side builds MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim) → row = head_dim elements fp8. Use cfg.get(\"head_dim\", cfg.get(\"ple_embed_dim\", 256))... but heads_per_ngram>1 might widen embedding_dim = heads*ple_embed_dim... the VocabParallelEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim) says head_dim. Use head_dim. Validate at runtime if fork importable: if ple_mmap._validate_layer_shards exists, introspect its expected row_bytes? validate_shards_for(model_config, layer_name, head_dim)... the third arg head_dim is passed in → so row_bytes == head_dim. ✓ Confirmed by dossier signature.\n\nStage 4 weight writing. Write a small safetensors serializer + tensor factories. Then a curated writer:\n\n```python\ndef curated_weights(cfg, geom):\n    H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E = EXPERTS; M = MOE_INTER\n    layer_types = cfg[\"layer_types\"]\n    tensors = {}\n    # bf16 factories...\n    emb = randn_bf16((V, H), scale=0.02)\n    tensors[\"model.embed_tokens.weight\"] = emb\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = emb  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    for i, lt in enumerate(layer_types):\n        p = f\"model.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(H)\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(H)\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((NH*HD, H))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((NKV*HD, H))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.v_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((NKV*HD, H))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.o_proj.weight\"] = fp8_zeros((H, NH*HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(HD)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(HD)\n            + scale_inv for each fp8\n        moe block: gate bf16 zeros (E,H); experts fp8 zeros + scales; shared experts fp8 zeros + scales if the config has shared_expert_intermediate_size\n    tensors[\"model.norm.weight\"] = ones_bf16(H)\n```\nfp8 zeros → scale_inv ones. All zeros → finite forward (analyzed earlier). Attention zeros → uniform softmax over seq → OK.\n\nWait, one hazard: if layer_types has linear_attention and we skip its tensors entirely — those Linears are quantized (quantize-all config) → uninitialized fp8 NaN risk. Covered by the ignore-regex probe (then unquantized → init by vLLM's own init? unquantized Linears init via the model's init_weights → finite ✓). So if the ignore probe succeeds, linear-attn stays bf16-init → safe. Attention/experts are quantized and provided → safe. embed/lm_head unquantized by loader rule ✓. So the ignore-regex success → fully safe. Ignore probe failure + quantize-all + unknown names → risk persists (flag it).\n\nHmm — furthermore, with ignore regex active, what about the curated full-attn tensors I write in fp8? If the prefix matches the ignore regex → vLLM expects bf16 unquantized weights but I'm providing fp8 + scale_inv → loader mismatch (dtype/shape error, unknown scale_inv name!). Consistency required: if ignore is active → write full-attn in bf16 and don't emit scale_inv for them; experts are always block-fp8. So parameterize the writer by ignore_active: linear is fp8+scale only when quantized. Experts are quantized in either mode ✓ (regex excludes only non-experts).\n\nStage 5 fork-introspection writer (upgrade path): after config.json exists, attempt model construction; enumerate parameters; derive names. Given the complexity, implement as \"best effort\":\n\n```python\ndef fork_introspect_weights():\n    try:\n        from vllm.config import ModelConfig, VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config\n        from vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry\n        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))   # may need tokenizer ✓ present\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]\n            with torch.device(\"meta\"):\n                model = cls(vllm_config=vc)\n        params = [(n, tuple(p.shape), str(p.dtype)) for n, p in model.named_parameters()]\n        stacked = getattr(model, \"stacked_params_mapping\", [])\n        return params, stacked\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"fork model introspection unavailable: ...\")\n        return None\n```\nModelConfig(model=str(OUT)) signature: ModelConfig(model=..., tokenizer=...?) default tokenizer=model path ✓. The constructor may require more (revision defaults OK). Might error on platform/memory? ModelConfig mostly parses config. Try it; broad except.\n\nIf params obtained → write the tensor list precisely: for each param name:\n- Mapping via stacked: vllm fused name → per-shard HF names (need mapping of shard_id→(hf suffix, slice)). stacked_params_mapping entries: (vllm_suffix, hf_suffix, shard_id). Derivation: vllm name = base + vllm_suffix; HF name = base + hf_suffix (+ .weight). Per-shard shape: slice along dim0 — need slice boundaries... complex for gate_up (equal halves), qkv (per head count). Feasible: compute from config NH/NKV/HD/M. But this introspection upgrade is a bonus path; if shape slicing is wrong → wrong bytes but right names → numerically fine (zeros anyway!). Even with wrong slice size, tensor total size matches the parameter so loader weight_loader errors out? vllm's weight_loader validates shard shape. Zeros everywhere so... slicing must be correct shape-wise. Doable but more code (~60 lines).\n\nTime/complexity budget — introspection upgrade implemented pragmatically:\n- Names: use introspected params;\n- Fused qkv/gate_up: use stacked mapping and config dims to emit HF-split names;\n- Everything else: emit under parameter name (vllm name ≈ usually HF name for non-fused);\n- dtype/quant: name contains \".mlp.experts.\" and is a weight (not scale) → fp8 block + scale_inv; other weights bf16; norms are ones; embeds randn-small; gate is zero;\n- Skip params that look like buffers (rotary inv_freq usually is a buffer so not in named_parameters).\nIf introspection is active, ignore-regex is unnecessary... names are exact → quantize-all is safe only if all quantized Linears are provided. Introspection provides all Linear param names ✓ So with introspection: quantize-all config OK; write fp8+scale for each quantized linear: which are quantized? All Linears except embed/lm_head/router. Parameter name tells us the module kind only heuristically... use ignore probe anyway: quantize-only-experts (ignore regex) + write bf16 for all non-expert params + fp8 for experts → consistent and safe under either semantics... but regex semantics must be verified ✓ (probe). If regex not verified → fall back to quantize-all + fp8 all Linear params + provide all → also consistent! Because introspection lists everything. So:\n\n- Introspection + verified regex → experts fp8, others bf16 (ignore list = the regex).\n- Introspection + regex unverified → quantize-all (no ignore), all Linear/Embedding method params fp8? Embedding is unquantized by loader rule; provide fp8 to params that are quantized Linear (fp8 e4m3 + scale_inv), provide bf16 to others. Which params are quantized Linears? Without the ignore predicate... assume all weight tensors under Linear-ish modules: heuristic on name excluding (embed_tokens, lm_head, norm, gate (router? name mlp.gate.weight — router is Linear! Fp8Config.get_quant_method is FusedMoE router... FusedMoE router: vLLM treats the router weight specially as unquantized (Fp8MoEMethod handles experts; router's ReplicatedLinear gets Fp8LinearMethod?? In FusedMoE the gate/router is created with `self.gate = ReplicatedLinear(..., bias=False)` without quant_method? Hmm FusedMoE creates `self.gate` unquantized (params_dtype) — yes, standard vLLM: router stays in compute dtype). Provide router as bf16 ✓.\n\nEnough already. This adaptive design covers most branches. One more simplification: always quantize all linears except when regex verified (drop ignore); and when introspection is unavailable, curated writer + quantize-all + ignore probe.\n\nOK also handle: what if get_config rejects my synthesized config (unknown extra keys are usually tolerated). If ModelConfig() can't parse (template mode), make-proxy fails loudly — acceptable typed failure.\n\nPLE shard writer:\n\n```python\ndef write_ple(cfg, geom):\n    rows = geom[\"rows_per_shard\"]; rb = head_dim; split = geom[\"split\"]\n    count = 0\n    for layer in range(LAYERS):\n        for s in range(split):\n            name = f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_{s:05d}.weight\"\n            t = fp8_zeros((rows, rb))\n            save_safetensors(OUT / f\"model-ple-{layer}-{s:05d}.safetensors\", {name: t})\n            count += 1\n        scale = f32 ones [1] name ...weight_scale → put in main file? The loader intercepts by (stripped) name; put in main safetensors alongside others.\n```\nWait — does every layer have PLE? If only some layers have a ple module, unknown checkpoint names → ValueError from AutoWeightsLoader per layer... risk either way. Per-layer PLE structure is this model family's signature (PLE = every-layer ngram lookup per dossier §2 \"per lookup, per PLE layer, per forward\"). Emit for all layers; note residual risk in manifest. Hmm... but if wrong → loud failure at serve weight-load (~5 min), typed error, fail receipt — acceptable failure mode for a synthetic campaign.\n\nTokenizer:\n\n```python\ndef stage_tokenizer():\n    copied = []\n    for f in (\"tokenizer.json\", \"tokenizer_config.json\", \"special_tokens_map.json\",\n              \"vocab.json\", \"merges.txt\", \"generation_config.json\", \"chat_template.jinja\"):\n        src = MODELS / f\n        if src.is_file():\n            shutil.copy2(src, OUT / f); copied.append(f)\n    if any(c.startswith(\"tokenizer\") for c in copied): return copied\n    # fallback synthetic WordLevel tokenizer paired with vocab_size 4096\n    ...write tokenizer_config.json + tokenizer.json...\n```\nWordLevel tokenizer.json structure:\n```json\n{\"version\":\"1.0\",\"truncation\":null,\"padding\":null,\"added_tokens\":[{\"id\":0,\"content\":\"<pad>\",\"single_word\":false,\"lstrip\":false,\"rstrip\":false,\"normalized\":false,\"special\":true},... bos1 eos2 unk3],\"normalizer\":{\"type\":\"NFC\"},\"pre_tokenizer\":{\"type\":\"Whitespace\"},\"post_processor\":null,\"decoder\":{\"type\":\"WordLevel\"},\"model\":{\"type\":\"WordLevel\",\"vocab\":{...},\"unk_token\":\"<unk>\"}}\n```\nvocab: special 0-3, then printable ASCII singles, then a few words. Tokenize splits on whitespace; unknown word → unk. Deterministic-ish greedy output will be mostly unk... output text quality irrelevant; finiteness of logits matters. OK.\n\nValidation stage:\n```python\ndef validate_with_fork():\n    try:\n        from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common import ple_mmap\n    except ImportError:\n        try: from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia import ple_mmap\n    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))\n    per_layer counts; compare against split; rows per shard vs geom; dtype map\n    record in scaffold[\"validation\"]\n    mismatch → SystemExit with detail\n```\nReturn found to confirm engagement. discover_shards is functools.cache'd — single call fine.\n\nManifest write + main flow with try/except → traceback to stderr, exit 1 (host bash adds its own message). Manifest always written (best-effort) so run-proxy can report provenance even on failure.\n\nNow host-side bash wrapper details for make-proxy.sh:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Header comment with doctrine\nset -euo pipefail\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nPROXY_DIR=\"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-${FN_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext}/proxy-checkpoint}\"\nMODEL_DIR=\"${FN_MODEL_DIR:-/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8}\"\n\nlog() { echo \"make-proxy: $*\" >&2; }\nmkdir -p \"$PROXY_DIR\"\nfind \"$PROXY_DIR\" -mindepth 1 -delete   # rebuild clean: the proxy is disposable by construction\n\nMOUNTS=(-v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nif [ -f \"$MODEL_DIR/config.json\" ]; then\n  log \"staged workload config present at $MODEL_DIR — shrinking it as the base\"\n  MOUNTS+=(-v \"$MODEL_DIR:/models:ro\")\nfi\n\npodman run --rm \\\n  -e FN_PROXY_LAYERS=\"${FN_PROXY_LAYERS:-8}\" \\\n  -e FN_PROXY_EXPERTS=\"${FN_PROXY_EXPERTS:-8}\" \\\n  \"${MOUNTS[@]}\" \"$IMAGE\" python3 - <<'PY'\n...\nPY\n\nlog \"checkpoint ready at $PROXY_DIR ($(find \"$PROXY_DIR\" -name '*.safetensors' | wc -l) safetensors files)\"\n```\n\nNow run-proxy.sh:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Header: claim 4.1, ruling P10 note, receipt path\nset -euo pipefail\nREPO_ROOT=...\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nPROXY_DIR=\"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-${FN_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext}/proxy-checkpoint}\"\nPORT=\"${FN_PROXY_PORT:-1235}\"\nCTR=\"flashnext-proxy-serve\"\nOUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/proxy.json\"\nBOOT_TIMEOUT=\"${FN_PROXY_BOOT_TIMEOUT:-3600}\"\nAPI=\"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT\"\nmkdir -p \"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\n\nlog() ...\nfail_receipt() { python heredoc to write fail receipt with reason \"$1\"; exit 1; }\n```\nCareful: write_receipt via python reading env vars (mirror build.sh pattern). Write one python receipt writer reused for pass/fail with env: FN_STATUS, FN_DATA_JSON (json string collected). Simpler: build receipt in the final python step; also write fail receipt in traps.\n\nFlow:\n1. Check checkpoint exists: [ -f \"$PROXY_DIR/config.json\" ] || fail \"no checkpoint at $PROXY_DIR — run scripts/make-proxy.sh first\"\n2. Cleanup leftovers: podman rm -f $CTR 2>/dev/null || true\n3. fork/build-info: BUILD_INFO=\"$(podman run --rm \"$IMAGE\" cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json 2>/dev/null || echo '{}')\"\n4. Launch:\n```bash\npodman run -d --name \"$CTR\" \\\n  --network host --ipc host \\\n  --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri \\\n  --security-opt seccomp=unconfined \\\n  --group-add keep-groups --ulimit memlock=-1:-1 \\\n  -v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy:ro\" \\\n  -e VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 \\\n  -e HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 -e VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1 -e VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK=1 \\\n  -e PYTHONHASHSEED=0 \\\n  -e HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1 \\\n  -e PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=\"expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85\" \\\n  \"$IMAGE\" bash -lc \"exec vllm serve /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy \\\n    --served-model-name flashnext-proxy \\\n    --host 127.0.0.1 --port $PORT \\\n    --tensor-parallel-size 1 \\\n    --max-model-len 4096 \\\n    --gpu-memory-utilization 0.6 \\\n    --disable-log-requests \\\n    -cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE\"\n```\nNote: no --enforce-eager; comment explains: the fork's check_cudagraph_safety (per ruling P10) rejects both full-graph capture and bare eager when VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1; piecewise capture with the mmap op as split boundary is the approved first-light mode. Avoid the literal \"--enforce-eager\" inside a comment for my tests? My tests assert absence of that string — keep it absent everywhere, comment uses the \"plain-eager mode\" phrasing.\n\nNote fn-cluster-up.sh warned: don't put comments inside backslash-continuations — leave none.\n\nHmm `--host 127.0.0.1` with --network host: host-side python binds to localhost and reaches it fine.\n\n5. Poll loop in bash or python? Python heredoc for poll + request + assert + receipt (mirrors run-tp2 style):\n```python\nimport json, math, os, subprocess, sys, time, urllib.request, urllib.error\nAPI=os.environ[\"FN_API\"]; CTR=os.environ[\"FN_CTR\"]; ...\ndef podman_logs(): return subprocess.run([\"podman\",\"logs\",CTR],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout+stderr\ndeadline = time.time()+BOOT\nready=False\nwhile time.time()<deadline:\n    if container not running → break fail with log tail\n    try GET /v1/models → if served name present ready=True break\n    sleep 5\n```\nThen completion:\n```python\nbody={\"model\":\"flashnext-proxy\",\"prompt\":\"First light on the proxy: \",\"max_tokens\":16,\"temperature\":0,\"logprobs\":5}\nr=post /v1/completions\ntext=choices[0][\"text\"]; tokens=usage[\"completion_tokens\"]\nlps=[]\nfor ch in choices: \n  tl=ch[\"logprobs\"][\"token_logprobs\"] → extend with non-None\n  top=ch[\"logprobs\"][\"top_logprobs\"] → values of dicts\nfinite = len(lps)>0 and all(math.isfinite(x))\n```\nAssert finite → status.\nEngagement: logs = podman logs; mmap_mentions = count of \"ple_mmap\"; engaged = mentions>0. If VLLM_PLE_MMAP didn't engage → fail (claim requires engagement).\n6. Shutdown (bash after python? keep inside same python via subprocess): podman stop -t 120 CTR; inspect ExitCode; rm. clean = exit==0.\n7. Receipt data: {checkpoint, manifest (from PROXY_DIR/proxy-manifest.json if present), engine:{image, fork_commit, torch}, serve:{port, cudagraph_mode:\"PIECEWISE\", vllm_ple_mmap:1, boot_seconds, tp:1}, completion:{prompt,text,tokens,finish_reason}, logits:{finite, values_checked}, mmap:{engaged, log_mentions}, shutdown:{clean, exit_code}}.\nstatus = pass iff ready & finite & engaged & clean.\nWrite OUT; also print.\n\nReceipt written inside python (python receives OUT via env). Exit code 0/1 → bash exits accordingly. Cleanup trap: on bash error before python completes, ensure container removed + fail receipt written. Simplify: trap 'on_err $LINENO' ERR → podman rm -f, write fail receipt with \"aborted at line N\" via inline python, exit 1. But careful: python heredoc exit 1 → ERR trap fires → overwrites receipt with fail — acceptable (same fail). But don't double-write: if python wrote a fail receipt already, trap rewrite is harmless (same status). But pass case: python exits 0, no trap.\n\nHmm — but if python exits 1 after writing fail receipt, bash `set -e` triggers ERR trap → rewrite receipt \"aborted\" losing detail. Let python exit 0 even on status fail after writing receipt? No — script should exit non-zero on step failure (overnight ladder grades). Compromise: trap checks if OUT already exists with valid JSON → don't overwrite. Implement write_receipt_once semantics in the trap's python: only write if file missing or unparseable. Good.\n\nEnv F.9 check for the run-proxy -e list: VLLM_PLE_MMAP is bool(int(os.getenv)) ✓ safe to export (fn-env does it too). HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT is not an engine probe. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF is fine. PYTHONHASHSEED is fine.\n\nNow tests/test_proxy_tooling.py — write as planned. Also mirror the run-tp2 header comment convention and keep script comment quality high.\n\nOne more check: does `results/receipts` dir exist and is it committed? results/receipts exists with build.json etc. ✓ git-tracked.\n\nAlso README/docs mention? out of boundary (only scripts/ + tests/). Fine.\n\nLet's write the files. Start with make-proxy.sh.\n\nAnother detail — inside the make-proxy container's python, we need `import shutil` for tokenizer copy, and numpy for randn? Use torch for randn (deterministic seed), then convert. bf16 bytes: t.to(torch.bfloat16).view(torch.int16).numpy().tobytes() — view requires contiguous ✓ .numpy on int16 ✓.\n\nfp8 zeros: torch.zeros(shape, dtype=torch.float8_e4m3fn) → view torch.uint8 → bytes. For nonzero small values: (torch.rand×2a−a).to(fp8). Keep mostly zeros + small randn embed for safety.\n\ne4m3 scale_inv: per-block [128,128] → shape (ceil(rows/128), ceil(cols/128)) fp32 ones.\n\nSafetensors serializer padding: format has no per-tensor alignment requirement? Spec: data_offsets absolute; alignment recommended 8-byte for zero-copy — my offsets: accumulate; pad each blob to 8 for safety (pad after each blob, not included in offsets). Implement pad after each tensor blob.\n\nEdge: empty header dict when no tensors — not applicable.\n\n\"__metadata__\" optional — add {\"format\":\"pt\"}. vLLM doesn't care; discover parses name→spec entries; must skip \"__metadata__\" — does discover's code handle it? parse_safetensors_header probably ignores metadata (header entries without data_offsets). Their parser reads the tensor entries — metadata entries lack dtype/shape; a strict parser could choke. Actual checkpoints don't carry format metadata? HF write adds {\"format\":\"pt\"}. Upstream parse_safetensors_header (ple_mmap.py:125-170) — unknown handling. Safest: omit __metadata__. ✓ Omit.\n\nFile naming: single main file `model-00001-of-00001.safetensors` + per-shard ple files `model-ple-{layer}-{shard:05d}.safetensors` (mirror fixture naming from dossier).\n\nNow — subtle point about discover_shards globbing: globs `*.safetensors` in model_path (flat). All files flat under OUT ✓.\n\nTime to write. Also don't forget acceptance: run-proxy.sh must contain literal `results/receipts/proxy.json` — my OUT= line contains it ✓.\n\nPython heredoc inside bash: use quoted 'PY' to avoid expansion. Pass variables via -e env.\n\nAlso decide FN_SERVED name for the proxy: \"flashnext-proxy\".\n\nOK let's write make-proxy.sh in full now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I now have the full picture. Key facts:\n\n- Fork is at `/opt/vllm` in the container; its mmap module lives at `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/common/ple_mmap.py` (patch 0009), with fixture naming `model-ple-{layer}-{shard:05d}.safetensors` and shard tensor names `layers.{i}.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_{j}.weight`.\n- The fork's `check_cudagraph_safety` guard **refuses plain-eager and full-graph capture** under `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1`; ruling P10 sanctions piecewise mode. So `run-proxy.sh` must run `-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE`, not eager.\n- Receipt shape: `{\"step\",\"status\",\"ts\",\"data\"}`; run-smoke.sh is the style reference; fn-env.sh gives env doctrine (no is-set-probe exports).\n- Workload config facts from evidence: `Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration`, `model_type qwen4_exp`, `layer_types` 3×linear+1×full, `hidden_size 2560`, `head_dim 256`.\n\nNow writing `scripts/make-proxy.sh`:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7db45de74a904edfb3d5852f","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# scripts/make-proxy.sh — the proxy checkpoint builder (prep for spec claim 4.1).\n#\n# Builds a tiny synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy with the\n# vocabulary contract of spec.md (\"proxy checkpoint\"): the same architecture\n# identifier and expert format as the workload — a handful of layers, 8 routed\n# experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size [128, 128], a small engram/PLE\n# lookup table under exactly the shard tensor naming the mmap path's\n# discover_shards expects, plus a tokenizer so the server never reaches for a\n# hub (spec F.6). The result proves the admitted kernel path and the ported\n# table path on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded.\n#\n# Fork-scaffold reuse doctrine (task goal: reuse, do not invent):\n#   - The base config is the staged workload config shrunk, whenever\n#     /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8/config.json is present, so every\n#     field the fork's config class reads keeps its exact shape.\n#   - The PLE table naming is validated against the fork's own mmap module\n#     (vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common.ple_mmap: _SHARD_RE, discover_shards),\n#     and the fork's tests/models/qwen4_exp scaffolding is probed for a\n#     shard-writer before the built-in writer is used.\n#   - Weight tensor names are derived from the fork's own model class by\n#     meta-device instantiation whenever that is possible; the curated\n#     qwen3-next-family naming below is the fallback only.\n#\n# The checkpoint directory is disposable by construction: it is rebuilt from\n# scratch on every run. Host-side default location keeps it OUTSIDE the repo\n# (compare container/build.sh's cache doctrine); override with FN_PROXY_DIR.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nPROXY_DIR=\"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-${FN_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext}/proxy-checkpoint}\"\nMODEL_DIR=\"${FN_MODEL_DIR:-/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8}\"\n\nlog() { echo \"make-proxy: $*\" >&2; }\n\nmkdir -p \"$PROXY_DIR\"\nfind \"$PROXY_DIR\" -mindepth 1 -delete\nlog \"building the proxy checkpoint at $PROXY_DIR\"\n\nMOUNTS=(-v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nif [ -f \"$MODEL_DIR/config.json\" ]; then\n    log \"staged workload config present at $MODEL_DIR — shrinking it as the base\"\n    MOUNTS+=(-v \"$MODEL_DIR:/models:ro\")\nelse\n    log \"no staged workload config at $MODEL_DIR — falling back to the evidence template\"\nfi\n\npodman run --rm \\\n    -e FN_PROXY_LAYERS=\"${FN_PROXY_LAYERS:-8}\" \\\n    -e FN_PROXY_EXPERTS=\"${FN_PROXY_EXPERTS:-8}\" \\\n    \"${MOUNTS[@]}\" \\\n    \"$IMAGE\" python3 - <<'PY'\n\"\"\"Build /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy: config + tokenizer + weights + PLE shards.\n\nEvery stage is loud: a stage that cannot complete raises with a typed message,\nand a manifest (proxy-manifest.json) records what was reused, what was\nfallback, and every residual risk, so run-proxy.sh and the morning ledger can\ngrade provenance rather than narrate it.\n\"\"\"\nimport importlib\nimport inspect\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport traceback\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport torch\n\nOUT = Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nMODELS = Path(\"/models\")  # read-only mount of the staged workload, if present\nLAYERS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_LAYERS\", \"8\"))\nEXPERTS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_EXPERTS\", \"8\"))\nTOPK = 2\nMOE_INTER = 256  # multiple of the 128 block size\nBLOCK = 128\nSEED = 42\n\nMANIFEST = {\n    \"built_by\": \"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\n    \"ts\": time.strftime(\"%FT%T\"),\n    \"geometry\": {\"layers\": LAYERS, \"experts\": EXPERTS,\n                 \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]},\n    \"base_config_source\": None,\n    \"config_edits\": {},\n    \"tokenizer_source\": None,\n    \"scaffold\": {\"fork_modules_probed\": [], \"reused\": [], \"validation\": []},\n    \"weight_source\": None,\n    \"files\": [],\n    \"warnings\": [],\n}\n\n\ndef note(msg):\n    print(f\"make-proxy: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    MANIFEST[\"warnings\"].append(msg)\n\n\ndef die(msg):\n    raise SystemExit(f\"make-proxy: FATAL: {msg}\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 1 — config: shrink the workload config, else the evidence template\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef load_base_config():\n    p = MODELS / \"config.json\"\n    if p.is_file():\n        return json.loads(p.read_text()), \"workload:%s\" % p\n    # Typed fallback: field values observed in the workload config per\n    # specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 3.3, completed\n    # with the PLE geometry names per specs/flashnext/evidence/\n    # moe-dispatch.md section 5. Only used when staging has not landed.\n    tmpl = {\n        \"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],\n        \"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\",\n        \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\",\n        \"hidden_size\": 2560,\n        \"head_dim\": 256,\n        \"num_attention_heads\": 16,\n        \"num_key_value_heads\": 2,\n        \"num_hidden_layers\": LAYERS,\n        \"full_attention_interval\": 4,\n        \"layer_types\": [],\n        \"vocab_size\": 4096,\n        \"max_position_embeddings\": 4096,\n        \"rms_norm_eps\": 1e-6,\n        \"tie_word_embeddings\": False,\n        \"use_qk_norm\": True,\n        \"decoder_sparse_step\": 1,\n        \"num_experts\": EXPERTS,\n        \"num_experts_per_tok\": TOPK,\n        \"moe_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"indexer_budget\": 2048,\n        \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 512,\n        \"heads_per_ngram\": 1,\n        \"ple_embed_dim\": 256,\n        \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 128,\n        \"split_ngram_parts\": 2,\n    }\n    return tmpl, \"template:evidence-dotfiles-observed-3.3+moe-dispatch-5\"\n\n\ndef shrink(cfg):\n    edits = {}\n\n    def set_(key, val):\n        edits[key] = [cfg.get(key), val]\n        cfg[key] = val\n\n    archs = cfg.get(\"architectures\") or []\n    if not any(\"Qwen4Exp\" in a for a in archs):\n        die(f\"base config architectures {archs} carry no Qwen4Exp identifier; \"\n            \"refusing to relabel a foreign model as the proxy\")\n    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    interval = int(cfg.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4))\n    pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\n    set_(\"num_experts\", EXPERTS)\n    set_(\"num_experts_per_tok\",\n         min(int(cfg.get(\"num_experts_per_tok\", TOPK)), EXPERTS))\n    # Every layer routed-MoE, so the admitted block-FP8 kernel runs on every\n    # decode step of the proxy serve.\n    set_(\"decoder_sparse_step\", 1)\n    set_(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"intermediate_size\", 2 * BLOCK)\n    set_(\"max_position_embeddings\",\n         min(int(cfg.get(\"max_position_embeddings\", 4096)), 4096))\n    if not (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file():\n        set_(\"vocab_size\", 4096)  # template tokenizer is paired with 4096\n    # Block-FP8 for the routed experts is the workload's expert format; the\n    # proxy quantizes every Linear so BOTH admitted paths run (the 0008 MoE\n    # admission and the 0012 linear twin). embed/lm_head stay bf16 by the\n    # loader's own rule.\n    set_(\"quantization_config\",\n         {\"quant_method\": \"fp8\", \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]})\n    # Small PLE table: shrink every large ngram-size field; keep heads/dims.\n    for key in list(cfg):\n        if \"ngram\" in key.lower() and re.search(r\"(size|base|vocab)\",\n                                                key.lower()):\n            val = cfg[key]\n            if isinstance(val, int) and val > 512:\n                set_(key, 512)\n    split_key = next((k for k in cfg\n                      if \"split\" in k.lower() and \"ngram\" in k.lower()), None)\n    if split_key is not None:\n        set_(split_key, 2)\n    return edits\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 2 — tokenizer: copy from the staged workload, else synthesize a pair\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef stage_tokenizer(cfg):\n    copied = []\n    for name in (\"tokenizer.json\", \"tokenizer_config.json\",\n                 \"special_tokens_map.json\", \"vocab.json\", \"merges.txt\",\n                 \"generation_config.json\", \"chat_template.jinja\"):\n        src = MODELS / name\n        if src.is_file():\n            shutil.copy2(src, OUT / name)\n            copied.append(name)\n    if any(n.startswith(\"tokenizer\") for n in copied):\n        return \"workload:\" + \",\".join(copied)\n    # Synthetic WordLevel tokenizer paired with the template vocab_size 4096.\n    specials = [\"<pad>\", \"<bos>\", \"<eos>\", \"<unk>\"]\n    vocab = {tok: i for i, tok in enumerate(specials)}\n    i = len(specials)\n    for c in (chr(x) for x in range(33, 127)):\n        vocab[c] = i\n        i += 1\n    for word in (\"the\", \"a\", \"of\", \"and\", \"to\", \"in\", \"is\", \"on\", \"for\",\n                 \"with\", \"that\", \"this\", \"night\", \"pair\", \"proxy\", \"light\"):\n        if i >= int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"]):\n            break\n        vocab[word] = i\n        i += 1\n    added = [{\"id\": n, \"content\": tok, \"single_word\": False, \"lstrip\": False,\n              \"rstrip\": False, \"normalized\": False, \"special\": True}\n             for tok, n in zip(specials, range(len(specials)))]\n    tok_json = {\n        \"version\": \"1.0\", \"truncation\": None, \"padding\": None,\n        \"added_tokens\": added,\n        \"normalizer\": {\"type\": \"NFC\"},\n        \"pre_tokenizer\": {\"type\": \"Whitespace\"},\n        \"post_processor\": None,\n        \"decoder\": {\"type\": \"WordLevel\"},\n        \"model\": {\"type\": \"WordLevel\", \"vocab\": vocab, \"unk_token\": \"<unk>\"},\n    }\n    (OUT / \"tokenizer.json\").write_text(json.dumps(tok_json))\n    (OUT / \"tokenizer_config.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\n        \"tokenizer_class\": \"PreTrainedTokenizerFast\",\n        \"model_max_length\": 4096,\n        \"pad_token\": \"<pad>\", \"bos_token\": \"<bos>\",\n        \"eos_token\": \"<eos>\", \"unk_token\": \"<unk>\",\n    }))\n    note(\"no staged workload tokenizer: synthesized a WordLevel pair \"\n         \"(proxy output text quality is not the claim; finite logits are)\")\n    return \"synthetic-wordlevel\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 3 — the fork's own scaffolding: probe, reuse where possible\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef probe_fork_scaffolds():\n    \"\"\"Probe the fork's tests/models/qwen4_exp tree for reusable writers and\n    import its ple_mmap module as the naming authority (_SHARD_RE).\"\"\"\n    ple_mmap = None\n    try:\n        from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common import ple_mmap as _pm\n        ple_mmap = _pm\n        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n            \"vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common.ple_mmap (naming authority)\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        try:\n            from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia import ple_mmap as _pm\n            ple_mmap = _pm\n            MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n                \"vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.ple_mmap (pre-0009 location)\")\n        except Exception as e2:\n            note(f\"ple_mmap not importable ({e!r}, {e2!r}); the serve itself \"\n                 \"remains the naming authority\")\n    sys.path.insert(0, \"/opt/vllm/tests\")\n    for modname in (\"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap_amd\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple\"):\n        entry = {\"module\": modname}\n        try:\n            mod = importlib.import_module(modname)\n            writers = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                       if callable(getattr(mod, n, None)) and re.search(\n                           r\"(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|ckpt|\"\n                           r\"checkpoint|fixture)\", n, re.I)]\n            entry[\"callable_writers\"] = writers\n            for wname in writers:\n                fn = getattr(mod, wname)\n                try:\n                    sig = inspect.signature(fn)\n                except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                    continue\n                # Reuse only a writer with a single path-like argument;\n                # anything else is a pytest fixture contract we must not guess.\n                pos = [p for p in sig.parameters.values()\n                       if p.kind in (p.POSITIONAL_ONLY, p.POSITIONAL_OR_KEYWORD)\n                       and p.default is p.empty]\n                if len(sig.parameters) == 1 and len(pos) <= 1:\n                    try:\n                        fn(str(OUT))\n                        entry[\"invoked\"] = wname\n                        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n                            f\"{modname}.{wname}\")\n                        break\n                    except Exception as e3:\n                        entry[f\"{wname}_error\"] = f\"{e3.__class__.__name__}\"\n        except Exception as e:\n            entry[\"import\"] = f\"FAIL {e.__class__.__name__}: {e}\"\n        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"fork_modules_probed\"].append(entry)\n    return ple_mmap\n\n\ndef ngram_geometry(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Mirror the loader's shard mapping (specs/flashnext/evidence/\n    ple-54129.md section 3): shard_size = ceil(org / split); the checkpoint\n    carries ceil(org / shard_size) row-block tensors per PLE layer.\"\"\"\n    base = int(cfg.get(\"ngram_vocab_size_base\", 512))\n    heads = int(cfg.get(\"heads_per_ngram\", 1))\n    div = int(cfg.get(\"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\", 1) or 1)\n    split = int(cfg.get(\"split_ngram_parts\", 512))\n    total = base * heads\n    padded = math.ceil(total / div) * div if div > 1 else total\n    return {\"base\": base, \"heads\": heads, \"divisible_by\": div,\n            \"split\": split, \"padded_rows\": padded,\n            \"rows_per_shard\": math.ceil(padded / split) if split else padded,\n            \"note\": \"mirror of (org + split - 1) // split; a mismatch is \"\n                    \"caught by the discover_shards validation below\"}\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 4 — weights: fork introspection first, curated naming as fallback\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef _bf16(t):\n    return (\"BF16\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous().view(torch.int16).numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef _fp8(t):\n    return (\"F8_E4M3\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.float8_e4m3fn).contiguous().view(torch.uint8).numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef _f32(t):\n    return (\"F32\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.float32).contiguous().numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef save_safetensors(path, tensors):\n    \"\"\"Minimal safetensors serializer (8-byte LE header length, JSON header,\n    packed blobs) so fp8 tensors never depend on library-version support.\"\"\"\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        pad = (8 - len(raw) % 8) % 8\n        blobs.append(raw + b\"\\x00\" * pad)\n        offset += len(raw) + pad\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    hpad = (8 - len(hjson) % 8) % 8\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\n        f.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)\n\n\ndef scale_inv_shape(shape):\n    return [math.ceil(d / BLOCK) for d in shape]\n\n\ndef try_fork_introspection(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Instantiate the fork's model class on the meta device and return the\n    exact parameter list, or None. When this works, weight names are the\n    fork's own, not the curated fallback's.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from vllm.config import ModelConfig, VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config\n        from vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry\n        torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]\n            with torch.device(\"meta\"):\n                model = cls(vllm_config=vc)\n        params = [(n, tuple(p.shape)) for n, p in model.named_parameters()]\n        stacked = list(getattr(model, \"stacked_params_mapping\", []))\n        if not params:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"model instantiated with zero parameters\")\n        return params, stacked\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"fork model introspection unavailable \"\n             f\"({e.__class__.__name__}: {e}); using the curated fallback \"\n             \"naming with its typed residual risks\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef probe_ignore_semantics():\n    \"\"\"Empirically determine how Fp8Config consumes modules_to_not_convert\n    (regex match vs literal membership) and, if regex, install a skip-list\n    that keeps every non-expert Linear UNQUANTIZED — an unprovided quantized\n    parameter is uninitialized fp8 memory, and NaN bits there would poison\n    the finite-logits claim. Returns True when the skip-list is active.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        import vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 as fp8mod\n        src = inspect.getsource(fp8mod)\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"Fp8Config source probe unavailable: {e!r}\")\n        return False\n    if re.search(r\"re\\.(match|search|fullmatch)\\s*\\([^)]*ignored\", src):\n        return True  # regex semantics: the negative-lookahead pattern works\n    note(\"Fp8Config appears to consume modules_to_not_convert by literal \"\n         \"membership; skipping the ignore-list (quantize-all mode)\")\n    return False\n\n\ndef curated_weights(cfg):\n    \"\"\"qwen3-next-family HF naming; the fallback path. Residual risks, typed:\n    (a) linear-attention module tensors are left to the fork's own init —\n    safe only when the ignore-list keeps them unquantized; (b) PLE shards are\n    written for EVERY layer on the family's per-layer PLE signature.\"\"\"\n    H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E, M = EXPERTS, int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n    S = int(cfg.get(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", 0) or 0)\n    gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n    tensors = {}\n    emb = torch.randn(V, H, generator=gen) * 0.02\n    tensors[\"model.embed_tokens.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    tensors[\"model.norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):\n        if quantized:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n            tensors[name + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n        else:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n\n    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n    for i, lt in enumerate(cfg[\"layer_types\"]):\n        p = f\"model.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            linear(f\"{a}.q_proj\", (NH * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.k_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.v_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.o_proj\", (H, NH * HD), quantize_linears)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n        # linear_attention layers: no checkpoint tensors are written — the\n        # fork's own init covers them when they stay unquantized (see above).\n        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        tensors[f\"{m}.gate.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(E, H))\n        for e in range(E):\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (M, H)), (\"up_proj\", (M, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, M))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.experts.{e}.{proj}\", shape, True)\n        if S > 0:\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (S, H)), (\"up_proj\", (S, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, S))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.shared_experts.{proj}\", shape, quantize_linears)\n    return tensors\n\n\ndef write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):\n    \"\"\"One row-block tensor per shard under the discover_shards naming, plus\n    the per-layer global weight_scale the load_weights interception keeps.\n    Values are fp8 zeros at scale 1.0: the PLE contribution is exactly zero,\n    which is finite by construction.\"\"\"\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    rows, split = geom[\"rows_per_shard\"], geom[\"split\"]\n    files = 0\n    scale = _f32(torch.ones(1))\n    main = {}\n    for layer in range(int(cfg[\"num_hidden_layers\"])):\n        for s in range(split):\n            name = (f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n                    f\"ngram_embedding.shard_{s:05d}.weight\")\n            save_safetensors(\n                OUT / f\"model-ple-{layer}-{s:05d}.safetensors\",\n                {name: _fp8(torch.zeros(rows, HD))})\n            files += 1\n        main[f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n             f\"ngram_embedding.weight_scale\"] = scale\n    return files, main\n\n\ndef validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom):\n    if ple_mmap is None:\n        note(\"skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)\")\n        return\n    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))\n    per_layer = {int(k): v for k, v in getattr(found, \"items\", lambda: found)()} \\\n        if isinstance(found, dict) else found\n    entry = {\"per_layer_shards\": {str(k): len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items()}}\n    expected = geom[\"split\"]\n    bad = {k: len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items() if len(v) != expected}\n    entry[\"expected_shards_per_layer\"] = expected\n    MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"validation\"].append(entry)\n    if bad:\n        die(f\"discover_shards found {bad} shards where the geometry expects \"\n            f\"{expected} per layer — the mmap path would refuse this table at \"\n            \"attach time; refusing to hand run-proxy.sh a doomed checkpoint\")\n    # Row-count cross-check against the mirror formula, via the first shard.\n    first = next(iter(per_layer.values()))[0]\n    rows = first[2] if isinstance(first, tuple) else None\n    if rows is not None and rows != geom[\"rows_per_shard\"]:\n        note(f\"discover_shards reports {rows} rows/shard vs the mirror's \"\n             f\"{geom['rows_per_shard']} — the serve is the tiebreaker\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# main\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef main():\n    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    cfg, source = load_base_config()\n    MANIFEST[\"base_config_source\"] = source\n    MANIFEST[\"config_edits\"] = shrink(cfg)\n\n    MANIFEST[\"tokenizer_source\"] = stage_tokenizer(cfg)\n\n    # Write config.json first: both fork introspection and the fork's config\n    # class read the checkpoint directory as the model path.\n    (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n\n    ple_mmap = probe_fork_scaffolds()\n    geom = ngram_geometry(cfg)\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ngram\"] = geom\n\n    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    if probe_ignore_semantics():\n        # Negative lookahead: skip every Linear except the routed experts.\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"]\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(\"modules_to_not_convert installed with regex semantics observed \"\n             \"in the fork's Fp8Config — non-expert linears stay unquantized\")\n\n    if introspected:\n        # Exact names from the fork's own class. Fused params are split back\n        # into their HF-side names; every other parameter is written under its\n        # own name, fp8-quantized iff it is an experts weight.\n        params, stacked = introspected\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n        V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n        tensors = {}\n        fused = {}  # vllm suffix -> (hf suffix, shard ids)\n        for vllm_sfx, hf_sfx, shard_id in stacked:\n            fused.setdefault(vllm_sfx, []).append((hf_sfx, shard_id))\n        for name, shape in params:\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and shape and len(shape) == 2:\n                base = name[:-len(\".weight\")]\n                hit = None\n                for vllm_sfx, entries in fused.items():\n                    if base.endswith(vllm_sfx):\n                        hit = (base[:-len(vllm_sfx)], entries)\n                        break\n                if hit:\n                    stem, entries = hit\n                    total_rows = shape[0]\n                    for hf_sfx, shard_id in entries:\n                        rows = total_rows // len(entries)\n                        sub = (rows, shape[1])\n                        hname = f\"{stem}{hf_sfx}\"\n                        if \".mlp.experts.\" in hname:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(sub))\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(sub)))\n                        else:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(sub))\n                    continue\n                if \".mlp.experts.\" in name and \"scale\" not in name:\n                    tensors[name] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n                    tensors[name[:-len(\".weight\")] + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = \\\n                        _f32(torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n                    continue\n            if \"embed_tokens\" in name and len(shape) == 2:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.randn(*shape, generator=gen) * 0.02)\n                continue\n            if \"norm\" in name and len(shape) == 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.ones(shape[0]))\n                continue\n            if len(shape) >= 1 and \"scale\" not in name:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n    else:\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"curated-fallback\"\n        tensors = curated_weights(cfg)\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n\n    shard_files, scale_tensors = write_ple_shards(cfg, geom)\n    if scale_tensors:\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-ple-scales.safetensors\", scale_tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-ple-scales.safetensors\")\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ple_shard_files\"] = shard_files\n    validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom)\n\n    manifest_path = OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\"\n    manifest_path.write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    total_bytes = sum(f.stat().st_size for f in OUT.iterdir() if f.is_file())\n    n_files = len(list(OUT.glob(\"*.safetensors\")))\n    print(f\"make-proxy: checkpoint complete: {n_files} safetensors files, \"\n          f\"{total_bytes / 2**20:.1f} MiB, weight_source=\"\n          f\"{MANIFEST['weight_source']}, base={source}\")\n    if MANIFEST[\"warnings\"]:\n        print(f\"make-proxy: {len(MANIFEST['warnings'])} warning(s) recorded \"\n              \"in proxy-manifest.json\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ntry:\n    main()\nexcept SystemExit as e:\n    try:\n        (OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    print(f\"{e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(1)\nexcept Exception:\n    traceback.print_exc()\n    try:\n        MANIFEST[\"warnings\"].append(\"unhandled exception; see container log\")\n        (OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    sys.exit(1)\nPY\n\nlog \"checkpoint ready at $PROXY_DIR: $(find \"$PROXY_DIR\" -name '*.safetensors' | wc -l) safetensors files\"\nlog \"next: scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":18402,"output":16485,"cacheRead":77824,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":8517,"totalTokens":112711,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787992737715,"responseId":"chatcmpl-d8b69d69-6e2c-46ff-a8c3-40d1030019c4","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_7db45de74a904edfb3d5852f","toolName":"write","args":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# scripts/make-proxy.sh — the proxy checkpoint builder (prep for spec claim 4.1).\n#\n# Builds a tiny synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy with the\n# vocabulary contract of spec.md (\"proxy checkpoint\"): the same architecture\n# identifier and expert format as the workload — a handful of layers, 8 routed\n# experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size [128, 128], a small engram/PLE\n# lookup table under exactly the shard tensor naming the mmap path's\n# discover_shards expects, plus a tokenizer so the server never reaches for a\n# hub (spec F.6). The result proves the admitted kernel path and the ported\n# table path on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded.\n#\n# Fork-scaffold reuse doctrine (task goal: reuse, do not invent):\n#   - The base config is the staged workload config shrunk, whenever\n#     /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8/config.json is present, so every\n#     field the fork's config class reads keeps its exact shape.\n#   - The PLE table naming is validated against the fork's own mmap module\n#     (vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common.ple_mmap: _SHARD_RE, discover_shards),\n#     and the fork's tests/models/qwen4_exp scaffolding is probed for a\n#     shard-writer before the built-in writer is used.\n#   - Weight tensor names are derived from the fork's own model class by\n#     meta-device instantiation whenever that is possible; the curated\n#     qwen3-next-family naming below is the fallback only.\n#\n# The checkpoint directory is disposable by construction: it is rebuilt from\n# scratch on every run. Host-side default location keeps it OUTSIDE the repo\n# (compare container/build.sh's cache doctrine); override with FN_PROXY_DIR.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nPROXY_DIR=\"${FN_PROXY_DIR:-${FN_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.local/state/flashnext}/proxy-checkpoint}\"\nMODEL_DIR=\"${FN_MODEL_DIR:-/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8}\"\n\nlog() { echo \"make-proxy: $*\" >&2; }\n\nmkdir -p \"$PROXY_DIR\"\nfind \"$PROXY_DIR\" -mindepth 1 -delete\nlog \"building the proxy checkpoint at $PROXY_DIR\"\n\nMOUNTS=(-v \"$PROXY_DIR:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nif [ -f \"$MODEL_DIR/config.json\" ]; then\n    log \"staged workload config present at $MODEL_DIR — shrinking it as the base\"\n    MOUNTS+=(-v \"$MODEL_DIR:/models:ro\")\nelse\n    log \"no staged workload config at $MODEL_DIR — falling back to the evidence template\"\nfi\n\npodman run --rm \\\n    -e FN_PROXY_LAYERS=\"${FN_PROXY_LAYERS:-8}\" \\\n    -e FN_PROXY_EXPERTS=\"${FN_PROXY_EXPERTS:-8}\" \\\n    \"${MOUNTS[@]}\" \\\n    \"$IMAGE\" python3 - <<'PY'\n\"\"\"Build /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy: config + tokenizer + weights + PLE shards.\n\nEvery stage is loud: a stage that cannot complete raises with a typed message,\nand a manifest (proxy-manifest.json) records what was reused, what was\nfallback, and every residual risk, so run-proxy.sh and the morning ledger can\ngrade provenance rather than narrate it.\n\"\"\"\nimport importlib\nimport inspect\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport traceback\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport torch\n\nOUT = Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nMODELS = Path(\"/models\")  # read-only mount of the staged workload, if present\nLAYERS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_LAYERS\", \"8\"))\nEXPERTS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_PROXY_EXPERTS\", \"8\"))\nTOPK = 2\nMOE_INTER = 256  # multiple of the 128 block size\nBLOCK = 128\nSEED = 42\n\nMANIFEST = {\n    \"built_by\": \"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\n    \"ts\": time.strftime(\"%FT%T\"),\n    \"geometry\": {\"layers\": LAYERS, \"experts\": EXPERTS,\n                 \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]},\n    \"base_config_source\": None,\n    \"config_edits\": {},\n    \"tokenizer_source\": None,\n    \"scaffold\": {\"fork_modules_probed\": [], \"reused\": [], \"validation\": []},\n    \"weight_source\": None,\n    \"files\": [],\n    \"warnings\": [],\n}\n\n\ndef note(msg):\n    print(f\"make-proxy: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    MANIFEST[\"warnings\"].append(msg)\n\n\ndef die(msg):\n    raise SystemExit(f\"make-proxy: FATAL: {msg}\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 1 — config: shrink the workload config, else the evidence template\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef load_base_config():\n    p = MODELS / \"config.json\"\n    if p.is_file():\n        return json.loads(p.read_text()), \"workload:%s\" % p\n    # Typed fallback: field values observed in the workload config per\n    # specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 3.3, completed\n    # with the PLE geometry names per specs/flashnext/evidence/\n    # moe-dispatch.md section 5. Only used when staging has not landed.\n    tmpl = {\n        \"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],\n        \"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\",\n        \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\",\n        \"hidden_size\": 2560,\n        \"head_dim\": 256,\n        \"num_attention_heads\": 16,\n        \"num_key_value_heads\": 2,\n        \"num_hidden_layers\": LAYERS,\n        \"full_attention_interval\": 4,\n        \"layer_types\": [],\n        \"vocab_size\": 4096,\n        \"max_position_embeddings\": 4096,\n        \"rms_norm_eps\": 1e-6,\n        \"tie_word_embeddings\": False,\n        \"use_qk_norm\": True,\n        \"decoder_sparse_step\": 1,\n        \"num_experts\": EXPERTS,\n        \"num_experts_per_tok\": TOPK,\n        \"moe_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\": MOE_INTER,\n        \"indexer_budget\": 2048,\n        \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 512,\n        \"heads_per_ngram\": 1,\n        \"ple_embed_dim\": 256,\n        \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 128,\n        \"split_ngram_parts\": 2,\n    }\n    return tmpl, \"template:evidence-dotfiles-observed-3.3+moe-dispatch-5\"\n\n\ndef shrink(cfg):\n    edits = {}\n\n    def set_(key, val):\n        edits[key] = [cfg.get(key), val]\n        cfg[key] = val\n\n    archs = cfg.get(\"architectures\") or []\n    if not any(\"Qwen4Exp\" in a for a in archs):\n        die(f\"base config architectures {archs} carry no Qwen4Exp identifier; \"\n            \"refusing to relabel a foreign model as the proxy\")\n    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    interval = int(cfg.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4))\n    pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\n    set_(\"num_experts\", EXPERTS)\n    set_(\"num_experts_per_tok\",\n         min(int(cfg.get(\"num_experts_per_tok\", TOPK)), EXPERTS))\n    # Every layer routed-MoE, so the admitted block-FP8 kernel runs on every\n    # decode step of the proxy serve.\n    set_(\"decoder_sparse_step\", 1)\n    set_(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"intermediate_size\" in cfg:\n        set_(\"intermediate_size\", 2 * BLOCK)\n    set_(\"max_position_embeddings\",\n         min(int(cfg.get(\"max_position_embeddings\", 4096)), 4096))\n    if not (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file():\n        set_(\"vocab_size\", 4096)  # template tokenizer is paired with 4096\n    # Block-FP8 for the routed experts is the workload's expert format; the\n    # proxy quantizes every Linear so BOTH admitted paths run (the 0008 MoE\n    # admission and the 0012 linear twin). embed/lm_head stay bf16 by the\n    # loader's own rule.\n    set_(\"quantization_config\",\n         {\"quant_method\": \"fp8\", \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]})\n    # Small PLE table: shrink every large ngram-size field; keep heads/dims.\n    for key in list(cfg):\n        if \"ngram\" in key.lower() and re.search(r\"(size|base|vocab)\",\n                                                key.lower()):\n            val = cfg[key]\n            if isinstance(val, int) and val > 512:\n                set_(key, 512)\n    split_key = next((k for k in cfg\n                      if \"split\" in k.lower() and \"ngram\" in k.lower()), None)\n    if split_key is not None:\n        set_(split_key, 2)\n    return edits\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 2 — tokenizer: copy from the staged workload, else synthesize a pair\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef stage_tokenizer(cfg):\n    copied = []\n    for name in (\"tokenizer.json\", \"tokenizer_config.json\",\n                 \"special_tokens_map.json\", \"vocab.json\", \"merges.txt\",\n                 \"generation_config.json\", \"chat_template.jinja\"):\n        src = MODELS / name\n        if src.is_file():\n            shutil.copy2(src, OUT / name)\n            copied.append(name)\n    if any(n.startswith(\"tokenizer\") for n in copied):\n        return \"workload:\" + \",\".join(copied)\n    # Synthetic WordLevel tokenizer paired with the template vocab_size 4096.\n    specials = [\"<pad>\", \"<bos>\", \"<eos>\", \"<unk>\"]\n    vocab = {tok: i for i, tok in enumerate(specials)}\n    i = len(specials)\n    for c in (chr(x) for x in range(33, 127)):\n        vocab[c] = i\n        i += 1\n    for word in (\"the\", \"a\", \"of\", \"and\", \"to\", \"in\", \"is\", \"on\", \"for\",\n                 \"with\", \"that\", \"this\", \"night\", \"pair\", \"proxy\", \"light\"):\n        if i >= int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"]):\n            break\n        vocab[word] = i\n        i += 1\n    added = [{\"id\": n, \"content\": tok, \"single_word\": False, \"lstrip\": False,\n              \"rstrip\": False, \"normalized\": False, \"special\": True}\n             for tok, n in zip(specials, range(len(specials)))]\n    tok_json = {\n        \"version\": \"1.0\", \"truncation\": None, \"padding\": None,\n        \"added_tokens\": added,\n        \"normalizer\": {\"type\": \"NFC\"},\n        \"pre_tokenizer\": {\"type\": \"Whitespace\"},\n        \"post_processor\": None,\n        \"decoder\": {\"type\": \"WordLevel\"},\n        \"model\": {\"type\": \"WordLevel\", \"vocab\": vocab, \"unk_token\": \"<unk>\"},\n    }\n    (OUT / \"tokenizer.json\").write_text(json.dumps(tok_json))\n    (OUT / \"tokenizer_config.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\n        \"tokenizer_class\": \"PreTrainedTokenizerFast\",\n        \"model_max_length\": 4096,\n        \"pad_token\": \"<pad>\", \"bos_token\": \"<bos>\",\n        \"eos_token\": \"<eos>\", \"unk_token\": \"<unk>\",\n    }))\n    note(\"no staged workload tokenizer: synthesized a WordLevel pair \"\n         \"(proxy output text quality is not the claim; finite logits are)\")\n    return \"synthetic-wordlevel\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 3 — the fork's own scaffolding: probe, reuse where possible\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef probe_fork_scaffolds():\n    \"\"\"Probe the fork's tests/models/qwen4_exp tree for reusable writers and\n    import its ple_mmap module as the naming authority (_SHARD_RE).\"\"\"\n    ple_mmap = None\n    try:\n        from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common import ple_mmap as _pm\n        ple_mmap = _pm\n        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n            \"vllm.models.qwen4_exp.common.ple_mmap (naming authority)\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        try:\n            from vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia import ple_mmap as _pm\n            ple_mmap = _pm\n            MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n                \"vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.ple_mmap (pre-0009 location)\")\n        except Exception as e2:\n            note(f\"ple_mmap not importable ({e!r}, {e2!r}); the serve itself \"\n                 \"remains the naming authority\")\n    sys.path.insert(0, \"/opt/vllm/tests\")\n    for modname in (\"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap_amd\",\n                    \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple\"):\n        entry = {\"module\": modname}\n        try:\n            mod = importlib.import_module(modname)\n            writers = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                       if callable(getattr(mod, n, None)) and re.search(\n                           r\"(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|ckpt|\"\n                           r\"checkpoint|fixture)\", n, re.I)]\n            entry[\"callable_writers\"] = writers\n            for wname in writers:\n                fn = getattr(mod, wname)\n                try:\n                    sig = inspect.signature(fn)\n                except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                    continue\n                # Reuse only a writer with a single path-like argument;\n                # anything else is a pytest fixture contract we must not guess.\n                pos = [p for p in sig.parameters.values()\n                       if p.kind in (p.POSITIONAL_ONLY, p.POSITIONAL_OR_KEYWORD)\n                       and p.default is p.empty]\n                if len(sig.parameters) == 1 and len(pos) <= 1:\n                    try:\n                        fn(str(OUT))\n                        entry[\"invoked\"] = wname\n                        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"reused\"].append(\n                            f\"{modname}.{wname}\")\n                        break\n                    except Exception as e3:\n                        entry[f\"{wname}_error\"] = f\"{e3.__class__.__name__}\"\n        except Exception as e:\n            entry[\"import\"] = f\"FAIL {e.__class__.__name__}: {e}\"\n        MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"fork_modules_probed\"].append(entry)\n    return ple_mmap\n\n\ndef ngram_geometry(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Mirror the loader's shard mapping (specs/flashnext/evidence/\n    ple-54129.md section 3): shard_size = ceil(org / split); the checkpoint\n    carries ceil(org / shard_size) row-block tensors per PLE layer.\"\"\"\n    base = int(cfg.get(\"ngram_vocab_size_base\", 512))\n    heads = int(cfg.get(\"heads_per_ngram\", 1))\n    div = int(cfg.get(\"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\", 1) or 1)\n    split = int(cfg.get(\"split_ngram_parts\", 512))\n    total = base * heads\n    padded = math.ceil(total / div) * div if div > 1 else total\n    return {\"base\": base, \"heads\": heads, \"divisible_by\": div,\n            \"split\": split, \"padded_rows\": padded,\n            \"rows_per_shard\": math.ceil(padded / split) if split else padded,\n            \"note\": \"mirror of (org + split - 1) // split; a mismatch is \"\n                    \"caught by the discover_shards validation below\"}\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Stage 4 — weights: fork introspection first, curated naming as fallback\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef _bf16(t):\n    return (\"BF16\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous().view(torch.int16).numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef _fp8(t):\n    return (\"F8_E4M3\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.float8_e4m3fn).contiguous().view(torch.uint8).numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef _f32(t):\n    return (\"F32\", list(t.shape),\n            t.to(torch.float32).contiguous().numpy().tobytes())\n\n\ndef save_safetensors(path, tensors):\n    \"\"\"Minimal safetensors serializer (8-byte LE header length, JSON header,\n    packed blobs) so fp8 tensors never depend on library-version support.\"\"\"\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        pad = (8 - len(raw) % 8) % 8\n        blobs.append(raw + b\"\\x00\" * pad)\n        offset += len(raw) + pad\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    hpad = (8 - len(hjson) % 8) % 8\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\n        f.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)\n\n\ndef scale_inv_shape(shape):\n    return [math.ceil(d / BLOCK) for d in shape]\n\n\ndef try_fork_introspection(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Instantiate the fork's model class on the meta device and return the\n    exact parameter list, or None. When this works, weight names are the\n    fork's own, not the curated fallback's.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from vllm.config import ModelConfig, VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config\n        from vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry\n        torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]\n            with torch.device(\"meta\"):\n                model = cls(vllm_config=vc)\n        params = [(n, tuple(p.shape)) for n, p in model.named_parameters()]\n        stacked = list(getattr(model, \"stacked_params_mapping\", []))\n        if not params:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"model instantiated with zero parameters\")\n        return params, stacked\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"fork model introspection unavailable \"\n             f\"({e.__class__.__name__}: {e}); using the curated fallback \"\n             \"naming with its typed residual risks\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef probe_ignore_semantics():\n    \"\"\"Empirically determine how Fp8Config consumes modules_to_not_convert\n    (regex match vs literal membership) and, if regex, install a skip-list\n    that keeps every non-expert Linear UNQUANTIZED — an unprovided quantized\n    parameter is uninitialized fp8 memory, and NaN bits there would poison\n    the finite-logits claim. Returns True when the skip-list is active.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        import vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.fp8 as fp8mod\n        src = inspect.getsource(fp8mod)\n    except Exception as e:\n        note(f\"Fp8Config source probe unavailable: {e!r}\")\n        return False\n    if re.search(r\"re\\.(match|search|fullmatch)\\s*\\([^)]*ignored\", src):\n        return True  # regex semantics: the negative-lookahead pattern works\n    note(\"Fp8Config appears to consume modules_to_not_convert by literal \"\n         \"membership; skipping the ignore-list (quantize-all mode)\")\n    return False\n\n\ndef curated_weights(cfg):\n    \"\"\"qwen3-next-family HF naming; the fallback path. Residual risks, typed:\n    (a) linear-attention module tensors are left to the fork's own init —\n    safe only when the ignore-list keeps them unquantized; (b) PLE shards are\n    written for EVERY layer on the family's per-layer PLE signature.\"\"\"\n    H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E, M = EXPERTS, int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n    S = int(cfg.get(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", 0) or 0)\n    gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n    tensors = {}\n    emb = torch.randn(V, H, generator=gen) * 0.02\n    tensors[\"model.embed_tokens.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    tensors[\"model.norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):\n        if quantized:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n            tensors[name + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n        else:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n\n    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n    for i, lt in enumerate(cfg[\"layer_types\"]):\n        p = f\"model.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            linear(f\"{a}.q_proj\", (NH * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.k_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.v_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.o_proj\", (H, NH * HD), quantize_linears)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n        # linear_attention layers: no checkpoint tensors are written — the\n        # fork's own init covers them when they stay unquantized (see above).\n        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        tensors[f\"{m}.gate.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(E, H))\n        for e in range(E):\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (M, H)), (\"up_proj\", (M, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, M))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.experts.{e}.{proj}\", shape, True)\n        if S > 0:\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (S, H)), (\"up_proj\", (S, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, S))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.shared_experts.{proj}\", shape, quantize_linears)\n    return tensors\n\n\ndef write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):\n    \"\"\"One row-block tensor per shard under the discover_shards naming, plus\n    the per-layer global weight_scale the load_weights interception keeps.\n    Values are fp8 zeros at scale 1.0: the PLE contribution is exactly zero,\n    which is finite by construction.\"\"\"\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    rows, split = geom[\"rows_per_shard\"], geom[\"split\"]\n    files = 0\n    scale = _f32(torch.ones(1))\n    main = {}\n    for layer in range(int(cfg[\"num_hidden_layers\"])):\n        for s in range(split):\n            name = (f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n                    f\"ngram_embedding.shard_{s:05d}.weight\")\n            save_safetensors(\n                OUT / f\"model-ple-{layer}-{s:05d}.safetensors\",\n                {name: _fp8(torch.zeros(rows, HD))})\n            files += 1\n        main[f\"model.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n             f\"ngram_embedding.weight_scale\"] = scale\n    return files, main\n\n\ndef validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom):\n    if ple_mmap is None:\n        note(\"skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)\")\n        return\n    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))\n    per_layer = {int(k): v for k, v in getattr(found, \"items\", lambda: found)()} \\\n        if isinstance(found, dict) else found\n    entry = {\"per_layer_shards\": {str(k): len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items()}}\n    expected = geom[\"split\"]\n    bad = {k: len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items() if len(v) != expected}\n    entry[\"expected_shards_per_layer\"] = expected\n    MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"validation\"].append(entry)\n    if bad:\n        die(f\"discover_shards found {bad} shards where the geometry expects \"\n            f\"{expected} per layer — the mmap path would refuse this table at \"\n            \"attach time; refusing to hand run-proxy.sh a doomed checkpoint\")\n    # Row-count cross-check against the mirror formula, via the first shard.\n    first = next(iter(per_layer.values()))[0]\n    rows = first[2] if isinstance(first, tuple) else None\n    if rows is not None and rows != geom[\"rows_per_shard\"]:\n        note(f\"discover_shards reports {rows} rows/shard vs the mirror's \"\n             f\"{geom['rows_per_shard']} — the serve is the tiebreaker\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# main\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef main():\n    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    cfg, source = load_base_config()\n    MANIFEST[\"base_config_source\"] = source\n    MANIFEST[\"config_edits\"] = shrink(cfg)\n\n    MANIFEST[\"tokenizer_source\"] = stage_tokenizer(cfg)\n\n    # Write config.json first: both fork introspection and the fork's config\n    # class read the checkpoint directory as the model path.\n    (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n\n    ple_mmap = probe_fork_scaffolds()\n    geom = ngram_geometry(cfg)\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ngram\"] = geom\n\n    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    if probe_ignore_semantics():\n        # Negative lookahead: skip every Linear except the routed experts.\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"]\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(\"modules_to_not_convert installed with regex semantics observed \"\n             \"in the fork's Fp8Config — non-expert linears stay unquantized\")\n\n    if introspected:\n        # Exact names from the fork's own class. Fused params are split back\n        # into their HF-side names; every other parameter is written under its\n        # own name, fp8-quantized iff it is an experts weight.\n        params, stacked = introspected\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n        V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n        tensors = {}\n        fused = {}  # vllm suffix -> (hf suffix, shard ids)\n        for vllm_sfx, hf_sfx, shard_id in stacked:\n            fused.setdefault(vllm_sfx, []).append((hf_sfx, shard_id))\n        for name, shape in params:\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and shape and len(shape) == 2:\n                base = name[:-len(\".weight\")]\n                hit = None\n                for vllm_sfx, entries in fused.items():\n                    if base.endswith(vllm_sfx):\n                        hit = (base[:-len(vllm_sfx)], entries)\n                        break\n                if hit:\n                    stem, entries = hit\n                    total_rows = shape[0]\n                    for hf_sfx, shard_id in entries:\n                        rows = total_rows // len(entries)\n                        sub = (rows, shape[1])\n                        hname = f\"{stem}{hf_sfx}\"\n                        if \".mlp.experts.\" in hname:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(sub))\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(sub)))\n                        else:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(sub))\n                    continue\n                if \".mlp.experts.\" in name and \"scale\" not in name:\n                    tensors[name] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n                    tensors[name[:-len(\".weight\")] + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = \\\n                        _f32(torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n                    continue\n            if \"embed_tokens\" in name and len(shape) == 2:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.randn(*shape, generator=gen) * 0.02)\n                continue\n            if \"norm\" in name and len(shape) == 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.ones(shape[0]))\n                continue\n            if len(shape) >= 1 and \"scale\" not in name:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n    else:\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"curated-fallback\"\n        tensors = curated_weights(cfg)\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n\n    shard_files, scale_tensors = write_ple_shards(cfg, geom)\n    if scale_tensors:\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-ple-scales.safetensors\", scale_tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-ple-scales.safetensors\")\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ple_shard_files\"] = shard_files\n    validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom)\n\n    manifest_path = OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\"\n    manifest_path.write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    total_bytes = sum(f.stat().st_size for f in OUT.iterdir() if f.is_file())\n    n_files = len(list(OUT.glob(\"*.safetensors\")))\n    print(f\"make-proxy: checkpoint complete: {n_files} safetensors files, \"\n          f\"{total_bytes / 2**20:.1f} MiB, weight_source=\"\n          f\"{MANIFEST['weight_source']}, base={source}\")\n    if MANIFEST[\"warnings\"]:\n        print(f\"make-proxy: {len(MANIFEST['warnings'])} warning(s) recorded \"\n              \"in proxy-manifest.json\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ntry:\n    main()\nexcept SystemExit as e:\n    try:\n        (OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    print(f\"{e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(1)\nexcept Exception:\n    traceback.print_exc()\n    try:\n        MANIFEST[\"warnings\"].append(\"unhandled exception; see container log\")\n        (OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    sys.exit(1)\nPY\n\nlog \"checkpoint ready at $PROXY_DIR: $(find \"$PROXY_DIR\" -name '*.safetensors' | wc -l) safetensors files\"\nlog \"next: scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\n"}}
