he ERR trap already recorded the fail receipt.\n-if [ ! -f \"$OUT\" ]; then\n-    write_receipt \"fail\" '{\"error\": \"receipt stage never ran\"}'\n-fi\n+# A non-zero exit above means the step failed; the ERR trap has recorded the\n+# fail receipt (or kept the one the python stage wrote) and cleaned up.\n cleanup_container\n-\n log \"receipt: $OUT\"\n-python3 - \"$OUT\" <<'PY'\n-import json, sys\n-r = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\n-sys.exit(0 if r.get(\"status\") == \"pass\" else 1)\n-PY\n","firstChangedLine":277},"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993187063},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Also: when the python stage exits with 1 (fail status), the ERR trap fires and calls on_error → write_receipt's fail (if already exists it gets preserved ✓) → cleanup_container → exit 1. Good. But note: in the fail path, the receipt written by python is preserved, because write_receipt checks the existing parseable receipt with step==\"proxy\" ✓.\n\nHowever — in the success path, python exits 0, then cleanup_container (no-op, already rm'd), log. Good.\n\nOne issue: in the success path, the python stage has already done podman rm; then `podman rm -f` in cleanup_container becomes a no-op ✓.\n\nAlso, the trap on the python heredoc failure line: `trap 'on_error $LINENO' ERR` — when python exits 1, LINENO = line of the heredoc. OK.\n\nNext, also verify that the FN_DATA environment variable usage in on_error is fine: it builds the data JSON via python -c using FN_TAIL/FN_LINE, then calls write_receipt. OK.\n\nWait, there's still a problem with write_receipt in on_error: the `$(python3 -c ...)` command substitution inside on_error — if it fails, set -e... inside the trap, ERR trap recursion is disabled by default. Acceptable.\n\nNext, check bash -n on both scripts. Also grep for the acceptance literals. After that, write tests/test_proxy_tooling.py and run the test suite.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d46960232eec45bea9864b8a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && chmod +x scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && bash -n scripts/run-proxy.sh && echo SYNTAX-OK && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh && echo GREP-OK"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1826,"output":433,"cacheRead":115712,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":313,"totalTokens":117971,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993187068,"responseId":"chatcmpl-559a388c-8487-47c1-ad62-5d55f5b65110","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d46960232eec45bea9864b8a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SYNTAX-OK\nGREP-OK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993200519},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Also, extract the heredoc and run py_compile to validate the embedded python. Let's extract it and check the syntax.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me syntax-check the embedded Python heredocs too:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b4249d2155cb4dd480ce1d5d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && for s in make-proxy run-proxy; do awk '/<<.PY.$/{f=1;next} /^PY$/{f=0} f' scripts/$s.sh > /tmp/$s.py && python3 -m py_compile /tmp/$s.py && echo \"$s.py OK\"; done"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1258,"output":161,"cacheRead":116736,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":25,"totalTokens":118155,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993200524,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e7ff4178-aa56-4782-8590-26bfc4ff8ffd","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b4249d2155cb4dd480ce1d5d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"make-proxy.py OK\nrun-proxy.py OK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993206201},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both heredocs compile. Note: in the case of run-proxy.sh, there are two heredocs (the python for write_receipt and the main one), and awk merged the two — but did it compile without issues even when merged? In reality, awk captured both blocks sequentially into a single file. Even so, it compiled. Well, that's good enough. In the first place, the main one was being validated at the same time. In practice, let's verify them individually — if the merged contents have two top-level scripts concatenated, it could potentially hide errors. However, since it compiled without issues, each part is syntactically valid (concatenating valid top-level code results in valid code).\n\nNext, add tests/test_proxy_tooling.py.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now the repo test pins for the proxy tooling (mirroring claim 6.4's package-assertion style):\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_900d7b8159904e75838eeb70","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"\"\"\"Proxy tooling pins — the cheap, offline half of spec claim 4.1.\n\nMirrors the claim-6.4 shape (\"the tests suite's package assertions pass:\nsyntax-clean scripts, …\"): these tests grade scripts/make-proxy.sh and\nscripts/run-proxy.sh BEFORE the overnight serve, so a doctrine drift in the\nrunner is caught by the repo-tests gate rather than by a burned night.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport pathlib\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport unittest\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nMAKE = ROOT / \"scripts\" / \"make-proxy.sh\"\nRUN = ROOT / \"scripts\" / \"run-proxy.sh\"\n\n\nclass ProxyTooling(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        for path in (MAKE, RUN):\n            self.assertTrue(path.is_file(), f\"{path} missing\")\n        self.make = MAKE.read_text()\n        self.run = RUN.read_text()\n\n    def test_scripts_are_syntax_clean(self):\n        for path in (MAKE, RUN):\n            subprocess.run([\"bash\", \"-n\", str(path)], check=True)\n\n    def test_run_proxy_writes_the_claimed_receipt(self):\n        # Claim 4.1's receipt is graded by scripts/receipts-verify.py.\n        self.assertIn(\"results/receipts/proxy.json\", self.run)\n\n    def test_mmap_path_is_engaged(self):\n        # The claim is \"with the mmap path engaged\"; the runner pins the flag\n        # (a plain bool(int(getenv)) read — safe to export, spec F.9 noted).\n        self.assertIn(\"VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1\", self.run)\n        # …and asserts engagement from the serve log, not from hope.\n        self.assertIn(\"mmap_engaged\", self.run)\n\n    def test_first_light_mode_is_piecewise_not_eager(self):\n        # Ruling P10: the table path's own guard refuses plain-eager mode and\n        # full-graph capture under VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1; the sanctioned first-light\n        # mode is piecewise capture with the mmap op as a split boundary.\n        self.assertIn(\"PIECEWISE\", self.run)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"--enforce-eager\", self.run,\n                         \"the fork's check_cudagraph_safety guard raises on \"\n                         \"plain-eager mode under VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1\")\n\n    def test_checkpoint_contract(self):\n        # The vocabulary contract of spec.md \"proxy checkpoint\": same\n        # architecture identifier, 8 experts, block-FP8 [128, 128], and the\n        # shard naming the mmap path's discover_shards expects.\n        self.assertIn(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\", self.make)\n        self.assertIn(\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\", self.make)\n        self.assertIn(\"weight_block_size\", self.make)\n        self.assertIn(\"ngram_embedding.shard_\", self.make)\n        self.assertIn(\"ngram_embedding.weight_scale\", self.make)\n        self.assertRegex(self.make, r\"FN_PROXY_EXPERTS(:-\\S*)?-(\\S*)?8|:-8\")\n\n    def test_no_is_set_probe_exports(self):\n        # Spec F.9 (mirrored from host/fn-env.sh): never export a default the\n        # engine reads through an is-set probe — exporting the value it\n        # already has diverts the fp8 oracle into a hard raise.\n        for probe in (\"VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM\", \"VLLM_MOE_USE_DEEP_GEMM\",\n                      \"VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER\"):\n            for name, text in ((\"make-proxy.sh\", self.make),\n                               (\"run-proxy.sh\", self.run)):\n                self.assertNotIn(probe, text,\n                                 f\"is-set probe {probe} in {name}\")\n\n    def test_runtime_hub_downloads_forbidden(self):\n        # Spec F.6: the proxy serves from its own disk; tokenizer comes from\n        # the staged workload or is synthesized, never fetched.\n        self.assertIn(\"HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1\", self.run)\n        for text in (self.make, self.run):\n            self.assertNotIn(\"huggingface.co\", text)\n            self.assertNotIn(\"hf download\", text)\n\n    def test_failure_is_graded_never_skipped(self):\n        # Spec F.12: every failure path lands a receipt.\n        self.assertIn(\"fail\", self.run)\n        self.assertIn('\"step\": \"proxy\"', self.run.replace(\"'\", '\"'))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/tests/test_proxy_tooling.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":4130,"output":1253,"cacheRead":114048,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":154,"totalTokens":119431,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993206207,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b5496a44-ae59-42ef-b2b5-b59908efdb17","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_900d7b8159904e75838eeb70","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 3934 b