{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no torch on this host, but numpy exists. Let's make a minimal torch shim that mimics the API used by the generator, so we can smoke-test the generator's logic end-to-end (config shrinking, geometry, safetensors serialization, fallback writer, PLE writer). The shim only needs to be sufficient for the fallback path (the introspection path imports vllm and will fail gracefully → fallback, which is exactly what we want to test).\n\nAPIs used in the fallback path:\n- torch.randn(V,H,generator=gen)*0.02, torch.zeros(shape), torch.ones(x), torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n- t.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous().view(torch.int16).numpy().tobytes()\n- t.to(torch.float8_e4m3fn).contiguous().view(torch.uint8).numpy().tobytes()\n- t.to(torch.float32).contiguous().numpy().tobytes()\n- torch.device(\"meta\") (introspection path — fails at vllm import before this)\n- torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n\nWrite the shim on top of numpy: Tensor wrapper class. bfloat16 conversion: fake it — store as float32 but .view(int16) needs 2 bytes... implement bf16 as float32→bf16 uint16 conversion (truncate mantissa) ✓. float8_e4m3fn: implement a simple encoder (just zero-fill / clamp) — shim returns uint8 zero-fill (values are zero anyway). Also implement torch.device, Generator.\n\nAfter that, run the generator with MODELS pointed at a fake (empty) directory and OUT pointed at a temp directory, with the vllm import failing → fallback path. Then, parse the generated safetensors header with a real safetensors library? Might not be installed. Verify with my own parser (header json). That's enough.\n\nLet's proceed with this test.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"No torch here, but I can smoke-test the generator's fallback path with a numpy-backed torch shim:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c278d8ac30d549fd9d79439c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/proxytest && cat > /tmp/proxytest/torch.py <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\n\nclass dtype:\n    def __init__(self, name, itemsize): self.name, self.itemsize = name, itemsize\n    def __repr__(self): return f\"torch.{self.name}\"\n\nfloat32 = dtype(\"float32\", 4); bfloat16 = dtype(\"bfloat16\", 2)\nfloat8_e4m3fn = dtype(\"float8_e4m3fn\", 1); int16 = dtype(\"int16\", 2)\nuint8 = dtype(\"uint8\", 1)\n\nclass Generator:\n    def manual_seed(self, s): self.seed = s; self.rng = np.random.default_rng(s); return self\n\nclass Tensor:\n    def __init__(self, arr, dt=float32): self.arr = np.asarray(arr); self.dtype = dt\n    def to(self, dt):\n        if dt.name == \"bfloat16\":\n            u = (self.arr.astype(np.float32).view(np.uint32) >> 16).astype(np.uint16)\n            return Tensor(u, dt)\n        if dt.name == \"float8_e4m3fn\":\n            a = np.clip(self.arr.astype(np.float32), -448, 448)\n            return Tensor(np.zeros(a.shape, np.uint8), dt)  # zeros path is exact\n        if dt.name == \"float32\": return Tensor(self.arr.astype(np.float32), dt)\n        return Tensor(self.arr, dt)\n    def contiguous(self): return self\n    def view(self, dt):\n        if dt.name == \"int16\" and self.dtype.name == \"bfloat16\":\n            return Tensor(self.arr.view(np.int16), dt)\n        if dt.name == \"uint8\": return Tensor(self.arr.view(np.uint8), dt)\n        return Tensor(self.arr, dt)\n    def numpy(self): return self.arr\n    def __mul__(self, o): return Tensor(self.arr * o, self.dtype)\n    def __rmul__(self, o): return self.__mul__(o)\n    @property\n    def shape(self): return tuple(self.arr.shape)\n\ndef zeros(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.zeros(tuple(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\ndef ones(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.ones(tuple(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\ndef randn(*shape, generator=None):\n    rng = generator.rng if generator else np.random.default_rng()\n    return Tensor(rng.standard_normal(tuple(shape)).astype(np.float32))\ndef manual_seed(s): pass\nclass device:\n    def __init__(self, name): self.name = name\n    def __enter__(self): return self\n    def __exit__(self, *a): return False\nEOF\necho shim-ok"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2520,"output":1118,"cacheRead":136192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":417,"totalTokens":139830,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993907851,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3f2029e8-4c59-4059-95e6-0c8a3afc0a02","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c278d8ac30d549fd9d79439c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"shim-ok\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993932395}]}
