{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Wait — the shim's `ones(shape)` also accepts scalar shapes (H,) ✓; `torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape))` is a list ✓. `torch.zeros(shape)` inside `_fp8` — the curated linear uses `torch.zeros(shape)` with a tuple ✓. `torch.ones(H)` scalar int ✓ tuple(H) fails — with Tensor(np.ones(tuple(H))) when H is an int → tuple(2560) error! `np.ones(2560)` is OK but `tuple(2560)` is a TypeError. Fix the shim: normalizing shape: `tuple(shape) if isinstance(shape,(list,tuple)) else (int(shape),)`. Patch the shim, and also the `Tensor` created from `torch.zeros(shape)` in the introspection branch is similar.\n\nAlso, the generator script reads env vars and runs main; imports vllm (fails) → no problem; sys.path.insert(\"/opt/vllm/tests\") is harmless.\n\nRun: set OUT to /tmp/proxytest/out via a script? OUT is hardcoded as Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")... For local testing, either patch a copy of mp.py with sed to replace the OUT path, or use a bind-like trick to run it: easiest is to make a copy with OUT replaced. Also the MODELS path is /models → doesn't exist → template path ✓.\n"}}
