{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The main findings obtained from running the actual image:\n\n1. Introspection fails: `VllmConfig` validation — \"Cannot find any of ['activation_scheme'] in the model's quantization config.\" The fork's Fp8Config requires `activation_scheme` in the quantization_config (a DeepSeek-style block-fp8 config includes `\"activation_scheme\": \"dynamic\"`). The actual workload's quantization_config must contain it… but my shrink() is replacing the quantization_config wholesale and losing activation_scheme! Fix: when replacing, preserve the existing fields from the workload's quantization_config (merge: keep existing keys like activation_scheme, and override quant_method/weight_block_size, delete modules_to_not_convert). Also, my template should include \"activation_scheme\": \"dynamic\".\n\n2. `Fp8Config appears to consume modules_to_not_convert by literal membership` — my source probe's regex `re\\.(match|search|fullmatch)\\s*\\([^)]*ignored` didn't match. Let me actually check how the fork consumes it — I can grep the file from inside the container! Let me investigate directly.\n\n3. KeyError 'hidden_size' in curated_weights — the actual workload's config.json is huge (72 KB) — hidden_size might be under a nested text_config, or maybe the model uses a different field name?! config.json is 72 KB — it's a multimodal configuration (\"Model ... is treated as multimodal\"). Hmm! Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration is multimodal-capable (conditional generation!). The config fields might be nested. Let me look at the keys of the actual config.json.\n\nLet me investigate the actual config + fp8.py's ignore semantics."}}
