{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"now the actual structure is coming into view:\n\n1. **The config is nested**: text_config holds all the fields; top-level is multimodal (vision_config + language_model). Module prefixes have `model.language_model.` on them (not `model.layers`). embed = `model.language_model.embed_tokens`, lm_head is at top level.\n\n2. **`ple_layer_ids = [2]`** — PLE only exists in layer 2!! Not in every layer. My assumption of \"per-layer PLE\" was wrong for this model. The proxy should respect ple_layer_ids: shrink to fewer layers → keep ple_layer_ids within range (e.g., 8 layers → [2] is still valid ✓).\n\n3. `split_ngram_parts = 128` exists as a config field ✓; `ngram_vocab_size_base = 20000000`, heads 8 → total 160M, divisor 128. Proxy: shrink base to 512 → total 4096, split 128 → shard_size 32, 128 shards for the single PLE layer.\n\n4. `modules_to_not_convert` = literal module names, 943 entries ('lm_head', 'model.language_model.embed_tokens', ...) — i.e., membership semantics by literal prefix. My probe said membership ✓ consistent.\n\n5. quantization_config needs activation_scheme (dynamic) + weight_per_tensor/act_per_tensor fields — merge instead of replace.\n\n6. Weight names carry the `model.language_model.` prefix; the multimodal architecture builds the vision tower too — shrink vision or drop it? Can I set `language_model_only: true`? There's a config flag \"language_model_only\": False — if I set it to true the vision tower won't be built! That shrinks things dramatically. But does vLLM respect this? Probably the model class checks this. If it exists, set language_model_only=true in the proxy. Hmm, risk: unknown semantics. In fact, the log showed \"Model ... is treated as multimodal but has no registered multimodal processor; running in text-only mode\" — vLLM is already demoting to text-only. Keep the vision config but it will still be built (vision tower weights will be needed