{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Progress: VllmConfig now validates (no more activation_scheme errors — ModelConfig/VllmConfig construction succeeded, config was parsed, IR ops, model runner logs). Introspection failed due to API details: `ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls()` requires `model_config` argument: `resolve_model_cls(model_config, architectures?)`. Signature in this vLLM: `ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(model_config, architectures=None)`? Fix: pass model_config=mc: `cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc)[0]`? Returns a tuple (model_cls, arch). Let's verify the actual signature inside the container.\n\nAnother critical observation: \"discover_shards found ZERO PLE shard tensors\" — wait, did the curated fallback write shards with the new prefix? No, wait — the order: main() first writes the weights (curated fallback — since introspection failed, KeyError on hidden_size? No, curated is now tc-compatible ✓ executed), then write_ple_shards with prefix model.language_model... then validate → zero shards found! Why? _SHARD_RE is `layers\\.(\\d+)\\.ple\\.ple_embedding\\.ngram_embedding\\.shard_(\\d+)\\.weight$` — my name: `model.language_model.layers.2.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_00000.weight` — search should match (unanchored). Unless the shard write itself failed, or the fallback writer crashed before writing shards? The exit message was from validate_ple → which means shards were written... but discover found zero. Hmm — prefix! In the actual model, the PLE module prefix may not contain `.ple.` — the actual checkpoint name is... `ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding` is what _SHARD_RE expects. Wait, does the actual weight name include a `model.language_model.` prefix? The actual modules_to_not_convert entries indicate `model.language_model.layers...`. So checkpoint tensors are probably named `model.language_model.layers.2.ple...` — regex unanchored → matches.\n\nSo why zero? discover_shards globs `os.path.join(model_path, \"*.safetensors\")` — flat ✓ my files are flat ✓. Let's debug directly inside the container: run discover_shards against the checkpoint and print what's found. The actual checkpoint directory is at ~/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint.\n\nAlso note: did the curated fallback write the weights? KeyError is gone. The files exist? Let's look at the directory. Also confirm prefix handling in the validate step. Let's debug inside the container."}}
