el ✓; but did the curated writer skip the ignore check? modules_to_not_convert is not installed → quantize_linears=True → fp8-ify full-attn q/k/v/o + scales. But other modules (hyperconnection, linear attn, indexer...) are also quantized (quantize-all) but not provided → NaN risk for uninitialized fp8. RESIDUAL RISK is already noted. If introspection starts working, this path becomes unused. Prioritize the introspection fix.\n\nAlso, the rope_parameters warning is harmless.\n\nUpdate try_fork_introspection with distributed initialization.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Introspection now needs the TP group initialized. Add a distributed-init attempt (gloo, world 1):\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_364fd29550f440d897b3d87f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\nold = '''        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):'''\nnew = '''        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        # The model's parallel layers assert an initialized TP group even at\n        # world size 1; give them a gloo one on the loopback.\n        try:\n            from vllm.distributed import (init_distributed_environment,\n                                          initialize_model_parallel)\n            init_distributed_environment(\n                world_size=1, rank=0, local_rank=0,\n                distributed_init_method=\"tcp://127.0.0.1:29511\",\n                backend=\"gloo\")\n            initialize_model_parallel(1, 1)\n        except Exception as e:\n            note(f\"distributed bootstrap for introspection: {e!r}\")\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):'''\nassert src.count(old) == 1\nopen(p, 'w').write(src.replace(old, new))\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && echo BASH-OK && time bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -12","timeout":1200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2079,"output":1010,"cacheRead":187392,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":597,"totalTokens":190481,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787995042674,"responseId":"chatcmpl-5a2c641c-d015-4e6c-a1f5-5c6bc1f474a0","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_364fd29550f440d897b3d87f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok\nBASH-OK\nINFO 08-29 09:18:11 [kernel.py:369] Final IR op priority after setting platform defaults: IrOpPriorityConfig(rms_norm=['native'], fused_add_rms_norm=['native'])\nWARNING 08-29 09:18:11 [vllm.py:638] Model Runner V2 requires Triton; using the V1 model runner instead.\nINFO 08-29 09:18:11 [compilation.py:329] Enabled custom fusions: norm_quant, act_quant\nINFO 08-29 09:18:11 [parallel_state.py:1638] world_size=1 rank=0 local_rank=0 distributed_init_method=tcp://127.0.0.1:29511 backend=gloo\nmake-proxy: distributed bootstrap for introspection: AssertionError(\"Current vLLM config is not set. This typically means get_current_vllm_config() was called outside of a set_current_vllm_config() context, or a CustomOp was instantiated at module import time or model forward time when config is not set. For tests that directly test custom ops/modules, use the 'default_vllm_config' pytest fixture from tests/conftest.py.\")\nmake-proxy: fork model introspection unavailable (AssertionError: tensor model parallel group is not initialized); using the curated fallback naming with its typed residual risks\nmake-proxy: Fp8Config appears to consume modules_to_not_convert by literal membership; skipping the ignore-list (quantize-all mode)\nmake-proxy: RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed — quantize-all mode; any quantized Linear whose name the fallback write