{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`init_distributed_environment` requires the current vllm config to be set — need to move it inside the `set_current_vllm_config(vc)` context. Also, the error message mentions the fork's own testing scaffolding: \"use the 'default_vllm_config' pytest fixture in tests/conftest.py\" — a better reuse approach: use the fork's tests/conftest fixture logic... A pytest fixture can't be called directly, but maybe the function it wraps can. For now, just move init inside the context.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_22afd8a91ff44d0b9e75e354","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\nold = '''        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        # The model's parallel layers assert an initialized TP group even at\n        # world size 1; give them a gloo one on the loopback.\n        try:\n            from vllm.distributed import (init_distributed_environment,\n                                          initialize_model_parallel)\n            init_distributed_environment(\n                world_size=1, rank=0, local_rank=0,\n                distributed_init_method=\"tcp://127.0.0.1:29511\",\n                backend=\"gloo\")\n            initialize_model_parallel(1, 1)\n        except Exception as e:\n            note(f\"distributed bootstrap for introspection: {e!r}\")\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures, mc)[0]'''\nnew = '''        mc = ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))\n        vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\n        with set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n            # The model's parallel layers assert an initialized TP group even\n            # at world size 1; give them a gloo one on the loopback. The init\n            # itself needs the config context (it reads the current config).\n            try:\n                from vllm.distributed import (init_distributed_environment,\n                                              initialize_model_parallel)\n                init_distributed_environment(\n                    world_size=1, rank=0, local_rank=0,\n                    distributed_init_method=\"tcp://127.0.0.1:29511\",\n                    backend=\"gloo\")\n                initialize_model_parallel(1, 1)\n            except Exception as e:\n                note(f\"distributed bootstrap for introspection: {e!r}\")\n            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures, mc)[0]'''\nassert src.count(old) == 1\nopen(p, 'w').write(src.replace(old, new))\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && time bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -12","timeout":1200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1574,"output":694,"cacheRead":189440,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":111,"totalTokens":191708,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787995097505,"responseId":"chatcmpl-84ec5c7b-b5b7-4bf4-a204-7be17f412116","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_22afd8a91ff44d0b9e75e354","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok\nINFO 08-29 09:19:00 [parallel_state.py:1982] rank 0 in world size 1 is assigned as DP rank 0, PP rank 0, PCP rank 0, TP rank 0, EP rank 0, EPLB rank N/A\nINFO 08-29 09:19:00 [__init__.py:695] Selected TritonFp8BlockScaledMMKernel for Fp8LinearMethod\nINFO 08-29 09:19:00 [rocm.py:806] Using Torch SDPA backend for ViT model.\nWARNING 08-29 09:19:00 [activation.py:808] [ROCm] PyTorch's native GELU with tanh approximation is unstable. Falling back to GELU(approximate='none').\nINFO 08-29 09:19:00 [mm_encoder_attention.py:375] Using AttentionBackendEnum.