{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Critical finding: `if (self.layer_idx + 1) in ple_layer_ids` — **ple_layer_ids uses 1-based numbering** (layer_idx+1 is in the list)! The actual config has ple_layer_ids=[2] → the module for layer_idx 1 (0-based) gets the PLE. In other words, the layer where PLE actually exists = id−1 = layer 1 (0-based). My shards were being written to layer 2 → the serve failed at layer 1, where no shards exist.\n\nTherefore, in the proxy config, keeping ple_layer_ids=[2] means the PLE module sits at 0-based layer 1. My writer must write shards to layer 1 (i.e., ple_ids value − 1). Also validate_ple's comparison — discover found layer 2 (my file), but the fork requires layer 1. Fix: in write_ple_shards and the manifest, ple_layers = [i-1 for i in tc's ple_layer_ids]. And my shrink's `ple_ids = [i for i in tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\", ...) if i < LAYERS]` — this semantics is 1-based: the condition should be i <= LAYERS (module exists when layer_idx+1 == i → layer_idx = i-1 < LAYERS → i <= LAYERS).\n\nAlso nvidia/model.py:194-197: mapping of abs_id→idx. OK.\n\nFix make-proxy:\n- shrink: `ple_ids = [i for i in tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\", []) if 1 <= i <= LAYERS]`, default when the field doesn't exist: all layers have PLE? In the template case, keep [2] (module at layer 1) ✓ template has 8 layers. If the result is empty → [LAYERS] (module at the last layer, 1-based).\n- write_ple_shards: `ple_layers = [i - 1 for i in tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\", range(1, L+1))]`.\n- manifest's ple_layers: store the 0-based list (or both).\n- validate_ple: compare against the 0-based expected values.\n\nNote the 1-based handling for the case when the field is missing: layers are 1..L.\n\nLet's apply the edits."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"`ple_layer_ids` is **1-indexed** (`(layer_idx + 1) in ple_layer_ids`) — so `[2]` means 0-indexed layer 1. Fix the builder:\n\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9d9ebe7864db479280fb24c0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && podman rm -f flashnext-proxy-debug >/dev/null 2>&1; python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\n\ndef rep(old, new, label):\n    global src\n    assert src.count(old) == 1, f\"BAD: {label}\"\n    src = src.replace(old, new)\n    print(\"ok:\", label)\n\n# shrink: ple_layer_ids is 1-INDEXED ((layer_idx + 1) in ple_layer_ids)\nrep('''    # PLE layers survive the layer shrink; the mmap claim needs at least one.\n    ple_ids = [i for i in tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\", range(LAYERS))\n               if i < LAYERS]\n    if not ple_ids:\n        ple_ids = [LAYERS - 1]\n    set_(\"ple_layer_ids\", ple_ids)''',\n'''    # PLE layers survive the layer shrink; the mmap claim needs at least one.\n    # The fork reads them 1-INDEXED: a PLE module lives on layer_idx when\n    # (layer_idx + 1) is in ple_layer_ids (amd/model.py:193-197).\n    ple_ids = [i for i in tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\", range(1, LAYERS + 1))\n               if 1 <= i <= LAYERS]\n    if not ple_ids:\n        ple_ids = [LAYERS]\n    set_(\"ple_layer_ids\", ple_ids)''', \"shrink 1-indexed\")\n\nrep('''    ple_layers = tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\") or range(int(tc[\"num_hidden_layers\"]))\n    files = 0\n    scale = _f32(torch.ones(1))\n    main = {}\n    for layer in ple_layers:''',\n'''    # ple_layer_ids is 1-indexed in the fork; shards live on layer_idx = id-1.\n    ple_ids = tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\") or range(\n        1, int(tc[\"num_hidden_layers\"]) + 1)\n    files = 0\n    scale = _f32(torch.ones(1))\n    main = {}\n    for layer in (i - 1 for i in ple_ids):''', \"ple writer 0-indexed\")\n\nrep('''    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ple_layers\"] = list(\n        text_cfg(cfg).get(\"ple_layer_ids\", range(LAYERS)))''',\n'''    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ple_layers_1indexed\"] = list(\n        text_cfg(cfg).get(\"ple_layer_ids\", range(1, LAYERS + 1)))''', \"manifest 1-indexed\")\n\nrep('''    ple_layers = text_cfg(cfg).get(\"ple_layer_ids\")\n    bad = {}''',\n'''    ple_ids = text_cfg(cfg).get(\"ple_layer_ids\")\n    expected_layers = sorted(i - 1 for i in ple_ids) if ple_ids else None\n    bad = {}''', \"validate expected\")\n\nrep('''    if ple_layers is not None and sorted(per_layer) != sorted(ple_layers):\n        die(f\"discover_shards found layers {sorted(per_layer)} but the config \"\n            f\"declares ple_layer_ids {sorted(ple_layers)}\")''',\n'''    if expected_layers is not None and sorted(per_layer) != expected_layers:\n        die(f\"discover_shards found layers {sorted(per_layer)} but the config \"\n            f\"declares PLE modules on 0-indexed layers {expected_layers} \"\n            f\"(ple_layer_ids {sorted(ple_ids)} are 1-indexed)\")''', \"validate compare\")\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(src)\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && echo BASH-OK && bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -3 && rm -f results/receipts/proxy.json","timeout":600}}}}
