{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have the exact formula from the fork source:\n\n- `ngram_heads = (ngram_size - 1) * heads_per_ngram` = (3-1)*8 = **16**\n- `embedding_dim` = ple_embed_dim = 2560; `head_dim = embedding_dim // ngram_heads` = 2560/16 = **160** ✓ (the row width of the shard!)\n- Per-head vocab size: `_nth_prime_after(ngram_vocab_size_base - 1, global_head + 1)` — a prime number per head! The size is the (global_head+1)-th prime greater than or equal to base. The total row count = sum of 16 per-head sizes (each ≈ base), padded to the divisor.\n- padded_vocab_size = ceil(sum/divisor)*divisor.\n- split_ngram_parts from config ✓.\n\nTherefore the row count is not base//heads — each of the 16 heads has a prime-number size starting from base (20M → each prime ≈ 20M; total 320M rows × 160 B = 51.2 GB ✓ — this matches the 51.2B parameter count!).\n\nAbout the proxy: base shrunk to 512 → per-head size = nth_prime_after(511, k) ≈ 512..600 (the 16th prime after 511). Total ≈ 16×~530 ≈ 8500 → padded to divisor 128 → ~8576 rows. split=2 → shard row count = 4288. Rows × 160 B ≈ 1.4 MB. No problem.\n\nMy writer must accurately reflect this: implement `_nth_prime_after` (simple trial division — the numbers are small for the proxy), ngram_heads=(ngram_size-1)*heads, head_dim=ple_embed_dim//ngram_heads, sizes/offsets per head, sum → padded → shard_size=ceil(padded/split)…\n\nWait — note: is padded_vocab_size the total row count of the table used for the shard mapping? _attach_table: expected shard count and shard_size computed from org_vocab_size and split_ngram_parts. Which \"org\" — probably padded_vocab_size (passed to MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, head_dim)). shard_size = ceil(padded/split); expected shard count = ceil(padded/shard_size) = split (when divisible). Rows per shard: the last shard may have fewer rows? _attach_table requires the per-shard row count recorded in the header… the loader's mapping `checkpoint_start = shard_index * shard_size` — is shard i rows = min(shard_size, padded - i*shard_size)? If padded % split != 0, the last shard is smaller. The shard row counts recorded in discover must match what _attach_table expects. Let's read ple_mmap's _attach_table to reflect it exactly.\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"The fork's exact table math is now visible (per-head prime sizes, `head_dim = ple_embed_dim // ((ngram_size-1)*heads)`). Read `_attach_table` to mirror the shard mapping exactly:\n\n"}}
