{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have all the information I need:\n\n**Shard placement calculation** (from `_attach_table`):\n- `vocab = embedding.org_vocab_size` (probably padded_vocab_size)\n- `shard_size = ceil(vocab / split)`\n- `num_expected_shards = min(split, ceil(vocab / shard_size))`\n- Shard i's row count = `min(shard_size, vocab - i*shard_size)` (the last shard could be smaller)\n\n**Table geometry** (from `Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.__init__`):\n- ngram_heads = (ngram_size - 1) * heads_per_ngram\n- head_dim = ple_embed_dim // ngram_heads (embedding_dim = ple_embed_dim... no wait, is the `embedding_dim` passed to init = ple_embed_dim? In the error, head_dim was 160 = 2560/16 ✓ so embedding_dim=2560=ple_embed_dim ✓)\n- Per-head size: prime = _nth_prime_after(base-1, global_head+1), where global_head = ple_dense_layer_id*ngram_heads + local_head. ple_dense_layer_id — the index of the PLE layer among PLE layers? \"ple_dense_layer_id\" — is it probably the index within the ple layers (0 for the first PLE layer), or is it the absolute layer ID? From the argument name `ple_dense_layer_id`... at model.py:193-197: `if (self.layer_idx + 1) in ple_layer_ids: ple_layer_ids_sorted...; abs_id: idx` — mapping abs_id → idx. Probably what gets passed as ple_dense_layer_id is idx (the dense index in the sorted list). So for our single PLE layer, ple_dense_layer_id=0.\n- offset is cumulative; padded to divisor.\n\nIn my proxy: ngram_size=3 (from config), heads_per_ngram=8 → ngram_heads=16; base=512; divisor=128; split=2; ple_dense_layer_id=0.\n\nPer-head size: _nth_prime_after(511, k) (k=1..16): primes after 511: 521? 512.. let's stop doing the hand calculation; I'll implement the same function in the generator (mirror of trial division).\n\nTotal ≈ 16 × approx 540 ≈ 8640 → padded to a multiple of 128 → 8704? Whatever; the code will compute it.\n\nRows per shard: shard_size = ceil(vocab/2); shard 0 has shard_size rows, shard 1 has vocab - shard_size rows.\n\nRow width = head_dim = 160 fp8 bytes.\n\nNext, update make-proxy's generator:\n1. `ngram_row_bytes(cfg)` → ple_embed_dim // ((ngram_size-1)*heads_per_ngram), fallback to the previous heuristic.\n2. Replace `ngram_geometry` with a full mirror: implement _nth_prime_after + per-head sizes + padded + shard row list. Return rows_per_shard as a list [rows_shard0, rows_shard1...].\n3. write_ple_shards writes rows[i] per shard index.\n4. Update validate_ple accordingly (validate by per-shard row count).\n\nNote: ple_dense_layer_id — if the proxy has multiple PLE layers, the global_head offset changes per PLE layer idx. Currently it's single PLE layer (idx 0) — support for multiple: idx = enumerate(sorted ple ids). I'll implement it generally.\n\nAlso `org_vocab_size` = padded_vocab_size? MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, head_dim) — _attach uses embedding.org_vocab_size — probably set from the constructor argument. ✓ = padded.\n\nAlright, let me rewrite the geometry part of make-proxy.sh."}}
