{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"\n[{\"newText\": \"    set_(\\\"num_hidden_layers\\\", LAYERS)\\n    # All layers stay linear_attention in the proxy: the fork's QSA\\n    # full-attention path requires FlashAttention\\n    # (amd/qsa.py: is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available) and the container's\\n    # pinned wheel set ships no flash-attn — a full_attention layer dies at\\n    # construction with NotImplementedError. That is a typed finding for the\\n    # pair first-light lane; the proxy's claim (the admitted block-FP8 MoE\\n    # kernel and the mmap table path) is attention-agnostic.\\n    if any(t == \\\"full_attention\\\" for t in tc.get(\\\"layer_types\\\", [])):\\n        note(\\\"workload pattern carries full_attention layers; the proxy \\\"\\n             \\\"drops them (no flash-attn in the pinned wheel set) — typed \\\"\\n             \\\"blocker for the pair first-light lane, not the proxy\\\")\\n    set_(\\\"layer_types\\\", [\\\"linear_attention\\\"] * LAYERS)\", \"oldText\": \"    set_(\\\"num_hidden_layers\\\", LAYERS)\\n    interval = int(tc.get(\\\"full_attention_interval\\\", 4))\\n    pattern = [\\\"linear_attention\\\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\\\"full_attention\\\"]\\n    set_(\\\"layer_types\\\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\"}]\n\n"}}
