{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available()` is False — flash-attn's varlen function isn't available in this image (ROCm without flash-attn). So any configuration with full attention layers fails to serve in this container. The actual pair-first-light task hits this too — that's a separate lane's problem (probably needs an upstream issue / fork fix, or aiter). Doesn't block my deliverable: the proxy can fulfill its purpose (the accepted MoE + mmap table) even with linear_attention-only layers.\n\nJudgment: shrink() forces layer_types. For the proxy, all layers should be linear_attention, but… hmm, wait, P10/claim 4.1 doesn't require full attention. However — there's one thing to consider: piecewise cudagraph capture + mmap's splitting op: those don't depend on attention type ✓.\n\nBut — if all layers are linear, does anything else demand full attention? The MTP sub-config has layer_types full_attention but MTP isn't constructed (no spec decoding) ✓.\n\nChange shrink(): pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * LAYERS (all linear), with a comment noting the reason (QSA requires FlashAttention, but the container's wheel set doesn't provide it — this is a typed campaign-level finding). Actually, to make this finding visible to the campaign, the comment + a note() warning + a \"full_attention_dropped\" field in the manifest.\n\nHmm wait — actually let me re-check `is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available` — maybe it's gated on an import that requires GPU init… the serve had the GPU. Probably needs a package like `flash_attn_2_cuda` / aotriton. The container doesn't have flash-attn (the container file doesn't install it). So indeed not available.\n\nAlternative: keep one full_attention layer and catch it… no, construction raises. Make it linear-only.\n\nUpdate shrink():\n```python\n    # All layers stay linear_attention in the proxy: the fork's QSA\n    # full-attention path requires FlashAttention\n    # (amd/qsa.py:is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available), and the container's\n    # pinned wheel set ships no flash-attn — a full_attention layer dies at\n    # construction. Typed finding for the pair first-light lane; the proxy's\n    # claim (admitted MoE kernel + mmap table) is attention-agnostic.\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [\"linear_attention\"] * LAYERS)\n```\nKeep full_attention_interval as is.\n\nAdditionally, add a note to the manifest. Then rebuild + re-run serve. Expected next blocker: weights (the curated quantize-all fallback)… anyway, let's try it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"`is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available()` is false — the pinned wheelset doesn't include flash-attn, so full-attention layers can't be built in this container (this is a type-determined finding in the pair-light lane). Since the proxy's purpose doesn't depend on attention, all proxy layers will be kept as `linear_attention`:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dfde0d474be443dbad1d52a1","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    # All layers stay linear_attention in the proxy: the fork's QSA\n    # full-attention path requires FlashAttention\n    # (amd/qsa.py: is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available) and the container's\n    # pinned wheel set ships no flash-attn — a full_attention layer dies at\n    # construction with NotImplementedError. That is a typed finding for the\n    # pair first-light lane; the proxy's claim (the admitted block-FP8 MoE\n    # kernel and the mmap table path) is attention-agnostic.\n    if any(t == \"full_attention\" for t in tc.get(\"layer_types\", [])):\n        note(\"workload pattern carries full_attention layers; the proxy \"\n             \"drops them (no flash-attn in the pinned wheel set) — typed \"\n             \"blocker for the pair first-light lane, not the proxy\")\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [\"linear_attention\"] * LAYERS)","oldText":"    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    interval = int(tc.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4))\n    pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])"}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1254,"output":1033,"cacheRead":219648,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":573,"totalTokens":221935,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787996082961,"responseId":"chatcmpl-47874377-3da5-4aec-bf07-280bd924b9d4","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dfde0d474be443dbad1d52a1","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 174     if \"language_model_only\" in cfg:\n 175         cfg[\"language_model_only\"] = True  # the proxy has no vision bytes\n 176         edits[\"language_model_only\"] = [False, True]\n 177     set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n-178     interval = int(tc.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4))\n-179     pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n-180     set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\n+178     # All layers stay linear_attention in the proxy: the fork's QSA\n+179     # full-attention path requires FlashAttention\n+180     # (amd/qsa.py: is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available) and the container's\n+181     # pinned wheel set ships no flash-attn — a full_attention layer dies at\n+182     # construction with NotImplementedError. That is a typed finding for the\n+183     # pair first-light lane; the proxy's claim (the admitted block-FP8 MoE\n+184