{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Also — the curated fallback writer only writes attention tensors for full_attention layers; now there are none at all, so that's fine.\n\nBut wait — the curated fallback's quantize-all mode: fp8-quantized Linears that the writer doesn't provide (linear-attn internals: in_proj_qkvz, conv1d, A_log, dt_bias, norm, out_proj, plus hyperconnection modules, indexer (not built without full attn)) → uninitialized fp8 → NaN risk → possibility of \"finite logits\" failing. Now is the time to prioritize actually making the ignore list work. I observed earlier: \"Fp8Config seems to consume modules_to_not_convert via literal membership\". The fork's `_get_ple_embedding_quant_method` was calling `is_layer_skipped(prefix, ignored_layers, packed_modules_mapping, match_mode=quant_config.ignored_layers_match_mode)` — so Fp8Config has `ignored_layers_match_mode`! There might be regex/match modes. Let me check the fork's Fp8Config and is_layer_skipped to understand the semantics exactly — that will determine how the fallback writer can safely install ignores even without introspection."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Now check the fork's actual ignore semantics (`is_layer_skipped` + `ignored_layers_match_mode`) to settle the fallback safety question:\n\n"}}
