e_linear(base...), the checkpoint name will be \"language_model.model.layers.0.mlp.shared_expert.gate_up_proj.weight\" — does the loader accept the fused gate_up_proj name from the checkpoint? vLLM's MergedColumnParallel weight_loader expects checkpoint shards gate_proj/up_proj separately via stacked mapping... For shared_expert, vLLM's qwen3_next model handles \"shared_expert.gate_up_proj\" via stacked_params_mapping with entries (\"gate_up_proj\", \"gate_proj\", 0)/(\"gate_up_proj\",\"up_proj\",1) — model-level stacked_params_mapping should contain it. My `fused` dict was built from model.stacked_params_mapping — shared_expert's mapping is probably there: suffix \"gate_up_proj\"?? But the param name ends in \".mlp.shared_expert.gate_up_proj\" — base.endswith(vllm_sfx) for vllm_sfx \"gate_up_proj\" ✓ should have matched! Unless the mapping uses full suffix \".shared_expert.gate_up_proj\" or similar... base = \"language_model.model.layers.0.mlp.shared_expert.gate_up_proj\"; if stacked entry's vllm_sfx = \"gate_up_proj\", then endswith ✓ → split into gate_proj/up_proj HF names → write_linear(f\"{stem}gate_proj\") with stem = base minus suffix = \"...shared_expert.\" → names \"...shared_expert.gate_proj\"/\"up_proj\" ✓. But the dump shows \"shared_expert.gate_up_proj.weight.weight\" → didn't match. Why? Maybe stacked_params_mapping entries are (\"gate_up_proj\", \".mlp.shared_expert.gate_proj\"...)... hmm, HF suffixes sometimes include the dot: entries look like (param_name=\"gate_up_proj\", weight_name=\"gate_proj\", shard_id=0) — matching in vLLM's load: `if weight_name in name` replacement. Not sure of the exact format. Simplest robust fix: in the writer's fallback, write with the checkpoint name = vLLM param name (base), letting the loader resolve it: vLLM's AutoWeightsLoader + stacked mapping handles checkpoint names equal to the vllm fused name (loading gate_up_proj directly works: weight_loader handles the full tensor). Yes — stacked mapping exists for HF-split checkpoints, but loading a pre-fused tensor under the fused name works too (param's weight_loader gets the full tensor... hmm, MergedColumnParallelParameter.weight_loader expects a shard_id when loading shards; loading the full fused tensor under the fused name: AutoWeightsLoader calls param's weight_loader(loaded) with no shard_id → for MergedColumnParallelParameter → loads into full shape ✓ I think it works).\n\nOK, so the minimal fix: in the introspection writer's fallback `write_linear(base, shape)` not name; skip ngram_embedding params; also expert fused w13/w2 handled. Additionally: `shared_expert_gate.weight.weight` — \"mlp.shared_expert_gate\" router for shared expert → fix base ✓.\n\nAlso `ngram_embedding.weight.weight` skip rule: names containing \".ngram_embedding.\" under ple — skip all (weight is covered by shards, scale by the scale file). But key_proj/value_proj must be kept (with base fix).\n\nAlso buffers: layer_multipliers, positions_buffer — named_parameters excludes buffers ✓ (no A_log... no wait A_log is there — in Mamba A_log is a parameter ✓; layer_multipliers is a persistent buffer — excluded from named_parameters — the loader: does the model need it? It's registered as a buffer with init computed in __init__ ✓ not from checkpoint).\n\nFixes to apply to the introspection writer:\n1. Fallback 2D: `write_linear(base, shape)`.\n2. Skip params matching `.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.` (mmap covers it).\n3. Also `if \"scale\" in name: continue` — keep (scales derive from the weight's handling; expert scales are written via write_linear).\n\nThen rebuild + rerun. The 300-entry ignore from introspection: prefixes like \"language_model.model.embed_tokens\" — Fp8Config's exact match compares against module prefix — the loader's module prefix for embed is \"language_model.model.embed_tokens\" ✓ consistent namespace ✓.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Bug found: my introspection writer double-appended `.weight`, and it must skip the PLE ngram embedding params (the mmap shards replace them). Fixing:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4a417885e06b4c7981ab6bc6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\n\ndef rep(old, new, label):\n    global src\n    assert src.count(old) == 1, f\"BAD: {label}\"\n    src = src.replace(old, new)\n    print(\"ok:\", label)\n\nrep('''        for name, shape in params:\n            if \"scale\" in name:\n                continue  # block scales ride beside their weights below\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and len(shape) == 2:''',\n'''        for name, shape in params:\n            if \"scale\" in name:\n                continue  # block scales ride beside their weights below\n            if \".ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.\" in name:\n                # Under VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 this module is a MmapNgramEmbedding\n                # with no resident weight: the shard files and the\n                # weight_scale file are the checkpoint face of this table.\n                continue\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and len(shape) == 2:''',\n\"skip ngram params\")\n\nrep('''                    continue\n                write_linear(name, shape)\n                continue''',\n'''                    continue\n                write_linear(base, shape)\n                continue''',\n\"base not name\")\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(src)\nprint(\"DONE\")\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -2 && python3 -c \"\nimport json, struct, pathlib\nf = pathlib.Path.home()/'.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint/model-00001-of-00001.safetensors'\nn = struct.unpack('<Q', open(f,'rb').read(8))[0]\nh = json.loads(open(f,'rb').read()[8:8+n])\nbad = [x for x in h if '.weight.weight' in x or 'ngram_embedding' in x]\nprint(len(h), 'tensors; bad:', bad[:5])\nexp = [x for x in h if 'experts.3.' in x]\nprint('expert sample:', sorted(exp)[:4])\n\"","timeout":600}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":4565,"output":2392,"cacheRead":227328,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1796,"totalTokens":234285,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787996323324,"responseId":"chatcmpl-aee71d9c-8aff-4704-ad6b-406edffd6ebf","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4a417885e06b4c7981ab6bc6","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok: skip ngram params\nok: base not name\nDONE\nmake-proxy: checkpoint ready at /home/tom/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint: 4 safetensors files\nmake-proxy: next: scripts/run-proxy.sh\n496 tensors; bad: []\nexpert sample: []\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787996415928}]}
