{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"In the new vLLM modular MoE, expert parameters are placed under `mlp.experts.routed_experts.w13_weight` (with `.routed_experts.` inserted), and my regex `r\"^(.*\\.mlp\\.experts)(?:\\.(\\d+))?\\.(w13|w2)_weight$\"` didn't match (it expects w13 to come right after experts or experts.{idx}). Fix the regex to allow any intermediate segment: `r\"^(.*\\.mlp\\.experts(?:\\.\\w+)?)\\.(w13|w2)_weight$\"`… Note: for the per-expert index case (`experts.0.w13_weight`), the current regex handles it, and for the batched case `experts.routed_experts.w13_weight` → stem is \"…mlp.experts.routed_experts\" → the per-expert HF name is stem + f\".{e}.gate_proj\" → becomes \"…mlp.experts.routed_experts.3.gate_proj\" — wrong; HF name is `mlp.experts.3.gate_proj`. So the per-expert name should be constructed as `{experts_stem}.{e}.gate_proj`, with experts_stem = path up to \".mlp.experts\". Reconstruct: match on `(.*\\.mlp\\.experts)(.*)\\.(w13|w2)_weight$`, and use group1 for the per-expert name.\n\nAlso, there's no scale tensor at all — the expert scale parameters are probably named `w13_weight_scale_inv` → they contain \"scale\" → skipped in my loop ✓ but they need to be written per-expert: `experts.{e}.gate_proj.weight_scale_inv`. Add this to the mex expansion (write_linear for experts already writes scale_inv via weight_scale_inv ✓). But wait — the reason the `sc` sample didn't show any scales is because the experts weren't expanded. After the fix, the scales should appear.\n\nFurthermore — batched w13_weight shape: (E, 2M, H)? My expansion writes (M, H) per-expert ✓. What about w13_weight_scale_inv (E, 2*cm, ck)? Write per-expert (cm, ck) for gate/up ✓ handled with write_linear's scale_inv_shape.\n\nFix the regex + stem logic.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The modular MoE nests experts under `mlp.experts.routed_experts.w13_weight` — my regex missed it. Fix the expansion:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02d49520cecf426c8986ed68","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\n\ndef rep(old, new, label):\n    global src\n    assert src.count(old) == 1, f\"BAD: {label}\"\n    src = src.replace(old, new)\n    print(\"ok:\", label)\n\nrep('''                # Batched or fused expert tensors: back to per-expert HF names.\n                mex = re.match(r\"^(.*\\\\.mlp\\\\.experts)(?:\\\\.(\\\\d+))?\\\\.\"\n                               r\"(w13|w2)_weight$\", name)\n                if mex:\n                    stem, eidx, w = mex.groups()\n                    es = [int(eidx)] if eidx is not None else range(E)\n                    for e in es:\n                        if w == \"w13\":\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.gate_proj\", (M, H))\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.up_proj\", (M, H))\n                        else:\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.down_proj\", (H, M))\n                    continue''',\n'''                # Batched or fused expert tensors: back to per-expert HF\n                # names. Modular MoE nests the batched tensors one level\n                deeper (mlp.experts.routed_experts.w13_weight); the per-\n                expert HF names hang off mlp.experts either way.\n                mex = re.match(r\"^(.*\\\\.mlp\\\\.experts)(?:\\\\.\\\\w+)?\\\\.\"\n                               r\"(?:(\\\\d+)\\\\.)?(w13|w2)_weight$\", name)\n                if mex:\n                    experts_stem, eidx, w = mex.groups()\n                    es = [int(eidx)] if eidx is not None else range(E)\n                    for e in es:\n                        if w == \"w13\":\n                            write_linear(f\"{experts_stem}.{e}.gate_proj\",\n                                         (M, H))\n                            write_linear(f\"{experts_stem}.{e}.up_proj\", (M, H))\n                        else:\n                            write_linear(f\"{experts_stem}.{e}.down_proj\",\n                                         (H, M))\n                    continue''',\n\"expert regex\")\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(src)\nprint(\"DONE\")\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -2 && python3 -c \"\nimport json, struct, pathlib\nf = pathlib.Path.home()/'.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint/model-00001-of-00001.safetensors'\nn = struct.unpack('<Q', open(f,'rb').read(8))[0]\nh = json.loads(open(f,'rb').read()[8:8+n])\nexp = sorted(x for x in h if 'layers.0.mlp.experts.3' in x)\nprint('expert-3 tensors:', exp)\nw = h[exp[0]]\nprint('sample:', w['dtype'], w['shape'])\n\"","timeout":600}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1376,"output":1301,"cacheRead":233472,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":508,"totalTokens":236149,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787996426705,"responseId":"chatcmpl-5938ec8b-5e84-4690-96bd-6f477a98f0f2","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02d49520cecf426c8986ed68","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok: expert regex\nDONE\n                                                        ^^^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 4, in <module>\n    n = struct.unpack('<Q', open(f,'rb').read(8))[0]\n                            ~~~~^^^^^^^^\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/home/tom/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint/model-00001-of-00001.safetensors'\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1787996457504}]}
