{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"\"There is no module or parameter named 'layers.0.linear_attn.in_proj_baa'\" — `in_proj_baa`?! My fused split handling generated `in_proj_baa`: the parameter `in_proj_ba.weight`, and the stacked mapping entry is something like (\"in_proj_ba\", \"in_proj_b\", 0/1)? The hf suffixes for in_proj_ba are probably \"in_proj_b\" + shard... My split processing: base = \"...in_proj_ba\"; the stacked entry is (vllm_sfx=\"in_proj_ba\", hf_sfx=\"in_proj_b\", shard_id=?), and maybe there's also another entry for \"a\"? If the hf suffix is \"in_proj_b\", then stem = base[:-len(\"in_proj_ba\")] + \"in_proj_b\" → \"...in_proj_b\" + the next entry hf_sfx \"a\"?? → \"...in_proj_b\" + \"a\" = in_proj_ba? And the second entry... produced 'in_proj_baa': base.endswith(\"in_proj_ba\") → stem = base[:-8] = \"...in_proj_\" wait: vllm_sfx = \"in_proj_ba\", base = \"layers.0.linear_attn.in_proj_ba\" (with language_model.model prefix), stem = base[:-len(\"in_proj_ba\")] = \"...linear_attn.\" Then f\"{stem}{hf_sfx}\": if the entry is hf_sfx = \"in_proj_ba\" itself → \"...linear_attn.in_proj_ba\" ✓ no problem. What the error shows is that the loader received 'in_proj_baa' — meaning the name I wrote was \"...in_proj_baa.weight\": stem \"...linear_attn.in_proj_b\" + hf_sfx \"a\"?? There must be an entry (vllm_sfx=\"in_proj_ba\", hf_sfx=\"a\", shard_id=...) — that is, the HF checkpoint stores in_proj_b and in_proj_a?? Hmm: \"in_proj_ba\" = b and a concatenated; HF names: in_proj_b + in_proj_a? Entry hf_sfx \"a\": stem = base[:-len(\"in_proj_ba\")]... no wait, my matching is: base.endswith(vllm_sfx=\"in_proj_ba\") ✓ → stem = base[:-10] = \"...linear_attn.\"; then name = stem + \"a\" = \"...linear_attn.a\"?? That would be 'a', not 'baa'.\n\nHmm, the 'in_proj_baa' that the loader sees... the loader's mapper: checkpoint name → vllm name is via hf_to_vllm_mapper, probably {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\", ...}? Or the model's hf_to_vllm_mapper maps HF→vLLM, and I wrote the vLLM name, but the mapper was applied to it anyway: mapper orig_to_new_substr {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\"?}... my checkpoint name \"...in_proj_ba.weight\" → substring \"in_proj_b\" was found → replaced with \"in_proj_ba\"?? → \"...in_proj_baa.weight\"! Yes — the mapper contains something like {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\"} (HF stores them separately, in_proj_b? no...). The actual HF checkpoint probably has in_proj_b and in_proj_a tensors; mapper {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\", \"in_proj_a\": \"in_proj_ba\"}? Hmm.\n\nKey insight: checkpoint names must be the HF-side names (before the mapper is applied). My introspection wrote the vLLM-side names; the loader applies hf_to_vllm_mapper to checkpoint names → collision/duplication. The fused split via stacked_params_mapping produced HF names for qkv and such, but even those pass through the mapper again (for qkv, the mapper probably doesn't contain those substrings, so they survived).\n\nThe cleanest fix: apply the inverse mapping myself — better yet: read the model's hf_to_vllm_mapper (WeightsMapper) inside the introspection, and write the checkpoint names as the preimage: for each vLLM parameter name, compute hf_name = the inverse of the mapper. WeightsMapper has orig_to_new_substr etc. Inversion: for each vllm param name, apply the reverse substitution new→orig (if the substitution is unambiguous). Let me look at the model's mapper: model.hf_to_vllm_mapper (does Qwen4ExpModel define it?). During introspection, grab `getattr(model, 'hf_to_vllm_mapper', None)` and dump its contents — then decide. Let me run a simple container probe that introspects the mapper (reuse the builder env? Simpler: a standalone python that builds the model the same way... that requires a full setup. Instead, temporarily patch make-proxy to dump the mapper to the manifest? Faster: a one-shot podman run python that reproduces the introspection setup and prints the mapper's dict. But that's about 50 lines of setup... Alternative: grep for WeightsMapper in the fork's model file."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"The loader applies an `hf_to_vllm_mapper` to checkpoint names — I must write HF-side names. Check the model's mapper definition:\n\n"}}
