{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The fused split wasn't performed: `in_proj_ba` is still fused as-is — the reason is that `packed.get(param_base)`: param_base = \"in_proj_ba\" — packed comes from `getattr(model, \"packed_modules_mapping\")` on the top-level model (ConditionalGeneration)... wait, packed is now being passed from introspection = dict(getattr(model, \"packed_modules_mapping\", {})) — the class attribute is defined on the CausalLM class (596), and on ConditionalGeneration it's merged (839) — getattr on the instance → should be found. But no split happened... Maybe param_base is what's failing: base = \"language_model.model.layers.0.linear_attn.in_proj_ba\" → rpartition(\".\") → param_base = \"in_proj_ba\" ✓ packed.get(\"in_proj_ba\") → [\"in_proj_b\",\"in_proj_a\"] ✓... then module = modules.get(mod_path) ✓ sizes come from the module... and then `fused_map[base]`... inside the writer loop: `if base in fused_map: for part, rows...: write_linear(f\"{base}.{part}\", ...)` — this writes out \"…in_proj_ba.in_proj_b\"?! Bug: the HF checkpoint name should replace the fused part name with the original part name, not append to it: \"...linear_attn.in_proj_b\", not \"...linear_attn.in_proj_ba.in_proj_b\". Split base into mod_path + param and use f\"{mod_path}.{part}\".\n\nAlso, the reason no split name showed up in hc's input_mix_weight_down_block_inject is the same reason.\n\nFurthermore, verify the pairing of sizes: in_proj_ba's sizes [48, 48]? packed [in_proj_b, in_proj_a] ✓.\n\nFix: inside fused_map, store mod_path along with it, and on write-out use f\"{mod_path}.{part}\". Store fused_map[base] = (mod_path, pairs).\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Split names were appended to the fused name instead of replacing it. Fix:\n\n"}}
