{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `output_partition_sizes` for these modules is 0 — because they were built under the META device: MergedColumnParallelLinear's __init__ sets output_partition_sizes from the argument — should be device-independent, though... maybe the attribute name is different, or perhaps these modules are ordinary nn.Linear (is GatedDeltaNet's in_proj_ba a custom linear?). \"0 partition sizes\" means getattr returned []. These are probably not MergedColumnParallelLinear, but rather the fork's own modules (QwenGatedDeltaNet's in_proj uses ColumnParallelLinear?).\n\nAlternative source for the shard sizes: the weight_loader's shard dimension, or — more simply — derive them from config:\n- in_proj_qkvz [16384, 2560]: parts [in_proj_qkv, in_proj_z]: qkv = (linear_num_key_heads*linear_key_head_dim?)… config: linear_num_key_heads=16, linear_key_head_dim=128 → q+k = 2*16*128 = 4096? Plus value: linear_num_value_heads=48 × linear_value_head_dim=128 = 6144 → qkv = 4096+6144 = 10240; z = 6144? 10240+6144 = 16384 ✓!! So qkv = (2*key_heads + value_heads)*… let's define it: qkv_rows = (linear_num_key_heads*linear_key_head_dim)*2 + linear_num_value_heads*linear_value_head_dim… 2×16×128=4096 (q and k) + 48×128=6144 (v) = 10240; z_rows = value_heads*value_head_dim = 6144 ✓ total 16384 ✓.\n- in_proj_ba [96, 2560]: parts [b, a]: b = a = linear_num_value_heads? 96/2 = 48 = linear_num_value_heads ✓ (b and a gates per value head). So 48/48.\n- shared_expert gate_up [1280, 2560]: even halves of moe... shared_expert_intermediate_size=640 → 640/640 ✓ even split.\n- input_mix_weight_down_block_inject [336, 10240]: parts [down, block_inject_weight, _padding]: hc_lowrank=320; hc_count=4: down = hc_count*hc_lowrank = 1280?? But the rows are only 336. Hmm: input_mix_weight_down [320, 10240]? block_inject: 16? 336 = 320+16. hc_lowrank 320, block_inject_weight rows = hc_count*4 = 16? Well — the padding part means the packed has 3 entries; sizes will probably be [320, 16] + padding…\n\nBetter approach: try alternative attributes: the module might be exposing `output_sizes`. First, probe the actual attribute of the module in the container — a quick one-shot: reproduce introspection and print dir(module) for in_proj_ba. That's another full build (~30 seconds). Worth doing.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b856296a090b4f9a9f6a7b4a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"podman run -i --rm --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host -v \"$HOME/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\" flashnext:dev python3 - <<'PY' 2>/dev/null\nimport json, torch\nfrom vllm.config import ModelConfig, VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config\nfrom vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry\nmc = ModelConfig(model=\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")\nvc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc)\nwith set_current_vllm_config(vc):\n    from vllm.distributed import init_distributed_environment, initialize_model_parallel\n    init_distributed_environment(world_size=1, rank=0, local_rank=0, distributed_init_method=\"tcp://127.0.0.1:29511\", backend=\"gloo\")\n    initialize_model_parallel(1, 1)\n    cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures, mc)[0]\n    with torch.device(\"meta\"):\n        model = cls(vllm_config=vc)\nmods = dict(model.named_modules())\nfor probe in (\"language_model.model.layers.0.linear_attn.in_proj_ba\",\n              \"language_model.model.layers.0.linear_attn.in_proj_qkvz\",\n              \"language_model.model.layers.0.attn_hyper_connection.input_mix_weight_down_block_inject\"):\n    m = mods.get(probe)\n    print(probe, type(m).__name__)\n    for attr in (\"output_partition_sizes\", \"output_sizes\", \"output_size\", \"partition_sizes\"):\n        if hasattr(m, attr):\n            print(\"   \", attr, getattr(m, attr))\nPY","timeout":300}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"q