{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"`output_partition_sizes` exists when probed directly! So why did my builder see 0? — in the builder, `modules` was captured in the same way… ah — the fused_map construction inside the builder uses `params` — and the size retrieval is `sizes = list(getattr(module, \"output_partition_sizes\", []) or [])` — module was `modules.get(mod_path)` (wrong key) → None → sizes is [] — fixed this to `modules.get(base)` in the previous edit! Let's re-run make-proxy (did I run it? The edit was made, but after the edit I only ran bash -n… no — after the edit I ran make-proxy, and it still failed with the same message? Wait, the order was: edit(mod_path→base), then make-proxy run → the manifest still showed \"0 partition sizes\"… hmm, did that run happen after the edit? Yes: \"ok: unpack tuple/DONE\", then bash -n + make-proxy + inspect → fused names still not split, then checked warnings → all \"0 partition sizes\"… was that run pre-edit? No — let me reconfirm the order:\n1. Replace the writer (modules = dict(model.named_modules()) inside main, references undefined `model`) → NameError.\n2. Fix introspection to return modules/packed; unpack. Run → works, but no split (in_proj_ba is still fused as before).\n3. At that point, check warnings → \"0 partition sizes\".\n4. Edit modules.get(mod_path) → modules.get(base).\n5. Haven't re-run make-proxy yet!\n\nExactly — step 5 is incomplete. Run it now. Also handle the HC case: sizes [320, 4, 12], parts [input_mix_weight_down, block_inject_weight, _input_mix_padding] — len(sizes)==len(parts)==3 → my code pairs all 3 then excludes \"_input_mix_padding\" → write out down (320 rows) + block_inject_weight (4 rows); padding (12 rows) is not written. Hmm — but the packed list expects 3 checkpoint pieces including padding?? \"_input_mix_padding\" — with underscore prefix: probably a padding shard not present in the checkpoint (the loader tolerates its absence). Trust this convention and see what happens.\n"}}
