{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"`safetensors._safetensors_rust.SafetensorError: Error while deserializing header: incomplete metadata, file not fully covered`\n\nMy handmade safetensors serializer's padding scheme is wrong: after the JSON header it's padded with spaces, but the header length recorded in the 8-byte prefix includes `hpad`… wait:\n\n```python\nf.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\nf.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n```\nThis writes length = len(hjson)+hpad, and the byte count also matches ✓. The header parser reads exactly that many bytes and parses the JSON (trailing spaces are OK for json.loads). \"file not fully covered\" means the sum of data_offsets != filesize. I'm padding each blob with nulls, but data_offsets only covers `len(raw)` — safetensors requires the file to end exactly at the last tensor's data_offsets[1]! Extra padding bytes after the last tensor violate \"fully covered\". Internal padding between tensors is also not allowed — offsets must be contiguous and cover the whole file. Solution: no padding at all (safetensors doesn't require alignment). Remove the padding logic.\n\nWhy did the earlier file pass my own checks? My validator only checked that the end of offsets <= filesize. And the fork's `parse_safetensors_header` (header only) tolerated it — the PLE shard file is read via memmap using offsets (tolerant), but the main file is read via the actual safetensors library → strict.\n\nFix to `save_safetensors`: contiguous offsets, no padding."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"My serializer's blob padding violates safetensors' \"file fully covered\" rule. Remove padding:\n\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_365983c3090043d59a576487","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"def save_safetensors(path, tensors):\n    \"\"\"Minimal safetensors serializer (8-byte LE header length, JSON header,\n    packed blobs) so fp8 tensors never depend on library-version support.\n    Offsets are contiguous and the file ends exactly at the last byte: the\n    rust parser refuses anything else (\"file not fully covered\").\"\"\"\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        blobs.append(raw)\n        offset += len(raw)\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson)))\n        f.write(hjson)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)","oldText":"def save_safetensors(path, tensors):\n    \"\"\"Minimal safetensors serializer (8-byte LE header length, JSON header,\n    packed blobs) so fp8 tensors never depend on library-version support.\"\"\"\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        pad = (8 - len(raw) % 8) % 8\n        blobs.append(raw + b\"\\x00\" * pad)\n        offset += len(raw) + pad\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    hpad = (8 - len(hjson) % 8) % 8\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\n        f.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)"}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`safetensors._safetensors_rust.SafetensorError: Error while deserializing header: incomplete metadata, file not fully covered`\n\nMy handmade safetensors serializer's padding scheme is wrong: after the JSON header it's padded with spaces, but the header length recorded in the 8-byte prefix includes `hpad`… wait:\n\n```python\nf.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\nf.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n```\nThis writes length = len(hjson)+hpad, and the byte count also matches ✓. The header parser reads exactly that many bytes and parses the JSON (trailing spaces are OK for json.loads). \"file not fully covered\" means the sum of data_offsets != filesize. I'm padding each blob with nulls, but data_offsets only covers `len(raw)` — safetensors requires the file to end exactly at the last tensor's data_offsets[1]! Extra padding bytes after the last tensor violate \"fully covered\". Internal padding between tensors is also not allowed — offsets must be contiguous and cover the whole file. Solution: no padding at all (safetensors doesn't require alignment). Remove the padding logic.\n\nWhy did the earlier file pass my own checks? My validator only checked that the end of offsets <= filesize. And the fork's `parse_safetensors_header` (header only) tolerated it — the PLE shard file is read via memmap using offsets (tolerant), but the main file is read via the actual safetensors library → strict.\n\nFix to `save_safetensors`: contiguous offsets, no padding.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"My serializer's blob padding violates safetensors' \"file fully covered\" rule. Remove padding:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_365983c3090043d59a576487","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"def save_safetensors(path, tensors):\n    \"\"\"Minimal safetensors serializer (8-byte LE header length, JSON header,\n    packed blobs) so fp8 tensors never depend on library-version support.\n    Offsets are contiguous and the file ends exactly at the last byte: the\n    rust parser refuses anything else (\"file not fully covered\").\"\"\"\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        blobs.append(raw)\n        offset += len(raw)\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson)))\n        f.write(hjson)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)","oldText":"def save_safetensors(path, tensors):\n    \"\"\"Minimal safetensors serializer (8-byte LE header length, JSON header,\n    packed blobs) so fp8 tensors never depend on library-version support.\"\"\"\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        pad = (8 - len(raw) % 8) % 8\n        blobs.append(raw + b\"\\x00\" * pad)\n        offset += len(raw) + pad\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    hpad = (8 - len(hjson) % 8) % 8\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\n        f.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)"}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1024,"output":906,"cacheRead":267264,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":345,"totalTokens":269194,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787997436161,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7bde02c4-5b26-4ed5-a461-76191929b0df","rawStopReason":"too