{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"My safetensors serializer pads the data (padding) — `pad = (8 - len(raw) % 8) % 8; blobs.append(raw + b\"\\x00\" * pad)` — but `data_offsets` doesn't include the padding: `\"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]`, followed by `offset += len(raw) + pad`. In other words, there's a gap between tensors. safetensors requires data to be contiguous (\"file not fully covered\"). The actual safetensors format requires data to be laid out continuously without gaps. The error \"incomplete metadata, file not fully covered\" confirms this. Let's remove the padding — offsets must be continuous.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The safetensors serializer pads blobs but the format requires fully contiguous data. Fix:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_09b50eb47add4d3fa2d7a39f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\nold = '''    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        pad = (8 - len(raw) % 8) % 8\n        blobs.append(raw + b\"\\\\x00\" * pad)\n        offset += len(raw) + pad\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    hpad = (8 - len(hjson) % 8) % 8\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson) + hpad))\n        f.write(hjson + b\" \" * hpad)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)'''\nnew = '''    # The safetensors format requires the data section fully covered, with\n    # each tensor's data_offsets contiguous — no padding between blobs.\n    header, blobs, offset = {}, [], 0\n    for name, (dtype, shape, raw) in tensors.items():\n        header[name] = {\"dtype\": dtype, \"shape\": shape,\n                        \"data_offsets\": [offset, offset + len(raw)]}\n        blobs.append(raw)\n        offset += len(raw)\n    hjson = json.dumps(header).encode()\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(struct.pack(\"<Q\", len(hjson)))\n        f.write(hjson)\n        for blob in blobs:\n            f.write(blob)'''\nassert src.count(old) == 1\nopen(p, 'w').write(src.replace(old, new))\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -2 && rm -f results/receipts/proxy.json && FN_PROXY_BOOT_TIMEOUT=3300 bash scripts/run-proxy.sh; echo \"RUNNER-EXIT=$?\"","timeout":3600}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1353,"output":708,"cacheRead":268288,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":145,"totalTokens":270349,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787997502395,"responseId":"chatcmpl-753ae87f-455c-476c-8e39-4d066c3dd103","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_09b50eb47add4d3fa2d7a39f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 31, in <module>\nAssertionError\nmake-proxy: checkpoint ready at /home/tom/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint: 4 safetensors files\nmake-proxy: next: scripts/run-proxy.sh\nrun-proxy: engine identity: bdb6f0420e797de9266de593326368091085cc3b\nrun-proxy: serving /home/tom/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint as 'flashnext-proxy' on 127.0.0.1:1235 (VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1, piecewise)\n922ccaa31aef836cb4b910a01226703f48a739af9622334478530d068152b14f\nrun-proxy: proxy receipt (fail): /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/results/receipts/proxy.json\nrun-proxy: FAILED at line 140 — recording a fail receipt and cleaning up\nrun-proxy: receipt already written (fail); keeping it\nRUNNER-