{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`Failed core proc(s): {'EngineCore': -9}` — EngineCore was killed by SIGKILL (-9). This is likely an OOM kill (this is a unified memory box, and loading weights onto GPU memory, or host memory pressure is the cause). Or a watchdog. Note: in previous failures EngineCore exited with code 1 due to a Python exception, but this time it's -9 = kill signal, suggesting OOM.\n\nAlso, it's possible that /tmp/proxy-serve logs remain from the manual debugging. Let's reproduce manually and check dmesg for OOM and full logs.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d6586963ad5d4166841378fc","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"dmesg 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"oom\\|killed process\" | tail -5; echo ====; cd /tmp && podman rm -f fnproxy-dbg >/dev/null 2>&1; podman run -d --name fnproxy-dbg \\\n  --network host --ipc host --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri \\\n  --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --group-add keep-groups --ulimit memlock=-1:-1 \\\n  -v \"$HOME/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy:ro\" \\\n  -e VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 -e HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 -e PYTHONHASHSEED=0 \\\n  flashnext:dev bash -lc \"exec vllm serve /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy \\\n    --served-model-name flashnext-proxy --host 127.0.0.1 --port 1238 \\\n    --tensor-parallel-size 1 --max-model-len 4096 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.6 \\\n    -cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE\" >/dev/null && sleep 150 && podman logs fnproxy-dbg > /tmp/proxy-serve3.log 2>&1; grep -n \"killed\\|Killed\\|SIGKILL\\|out of memory\\|OOM\\|Cannot allocate\" /tmp/proxy-serve3.log | head; grep -n \"Loading\\|weights\\|memory\" /tmp/proxy-serve3.log | tail -15; podman inspect -f '{{.State.Status}} {{.State.ExitCode}}' fnproxy-dbg","timeout":240}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":620,"output":549,"cacheRead":270336,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":128,"totalTok