{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Big progress: **Weights loaded successfully!** \"Loading weights took 1.38 seconds\", \"Model loading took 4.51 GiB memory\" — the entire checkpoint (names, shapes, fp8 experts, mmap table) was loaded without issues.\n\nNew failure: during memory profiling (`determine_available_memory`), it tries to allocate **256 GiB** → OOM. The profiling forward run is allocating a huge buffer — 274877906944 bytes = exactly 256 GiB. What allocates 256 GiB during the dummy forward? Probably the PLE mmap gather staging: MmapNgramEmbedding's forward allocates output (num_tokens × embedding_dim)... no wait. 256 GiB = 274877906944 B. max_num_batched_tokens default is 2048? 274877906944 / 2048 = 134217728 = 128 MiB per token?? Hmm: 274877906944 = 2^38. Something sized 2^38 — suspicious: int overflow/wraparound, or a size derived from a huge config value (e.g., something based on the full ngram table, 248320 vocab × something?). 274877906944 / 160 (row byte count) = 1717986918.4 — not an integer. /2560 = 107374182.4. Hmm 274877906944 = 1073741824 × 256 = 2^30 × 256.\n\nProbably a dummy-input allocation for multimodal ViT (num_position_embeddings?), or a prewarm of `positions_buffer`/PLE? Or a profiler dummy for mamba/GDN conv state: GDN's state cache per request × layers... For example, mamba conv state: max_num_reqs × layers × dstate...\n\nActually — thinking about vLLM's memory profiling: run dummy forward with max_num_batched_tokens tokens. GDN linear attention has a per-request recurrent state buffer sized by mamba_cache_params... On this model, the state per sequence = linear_num_value_heads × value_head_dim × key_dim? = 48×128×128×4 bytes ≈ 3 MB/req/layer... × 8 layers × num_reqs... doesn't get to 256 GiB.\n\n256 GiB = 2^38: it smells like a negative number or -1 wrapping around in unsigned size calculation... or 2^31 × 128. Could the allocation be `positions_buffer` × ...? Or the indexer with indexer_budget 2048? No, there's no full-attention layer now (indexer isn't built).\n\nHmm — what about the PLE prewarm/buffer: MmapNgramEmbedding's max_total_tokens buffer? `positions_buffer = arange(max_total_tokens)`. Small.\n\nWhat allocates during determine_available_memory? Dummy run of the model with a full batch. 2048 tokens. Hidden 2560. Logits buffer: 2048 × vocab 248320 × 2B (bf16) = 1.0 GB. Not 256G.\n\n274877906944 / (2048 × 2560) = 52428.8. Hmm. / (248320) = 1106947...\n\nLet me look at the log more closely to see the exact traceback of the OOM allocation.\n"}}
