{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The OOM originates from the **vision encoder** (`self.visual(pixel_values, grid_thw)` inside profile_run → encoder_runner.profile_encoder_cache) — the multimodal dummy inputs are running ViT with an enormous dummy image token budget (256 GiB activation). `language_model_only=True` is set, but vLLM still registers the model as multimodal and profiles the encoder.\n\nOptions:\n1. Remove multimodality from the proxy config: delete the vision_config / image/video token IDs and set architectures... the architecture \"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\" requires multimodal registration (the registry maps to the MM model). If vision_config is removed from the config, the model class might skip building the visual module (and `language_model_only` does exist as a config flag — but vLLM's ModelConfig still treats it as MM because the architectures is a registered MM architecture).\n\n2. Limit the MM profiler's budget: `--limit-mm-per-prompt image=0,video=0`! This disables mm inputs → encoder profiling is skipped. vLLM CLI: --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\": 0, \"video\": 0}'. This should make the model text-only at runtime. A simple serve-side fix — add to run-proxy.sh.\n\nLet's try adding `--limit-mm-per-prompt image=0,video=0` to serve. In newer vLLM, the syntax accepts JSON or key=value pairs: `--limit-mm-per-prompt image=0,video=0`? In the new version, `--mm-processor-kwargs`... is the flag `--limit-mm-per-prompt` (the older one) or `--limit-mm-per-prompt` + `--limit-mm-per-...`? Let me quickly check the CLI help inside the container."}}
