{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's a `--language-model-only` CLI flag! That's the cleanest — it tells vLLM to treat the model as language-model-only and skip the vision tower and MM profiling. Our config already sets language_model_only=True in config.json, but passing the CLI flag forces it. Actually, the config has language_model_only=True already set. But vLLM still builds the visual and profiles it. Hmm.\n\nWait — the config field is `language_model_only` at the top level. Let me check: in the config, we set `cfg[\"language_model_only\"] = True`. And the model reads `self.language_model_only`. At line 1005, when language_model_only, it ignores the visual weights. But the MM registry still registers it as multimodal, and the profiler still runs the encoder.\n\nThe `--language-model-only` CLI flag is the direct route. Let's add that. It should disable multimodal processing entirely. Let me check what it does.\n\nActually, the cleanest is to use `--language-model-only` — this is designed for exactly this case (a ConditionalGeneration architecture served in text-only mode). Let's add that to the serve command.\n\nLet me verify it works. I'll manually test the flag with a debug container.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"There's a dedicated `--language-model-only` flag — exactly right for a text-only serve of this ConditionalGeneration arch. Let me verify it fixes the OOM:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b6858f21eace490c971e4e8b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp && podman rm -f fnproxy-dbg >/dev/null 2>&1; timeout 400 podman run --rm --name fnproxy-dbg \\\n  --network host --ipc host --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri \\\n  --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --group-add keep-groups --ulimit memlock=-1:-1 \\\n  -v \"$HOME/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint:/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy:ro\" \\\n  -e VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 -e HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 -e PYTHONHASHSEED=0 \\\n  flashnext:dev bash -lc \"exec vllm serve /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy \\\n    --served-model-name flashnext-proxy --host 127.0.0.1 --port 1239 \\\n    --tensor-parallel-size 1 --max-model-len 4096 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.6 \\\n    --language-model-only \\\n    -cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE\" > /tmp/proxy-lmo.log 2>&1 &\nSVPID=$!\nfor i in $(seq 1 75); do\n  if curl -s http://127.0.0.1:1239/v1/models 2>/dev/null | grep -q flashnext-proxy; then echo \"UP after ~$((i*5))s\"; break; fi\n  sleep 5\ndone\ncurl -s http://127.0.0.1:1239/v1/models 2>/dev/null | head -c 300; echo\necho \"=== last log lines ===\"; tail -5 /tmp/proxy-lmo.log | cut -c1-160\npodman rm -f fnproxy-dbg >/dev/null 2>&1 || true","timeout":420}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1362,"output":769,"cacheRead":277504,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":267,"totalTokens":279635,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787998013354,"responseId":"chatcmpl-06d92fd7-9afd-4978-96b5-6c464a261c40","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b6858f21eace490c971e4e8b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n=== last log lines ===\n(APIServer pid=1)   File \"/opt/vllm/vllm/v1/engine/utils.py\", line 1240, in launch_core_engines\n(APIServer pid=1)     wait_for_engine_startup(\n(APIServer pid=1)   File \"/opt/vllm/vllm/v1/engine/utils.py\", line 1320, in wait_for_engine_startup\n(APIServer pid=1)     raise RuntimeError(\n(APIServer pid=1) RuntimeError: Engine core initialization failed. See root cause above. Failed core proc(s): {}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787998416121}]}
