{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The crash is inside `get_device_name_as_file_name` → `current_platform.get_device_name(device_id)` → the rocm wrapper at line 169, which calls `amdsmi_init()` without importing it. In this environment amdsmi is not available. This is a ROCm platform bug when amdsmi doesn't exist.\n\nWait — this is about fetching the MOE config file name. `get_config_file_name` calls `get_device_name_as_file_name`, which calls `current_platform.get_device_name()`. In the ROCm case, this goes through `with_amdsmi_context`, which references `amdsmi_init` — but the amdsmi import fails at the top of the module (I confirmed \"Failed to import from amdsmi\"). So `amdsmi_init` is undefined → NameError.\n\nThis is a genuine fork/platform bug, but I can't modify the fork (it's an engine, not in my conflict domain). But wait — I can avoid it by setting an override config for MOE so that `try_get_optimal_moe_config` uses `override_config` and skips `get_moe_configs`. Actually there's an easier way: there might be an environment variable to set a tuned config folder. Or, I could provide the MOE config via `VLLM_TUNED_CONFIG_FOLDER`.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The cleanest avoid: this only gets triggered when loading the MOE tuned config. If I set `VLLM_TUNED_CONFIG_FOLDER` to a directory containing properly named configs, it would still call get_config_file_name... no wait, let me check. Actually get_moe_configs calls get_config_file_name, which calls get_device_name_as_file_name → the crash. So the tuned config folder doesn't avoid it.\n\n`override_config` path: `from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe import get_config; override_config = get_config()`. If I could set an override config, it would skip get_moe_configs. How is get_config set? Let me check.\n\nActually — wait. Let me reconsider whether this is really in-scope. My task is scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, tests/. The amdsmi bug is a bug in the engine/container. But maybe I can avoid it via environment variables in run-proxy.sh (which I can control).\n\nLet me check what's going on at rocm.py:169 and whether there's an environment variable to avoid the amdsmi path for get_device_name. Let me look at get_device_name in rocm.py."}}
