{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Acceptance criteria pass; receipts-verify is also clean. Now, before committing, carefully review make-proxy.sh's python logic for bugs. Let me re-read the important parts.\n\nPotential issues in make-proxy's python:\n\n1. `validate_ple`: `found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))` — the dossier says it returns `per_layer[layer_idx][shard_idx] = (path, offset, rows)`. Probably a dict keyed by int. My code: `per_layer = {int(k): v for k, v in getattr(found, \"items\", lambda: found)()} if isinstance(found, dict) else found` — clunky but works for the dict case. If it's a dict with int keys, fine. `first = next(iter(per_layer.values()))[0]` — if some layer has zero shards, per-layer value could be an empty dict/list → IndexError. Guard: skip empties. Also `bad`'s comprehension iterates per_layer.items() — if v is a dict {shard_idx: tuple}, len(v) works ✓.\n\nBut if discover finds zero layers (e.g., PLE name mismatch), per_layer is empty → `next(iter(...))` StopIteration. Need guard: if no layers discovered → die (fatal) — that's an actual problem. Let me patch validate_ple.\n\n2. In `try_fork_introspection`'s fused split: `rows = total_rows // len(entries)` — qkv entries = 3 (q,k,v) but row split isn't equal (q=NH*HD, k/v=NKV*HD). With NH=16, NKV=2: total = (16+2+2)*256 = 5120; 5120//3 isn't an integer → wrong shape → loader weight_loader failure on serve. Better split: use config dims when suffixes are q/k/v. Handle: if set of shard_ids is {\"q\",\"k\",\"v\"} → row counts from config NH*HD, NKV*HD, NKV*HD. gate_up: two halves equally ✓.\n\nLet me fix:\n```python\nshard_rows = {}\nif {sid for _, sid in entries} == {\"q\", \"k\", \"v\"}:\n    shard_rows = {\"q\": NH*HD, \"k\": NKV*HD, \"v\": NKV*HD}\nfor hf_sfx, shard_id in entries:\n    rows = shard_rows.get(shard_id, total_rows // len(entries))\n```\nNeed NH/NKV/HD in scope: cfg is passed to the function ✓ (already has H, V; add NH/NKV/HD).\n\nEdge case: gate_up shard_ids could be (\"gate\",\"up\") or (0,1)? In vLLM's stacked_params_mapping, qwen's shard_ids are \"q\",\"k\",\"v\", and \"gate\",\"up\" for MergedColumnParallel. Fallback for equal split is fine.\n\n3. `curated_weights` — `quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))`: when ignore probe succeeded and installed the regex → non-expert linears are written in bf16 ✓; full-attn q/k/v/o are bf16 ✓ consistent with ignore semantics (skipped = unquantized). Experts are fp8 ✓ quantized regardless. Consistent.\n\nBut wait — in the quantize-all mode (ignore not installed), full-attn is written in fp8 with scale_inv ✓ consistent. embed/lm_head bf16 ✓ (loader rule). Router gate bf16 — in quantize-all mode, would Fp8LinearMethod get attached to the router? In vLLM, FusedMoE's gate is built as ReplicatedLinear(..., quant_method=None?) — router is created explicitly unquantized in qwen3_next (self.gate = ReplicatedLinear(config.num_experts, ..., bias=False, prefix=...) — hmm, with default quant_method=None it gets quant_config.get_quant_method applied?). In FusedMoE code, router `self.gate` typically uses `UnquantizedLinearMethod`… In qwen3_next.py: `self.gate = ReplicatedLinear(hidden_size, num_experts, bias=False, params_dtype=...)`? Don't fully recall; risk either way is minor; if router gets quantized and we supply bf16 → dtype mismatch error on serve. Hmm. FusedMoE router: FusedMoE.__init__ in vllm creates self.gate = ReplicatedLinear(..., bias=False, prefix=f\"{prefix}.gate\") without quant_method arg → quant_config.get_quant_method(layer) gets called → Fp8Config returns Fp8LinearMethod unless skipped! DeepSeek-V3's checkpoint has `mlp.gate.weight` unquantized… but their quantization_config's modules_to_not_convert includes every gate. Hmm, so with quantize-all, gate would expect fp8. My curated writer provides gate in bf16 → weight_loader shape/dtype mismatch? The fp8 param dtype is e4m3; copying bf16→fp8 param would error out.\n\nMitigation: provide gate in fp8 too in quantize-all mode? Router weight in fp8 with scales — Fp8LinearMethod.apply would work numerically. But router fp8 quantization on serve → routing logits quantized — for proxy that's fine (zeros anyway). But is the gate even subject to quantization? ReplicatedLinear with quant_method: if quant_method is None and quant_config given → quant gets resolved — probably yes. In quantize-all mode, write gate in fp8 (zeros + scale). In ignore-regex mode, gate stays bf16 ✓ (regex matches \"mlp.gate\" — wait: regex `^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$` — \"model.layers.3.mlp.gate\" doesn't contain \".mlp.experts.\" → skip ✓ bf16 ✓).\n\nUpdate curated_weights: gate is fp8 when quantize_linears else bf16. Same for introspection path: \"mlp.gate.weight\" has 2D shape — my introspection writer writes non-expert 2D weights as bf16 zeros. In quantize-all mode (ignore not installed) gate should be fp8… introspection path: when is it chosen vs the ignore probe? probe_ignore_semantics is called regardless; if regex semantics detected → ignore installed → non-experts bf16 ✓ gate bf16 ✓ consistent. If not detected → quantize-all → gate needs fp8 → introspection writer writes gate in bf16 → mismatch risk. Patch introspection writer too: treat \"mlp.gate\" weights as fp8 when ignore not installed.\n\nHmm — but wait, is router actually quantized by Fp8Config in quantize-all mode? If not (vLLM special-cases router), then providing fp8+scale_inv for gate → unknown param name error (\"gate.weight_scale_inv\" unmatched)! Ugh, double risk. Which is more likely? vLLM FusedMoE: `self.gate = ReplicatedLinear(config.num_experts, ... )` hmm actually let me recall vLLM's qwen3_next.py lines around 165: `self.experts = FusedMoEFactory(...)`, and `self.gate = UnquantizedLinearMethod`…? In vLLM models with quantized MoE (DeepSeekV3), the router stays bf16 and checkpoint has mlp.gate.weight as bf16 with modules_to_not_convert including… I recall seeing \"mlp.gate\" listed in DeepSeek's FP8 config? Not sure.\n\nGiven router quantization is uncertain and both choices can be wrong, safest: keep router in bf16 (matches DeepSeek-FP8 precedent where router stays unquantized — I'm fairly confident that vLLM's FusedMoE builds the gate without quant, or Fp8Config skips the router… hmm).\n\nActually — I recall vLLM's Fp8Config.get_quant_method: `if isinstance(layer, (LinearBase,))`… router ReplicatedLinear is a LinearBase → would receive Fp8LinearMethod. But then DeepSeek FP8 serving would need gate in fp8, contradicting the checkpoint (gate bf16, and it works). Resolution: DeepSeek's config.json's quantization_config has modules_to_not_convert with 943 entries… and the dossier said \"Only `mlp.experts.*` survives the 943-entry ignore list\" — wait re-read: \"so only `mlp.experts.*` survives the 943-entry ignore list, routed experts get Fp8MoEMethod\". Hmm — that says experts survive the ignore list (not ignored), all else ignored. So the 943 entries include all the gates etc. So yes: without ignore, router would be quantized. So quantize-all mode needs gate in fp8.\n\nDecision: write router in fp8 when quantize_linears mode (curated + introspection). If vLLM actually doesn't quantize router, then \"mlp.gate.weight_scale_inv\" name is unknown → loud error; acceptable risk given evidence suggests router quantized under quantize-all mode. Hmm actually wait — even if gate is quantized, the checkpoint name is \"weight_scale_inv\"? Fp8LinearMethod's block quant has weight_scale_inv param ✓ same convention.\n\nSimilarly lm_head: ParallelLMHead — quant doesn't apply (not LinearBase). ✓ bf16.\n\nembed_tokens: VocabParallelEmbedding with quant_config: Fp8Config.get_quant_method for embedding returns UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod unless checkpoint is fp8-serialized embedding — Fp8EmbeddingMethod exists for is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized… Fp8Config handles embedding: `if isinstance(layer, EmbeddingBase)`: returns Fp8EmbeddingMethod if is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized else Unquantized? Fp8Config.is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized is True when quantization_config present with fp8… hmm — Fp8Config.is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized: `self.quant_config.get(\"quant_method\") == \"fp8\"`… actually `is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized` is a property on Fp8Config that checks quant_config… For VocabParallelEmbedding under Fp8Config: in vLLM Fp8Config.get_quant_method → `if isinstance(layer, EmbeddingBase): return Fp8EmbeddingMethod(self) if self.is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized else UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod()`. And Fp8EmbeddingMethod expects fp8 weights named .weight with weight_scale… DeepSeek's embed_tokens is bf16 in checkpoint, and the ignore list includes embed? Their modules_to_not_convert certainly covers lm_head/embed (943 entries). With quantize-all → embed expected fp8!! Hmm. Fp8EmbeddingMethod: creates weight in fp8 dtype? If it expects checkpoint fp8 and we provide bf16 → mismatch.\n\nUgh, quantize-all mode keeps piling on risks. New decision: prefer the ignore-regex mode heavily; when regex semantics can't be verified, fall back to literal ignore list generated from… curated names I write? Fp8Config membership semantics: `prefix in ignored_layers` — prefix is the module prefix like \"model.layers.3.mlp.gate\". I know every non-expert Linear I write (curated): put their prefixes in modules_to_not_convert as literals; unknown linear-attn modules aren't in the list → would get quantized → unprovided → NaN risk. Hmm. But regex failure + membership semantics is only one branch.\n\nActually — the best hybrid for the membership semantics case: enumerate unknown modules via model introspection (if available) — we have full module list! From introspection: all param names → modules_to_not_convert = [prefix of every param that isn't experts weight/scale] as literals. Works under membership semantics ✓, also works under regex semantics (literal strings are also valid regexes that match themselves — re.match(\"model.layers.3.linear_attn.in_proj_qkvz\", prefix)… dots are regex any-char but still match ✓). So:\n\n- Introspection available → ignore list = literal prefixes of all non-expert params (works regardless of semantics!) → quantize config = experts-only (exactly workload shape!) → write experts in fp8, everything else in bf16. No regex needed.\n- No introspection → probe regex semantics; if regex → lookahead pattern; if not → quantize-all mode + curated writer with gate in fp8 (accept embed risk? no — embed: is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized… hmm, if Fp8EmbeddingMethod active for embed, expects fp8).\n\nWait, let me check Fp8Config.is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized: in vLLM fp8.py, `self.is_checkpoint_fp8_serialized = quant_config.get(\"quant_method\") == \"fp8\"`? Something like `bool(self.quant_config)`. If True → Fp8EmbeddingMethod for embed → embed should be fp8 + weight_scale… DeepSeek serves fine with bf16 embed because their ignore list covers \"model.embed_tokens\". OK so quantize-all mode risks embed too. To cap the damage in the last-resort mode, write embed + lm_head in fp8 with scale too?? If the loader path is UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod (other interpretation), then providing fp8 embed → copy to bf16 param → dtype conversion on load… does vLLM's default weight copy cast dtype? `param.data.copy_(loaded_weight.to(device, dtype=param.dtype))`? AutoWeightsLoader's default `load_into` does conversion… many loaders cast. Honestly, fp8 embed with scale named \"model.embed_tokens.weight_scale\" — if unquantized, that scale name is unknown → error. If quantized, and we gave bf16, also error.\n\nEnough — quantize-all mode has irreducible risks around embed/lm_head/gate semantics. The right move: make ignore-regex/literal the only path that ships weights; if neither introspection nor regex verification works, still install ignore list as best effort:\n- Membership + no introspection → can't enumerate → use regex pattern anyway and pray? If semantics is membership, regex string is treated as literal → matches nothing → everything quantized → NaN risk + possible mismatch errors. Bad.\n\nAlternative last resort: don't quantize at all except experts, via… quantization_config is required for experts. OK another idea: keep quantization_config, make modules_to_not_convert list a superset of prefixes covering every possible non-expert Linear. Prefix matching (membership) needs exact prefix. Regex semantics tolerates patterns. Can include both: patterns (for regex semantics) + guessed literals are useless for membership. Accept last-resort risk and flag loudly. Realistically: vLLM's Fp8 ignore semantics is regex (I'm fairly sure modern vLLM uses `re.match` via `is_layer_skipped` in quantization/utils… in compressed_tensors_utils `is_layer_skipped(prefix, ignored_layers, fqn)` does `return any(re.match(layer, prefix) for layer in ignored_layers)`). Probe will confirm at runtime. Move on.\n\nAdditional fix for last-resort mode: gate fp8 + embed risk: embed under Fp8EmbeddingMethod — if that's really active under quantize-all, DeepSeek-style checkpoints universally break without ignore entries… which is why real checkpoints have ignore entries. I'll keep embed/lm_head in bf16 and note the risk. Accept.\n\n4. Introspection path: names written include buffers? named_parameters excludes buffers ✓. But params like \"model.layers.X.linear_attn.A_log\" — 1-D, written as bf16 zeros ✓ (zeros for A_log is bad for dynamics? e^{-0}=1 → decay 1 → state accumulation — finite ✓; dt_bias zero → softplus(0)=ln2 ✓ finite).\n\nParams like MTP draft layers? architectures is ConditionalGeneration; MTP module (Qwen4ExpMTP) is a separate registry entry — not built ✓.\n\n\"rotary_emb.inv_freq\" — buffer, excluded ✓. If it were a param, zeros would be fine.\n\n5. Introspection path's expert handling: expert params may be batched: vLLM FusedMoE v1 uses batched expert tensors \"w13_weight\" with shape (E, 2M, H)? When experts are batched (modular kernel, \"Batched\"), HF names are still per-expert and weight_loader fuses — my per-expert HF naming via fused mapping: stacked_params_mapping is at attention level; expert fusion is handled inside FusedMoE's weight_loader via expert_id parsing of name \"experts.3.gate_proj.weight\". My introspection writer: for name containing \".mlp.experts.\" — param names on batched experts are \"model.layers.0.mlp.experts.w13_weight\" (no per-expert index!). My code checks `\".mlp.experts.\" in name and \"scale\" not in name` → writes that param name as-is, e.g., \"model.layers.0.mlp.experts.w13_weight\" in fp8 with shape (E,2M,H) — but the checkpoint convention is per-expert HF names, and vLLM's FusedMoE weight_loader maps \"experts.{id}.{gate|up|down}_proj.weight\" → w13/w2. If we write \"w13_weight\" name directly — does FusedMoE's loader also accept vLLM-side names? FusedMoE.load_weights handles `if \"w13_weight\" in name...`? I think modern FusedMoE.load_weights handles both HF per-expert names and direct w13/w2 names (maps checkpoint names like \"mlp.experts.0.gate_proj.weight\"). Direct \"w13_weight\" from checkpoint — in some implementations there's a branch for \"expert_params_mapping\"… risky. Safer: expand batched expert params into per-expert HF names: detect names ending in \".w13_weight\" → for e in E, write experts.{e}.gate_proj.weight (M,H) and experts.{e}.up_proj.weight (M,H); \".w2_weight\" → experts.{e}.down_proj.weight (H,M); scale_inv similarly split per-expert (w13_weight_scale_inv shape (E, 2*ceil(M/128), ceil(H/128))? per-expert scales: (ceil(M/128), ceil(H/128)) each for gate/up).\n\nImplementation: in introspection branch, if name matches r\"mlp\\.experts\\.(w13|w2)_weight$\": expand per expert with slice (zeros so values are trivial). Need E, M from cfg ✓.\n\nNon-batched fused experts (traditional FusedMoE): param name is \"model.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.w13_weight\"? No — traditional has per-expert FusedMoE module \"experts.0.w13_weight\" — per-expert index present. Then expansion would be different. Handle both: if \".experts.\" with digit index → per-expert HF name via fused mapping? Those aren't in stacked_params_mapping… FusedMoE's own expert_params_mapping handles \"gate_proj/up_proj → w13\". Checkpoint side HF name is still experts.{e}.gate_proj.weight. So when param name has numeric expert index + w13_weight suffix → convert to gate/up halves. Generalize: suffix w13_weight (with or without expert index) → emit gate+up; w2_weight → down; w13_weight_scale_inv → gate/up scale_inv; w2_weight_scale_inv → down scale_inv. Shapes: for batched w13 (E,2M,H) per-expert slice (M,H)… wait (2M,H): gate = [0:M], up=[M:2M] ✓ zeros anyway.\n\nFor scale_inv batched (E, 2*cm, ck) → per expert gate (cm, ck), up (cm, ck) ✓.\n\n6. In curated_weights gate fp8 fix (quantize-all mode): discussed; implement.\n\n7. validate_ple fix for empty per_layer + zero-shard layers.\n\n8. make-proxy bash: `find \"$PROXY_DIR\" -mindepth 1 -delete` ✓.\n\n9. run-proxy: `podman run --rm --entrypoint cat \"$IMAGE\" /opt/flashnext/build-info.json` — --entrypoint cat with args: podman run IMAGE arg → cat /opt/... ✓ (--entrypoint cat, CMD args = path) ✓.\n\n10. run-proxy ERR trap: `podman logs --tail 40 \"$CTR\"` when container doesn't exist → guarded with || true ✓. But `write_receipt` inside on_error runs `$(python3 -c ...)` using FN_TAIL — tail may have newlines/quoting — python -c reads env ✓ safe.\n\nHowever on_error runs when write_receipt itself fails (e.g., python error)… fine.\n\nAlso note: on_error calls write_receipt which runs heredoc python; inside, `existing` check keeps earlier receipt ✓.\n\n11. In run-proxy python stage, `urllib.error` imported but unused — fine (flake OK, not gated).\n\n12. `data[\"serve\"][\"port\"]` = \"1235\" string ✓.\n\n13. make-proxy: `torch.device(\"meta\")` context with model build — model ctor may do actual device allocations (buffers via register_buffer with device?) — try/except covers.\n\n14. make-proxy's `probe_fork_scaffolds`: `sys.path.insert(0, \"/opt/vllm/tests\")` then import \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap\" — need packages with __init__? pytest tree may lack __init__.py in tests/models/qwen4_exp… upstream vLLM tests uses rootdir imports without __init__ (pytest's rootdir sys.path magic). If plain import fails, entry records FAIL ✓ non-fatal.\n\n15. make-proxy curated: tensors dict with same bf16 bytes object for embed+lm_head? I make emb once, then _bf16(emb) twice → bytes computed twice (no object identity issue) ✓.\n\n16. PLE scale file \"model-ple-scales.safetensors\" — discover_shards only globs names matching _SHARD_RE ✓ scale file ignored by discovery ✓; loader reads all files for weights ✓.\n\n17. write_ple_shards row width: HD from head_dim (256) — matches MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab, head_dim) ✓.\n\n18. config template \"layer_types\" is filled by shrink ✓ (template starts with [] and shrink sets it).\n\n19. shrink: `set_(\"decoder_sparse_step\", 1)` unconditionally — may add a field unknown to real model… probably actual config field (qwen3_next has decoder_sparse_step) ✓.\n\n20. If workload config exists, it may include \"quantization_config\" which we replace ✓ (set_ overwrites).\n\n21. make-proxy: after shrink, we write config.json before tokenizer? stage_tokenizer is called before config.json is written — template vocab uses cfg[\"vocab_size\"] ✓ already shrunk ✓. Order: load→shrink→stage_tokenizer→write config ✓ tokenizer doesn't need config.json ✓.\n\n22. `save_safetensors` with tensors sharing bytes — fine.\n\n23. `_bf16` on meta tensors? Introspection writes zeros via torch.zeros (real tensors) ✓ not meta.\n\nOK let me implement fixes: (a) validate_ple robustness; (b) q/k/v row split + batched-expert expansion + gate dtype in introspection writer; (c) curated gate dtype; (d) also in introspection, if regex not installed, non-expert 2D weights are written in bf16 (correct under ignore list from introspection — when introspection succeeds, we now always install literal ignore list!).\n\nRestructure the decision flow in make-proxy's main():\n```\nintrospected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\nif introspected:\n    ignore = [literal prefix of every non-expert 2D weight param]\n    cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = ignore   # works under regex or membership\n    rewrite config.json\nelif probe_ignore_semantics():\n    cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = [lookahead regex]\n    rewrite config.json\nelse:\n    note quantize-all residual risk\n```\nLiteral prefix: from introspected param names ending in \".weight\", 2-D, non-expert, non-embed? embed: under ignore list, embed is unquantized ✓ we provide bf16 ✓ good — include embed_tokens prefix in ignore list (safe under either semantics). lm_head too (harmless).\n\nAnd curated_weights's quantize_linears flag reads cfg's modules_to_not_convert ✓ (set before curated call). Gate: fp8 when quantize_linears.\n\nIntrospection writer: non-expert weights bf16 (ignore list active — everything except experts non-quantized) ✓ current code OK; gate handled as non-expert ✓ bf16 ✓. Expert batched expansion fix needed; fused attention split fix needed.\n\nLet me rewrite those functions in make-proxy.sh.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me harden several edge cases I identified in the make-proxy generator (fused-param shape splits, batched expert tensors, router/embed quant semantics, discovery validation):\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_862a44dcf2714a859dcb9e64","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"def validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom):\n    if ple_mmap is None:\n        note(\"skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)\")\n        return\n    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))\n    per_layer = ({int(k): v for k, v in found.items()}\n                 if isinstance(found, dict) else found)\n    entry = {\"per_layer_shards\": {str(k): len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items()}}\n    expected = geom[\"split\"]\n    entry[\"expected_shards_per_layer\"] = expected\n    MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"validation\"].append(entry)\n    if not per_layer:\n        die(\"discover_shards found ZERO PLE shard tensors — the shard naming \"\n            \"does not match the fork's _SHARD_RE; refusing to proceed\")\n    bad = {k: len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items() if len(v) != expected}\n    if bad:\n        die(f\"discover_shards found {bad} shards where the geometry expects \"\n            f\"{expected} per layer — the mmap path would refuse this table at \"\n            \"attach time; refusing to hand run-proxy.sh a doomed checkpoint\")\n    # Row-count cross-check against the mirror formula, via the first shard.\n    first = next(v[0] for v in per_layer.values() if len(v))\n    rows = first[2] if isinstance(first, tuple) else None\n    if rows is not None and rows != geom[\"rows_per_shard\"]:\n        note(f\"discover_shards reports {rows} rows/shard vs the mirror's \"\n             f\"{geom['rows_per_shard']} — the serve is the tiebreaker\")","oldText":"def validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom):\n    if ple_mmap is None:\n        note(\"skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)\")\n        return\n    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))\n    per_layer = {int(k): v for k, v in getattr(found, \"items\", lambda: found)()} \\\n        if isinstance(found, dict) else found\n    entry = {\"per_layer_shards\": {str(k): len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items()}}\n    expected = geom[\"split\"]\n    bad = {k: len(v) for k, v in per_layer.items() if len(v) != expected}\n    entry[\"expected_shards_per_layer\"] = expected\n    MANIFEST[\"scaffold\"][\"validation\"].append(entry)\n    if bad:\n        die(f\"discover_shards found {bad} shards where the geometry expects \"\n            f\"{expected} per layer — the mmap path would refuse this table at \"\n            \"attach time; refusing to hand run-proxy.sh a doomed checkpoint\")\n    # Row-count cross-check against the mirror formula, via the first shard.\n    first = next(iter(per_layer.values()))[0]\n    rows = first[2] if isinstance(first, tuple) else None\n    if rows is not None and rows != geom[\"rows_per_shard\"]:\n        note(f\"discover_shards reports {rows} rows/shard vs the mirror's \"\n             f\"{geom['rows_per_shard']} — the serve is the tiebreaker\")"},{"newText":"    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):","oldText":"    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n    for i, lt in enumerate(cfg[\"layer_types\"]):"},{"newText":"        if quantized else _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n    # The router is a Linear too: without an ignore list the Fp8 config would\n    # claim it, so its checkpoint bytes must follow the same rule.\n    linear_gate = lambda name, shape: linear(name, shape, quantize_linears)\n    for i, lt in enumerate(cfg[\"layer_types\"]):","oldText":"        else:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))"},{"newText":"        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        linear_gate(f\"{m}.gate\", (E, H))","oldText":"        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        tensors[f\"{m}.gate.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(E, H))"}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":233,"output":6592,"cacheRead":124928,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5443,"totalTokens":131753,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993639126,"responseId":"chatcmpl-4d22041a-9215-48f7-be7b-23dd72377b08","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_862a44dcf2714a859dcb9e64","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 4 block(s) in /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 434 