ashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && awk '/def curated_weights/,/def write_ple_shards/' scripts/make-proxy.sh"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":7908,"output":183,"cacheRead":123904,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":104,"totalTokens":131995,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993805630,"responseId":"chatcmpl-5bd13f76-799b-4712-8eef-5484af32e94b","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b0d04fa2aec844b78171eb85","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def curated_weights(cfg):\n    \"\"\"qwen3-next-family HF naming; the fallback path. Residual risks, typed:\n    (a) linear-attention module tensors are left to the fork's own init —\n    safe only when the ignore-list keeps them unquantized; (b) PLE shards are\n    written for EVERY layer on the family's per-layer PLE signature.\"\"\"\n    H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E, M = EXPERTS, int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n    S = int(cfg.get(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", 0) or 0)\n    gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n    tensors = {}\n    emb = torch.randn(V, H, generator=gen) * 0.02\n    tensors[\"model.embed_tokens.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    tensors[\"model.norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):\n        if quantized:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n            tensors[name + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n        if quantized else _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n    # The router is a Linear too: without an ignore list the Fp8 config would\n    # claim it, so its checkpoint bytes must follow the same rule.\n    linear_gate = lambda name, shape: linear(name, shape, quantize_linears)\n    for i, lt in enumerate(cfg[\"layer_types\"]):\n\n    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):\n        p = f\"model.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            linear(f\"{a}.q_proj\", (NH * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.k_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.v_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.o_proj\", (H, NH * HD), quantize_linears)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n        # linear_attention layers: no checkpoint tensors are written — the\n        # fork's own init covers them when they stay unquantized (see above).\n        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        linear_gate(f\"{m}.gate\", (E, H))\n        for e in range(E):\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (M, H)), (\"up_proj\", (M, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, M))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.experts.{e}.{proj}\", shape, True)\n        if S > 0:\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (S, H)), (\"up_proj\", (S, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, S))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.shared_experts.{proj}\", shape, quantize_linears)\n    return tensors\n\n\ndef write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993812653},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Just as I was worried, that function got messed up. Let me rewrite `curated_weights` cleanly as a single block replacement.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The edits scrambled that function — let me rewrite `curated_weights` cleanly:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_95954c9b289047ddb2bc8090","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\nstart = src.index('def curated_weights(cfg):')\nend = src.index('def write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):')\nnew = '''def curated_weights(cfg):\n    \"\"\"qwen3-next-family HF naming; the fallback path. Residual risks, typed:\n    (a) linear-attention module tensors are left to the fork's own init —\n    safe only when the ignore-list keeps them unquantized; (b) PLE shards are\n    written for EVERY layer on the family's per-layer PLE signature.\"\"\"\n    H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E, M = EXPERTS, int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n    S = int(cfg.get(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", 0) or 0)\n    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n    gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n    tensors = {}\n    emb = torch.randn(V, H, generator=gen) * 0.02\n    tensors[\"model.embed_tokens.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    tensors[\"model.norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):\n        if quantized:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n            tensors[name + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n        else:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n\n    for i, lt in enumerate(cfg[\"layer_types\"]):\n        p = f\"model.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            linear(f\"{a}.q_proj\", (NH * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.k_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.v_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.o_proj\", (H, NH * HD), quantize_linears)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n        # linear_attention layers: no checkpoint tensors are written — the\n        # fork's own init covers them when they stay unquantized (see above).\n        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        # The router is a Linear too: without an ignore list the Fp8 config\n        # would claim it, so its bytes follow the same rule as the linears.\n        linear(f\"{m}.gate\", (E, H), quantize_linears)\n        for e in range(E):\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (M, H)), (\"up_proj\", (M, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, M))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.experts.{e}.{proj}\", shape, True)\n        if S > 0:\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (S, H)), (\"up_proj\", (S, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, S))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.shared_experts.{proj}\", shape, quantize_linears)\n    return tensors\n\n\n'''\nopen(p, 'w').write(src[:start] + new + src[end:])\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && echo BASH-OK && awk '/<<.PY.$/{f=1;next} /^PY$/{f=0} f' scripts/make-proxy.sh > /tmp/mp.py && python3 -m py_compile /tmp/mp.py && echo PY-OK"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1814,"output":1098,"cacheRead":131072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":27,"totalTokens":133984,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993812659,"responseId":"chatcmpl-05d33154-5e4a-41f2-88cf-bfa1d756fe6f","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_95954c9b289047ddb2bc8090","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"BASH-OK\nPY-OK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993834953},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Next, let's fix the main() flow and the introspection writer. Current main():\n\n```python\n    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    if probe_ignore_semantics():\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"]\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(...)\n```\n\nReplace this with the following:\n```python\n    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    ignore = None\n    if introspected:\n        # Literal non-expert prefixes: valid under both re.match and\n        # membership semantics, so no semantic probing is needed.\n        params, _stacked = introspected\n        ignore = sorted({n[:-len(\".weight\")] for n, s in params\n                         if n.endswith(\".weight\") and len(s) >= 1\n                         and \".mlp.experts.\" not in n and \"scale\" not in n})\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n    elif probe_ignore_semantics():\n        ignore = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"]\n    if ignore:\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = ignore\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(...)\n```\nHmm, wait, but literal prefixes like \"model.embed_tokens\" would be unquantized under regex semantics too: re.match(\"model.embed_tokens\", prefix) ✓. But regex special characters: dots match any character — still matches itself ✓. Names contain no other metacharacters ✓.\n\nEdge case: could the ignore literal list become huge (hundreds)? 8 layers × dozens of modules → a few hundred entries; config.json size is fine.\n\nNext, rewrite the introspection branch of the writer to handle the fused split and batched experts. Rewriting the entire introspection if branch:\n\n```python\n    if introspected:\n        params, stacked = introspected\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n        HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n        NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n        NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n        M = int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n        E = EXPERTS\n        tensors = {}\n        fused = {}\n        for vllm_sfx, hf_sfx, shard_id in stacked:\n            fused.setdefault(vllm_sfx, []).append((hf_sfx, shard_id))\n\n        def write_linear(hname, shape):\n            # With the ignore list active, only experts get quantized.\n            if \".mlp.experts.\" in hname:\n                tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n                tensors[hname + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n            else:\n                tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n\n        for name, shape in params:\n            if \"scale\" in name:\n                continue  # block scales are derived and written beside their weights\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and len(shape) == 2:\n                base = name[:-len(\".weight\")]\n                # batched / fused expert tensors are split back out into per-expert HF names\n                mex = re.match(r\"^(.*\\.mlp\\.experts)(?:\\.(\\d+))?\\.(w13|w2)_weight$\", name)\n                if mex:\n                    stem, eidx, w = mex.groups()\n                    es = [int(eidx)] if eidx is not None else range(E)\n                    cm, ck = scale_inv_shape((M, H))\n                    if w == \"w13\":\n                        for e in es:\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.gate_proj\", (M, H))\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.up_proj\", (M, H))\n                    else:\n                        for e in es:\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.down_proj\", (H, M))\n                    continue\n                hit = None\n                for vllm_sfx, entries in fused.items():\n                    if base.endswith(vllm_sfx):\n                        hit = (base[: -len(vllm_sfx)], entries)\n                        break\n                if hit:\n                    stem, entries = hit\n                    sids = {sid for _, sid in entries}\n                    if sids == {\"q\", \"k\", \"v\"}:\n                        rows = {\"q\": NH * HD, \"k\": NKV * HD, \"v\": NKV * HD}\n                    else:\n                        rows = {sid: shape[0] // len(entries) for _, sid in entries}\n                    for hf_sfx, sid in entries:\n                        write_linear(f\"{stem}{hf_sfx}\", (rows.get(sid, shape[0] // len(entries)), shape[1]))\n                    continue\n                write_linear(name, shape)\n                continue\n            if \"embed_tokens\" in name and len(shape) == 2:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.randn(*shape, generator=gen) * 0.02)\n                continue\n            if \"norm\" in name and len(shape) == 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.ones(shape[0]))\n                continue\n            if len(shape) >= 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n        save_safetensors(...)\n```\n\nWait, the scale_inv of the batched experts' per-expert w13: the per-expert gate scale shape is (cm, ck) ✓ handled inside write_linear (experts → fp8 + scale_inv) ✓.\n\nAlso, expert bias doesn't exist. Non-expert fused gate_up (shared_experts' merged gate_up_proj, etc.): entries {\"gate\",\"up\"} → even split ✓.\n\nNote: the `re` import exists inside python ✓.\n\nAlso, delete the now-obsolete duplicated old introspection branch. For replacement, let's check the current main + branch text.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now fix the main flow (ignore-list derivation) and the introspection writer (fused q/k/v splits, batched experts):\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5a221f9eafa14a5a9c3babce","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && awk '/^def main/,/^try:/' scripts/make-proxy.sh | head -120"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1911,"output":1490,"cacheRead":132096,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1381,"totalTokens":135497,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993834959,"responseId":"chatcmpl-6eb42481-5f2f-4f0c-b770-b45441bb810c","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5a221f9eafa14a5a9c3babce","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def main():\n    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    cfg, source = load_base_config()\n    MANIFEST[\"base_config_source\"] = source\n    MANIFEST[\"config_edits\"] = shrink(cfg)\n\n    MANIFEST[\"tokenizer_source\"] = stage_tokenizer(cfg)\n\n    # Write config.json first: both fork introspection and the fork's config\n    # class read the checkpoint directory as the model path.\n    (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n\n    ple_mmap = probe_fork_scaffolds()\n    geom = ngram_geometry(cfg)\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ngram\"] = geom\n\n    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    if probe_ignore_semantics():\n        # Negative lookahead: skip every Linear except the routed experts.\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\.mlp\\.experts\\.).*$\"]\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(\"modules_to_not_convert installed with regex semantics observed \"\n             \"in the fork's Fp8Config — non-expert linears stay unquantized\")\n\n    if introspected:\n        # Exact names from the fork's own class. Fused params are split back\n        # into their HF-side names; every other parameter is written under its\n        # own name, fp8-quantized iff it is an experts weight.\n        params, stacked = introspected\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n        V = int(cfg[\"vocab_size\"])\n        tensors = {}\n        fused = {}  # vllm suffix -> (hf suffix, shard ids)\n        for vllm_sfx, hf_sfx, shard_id in stacked:\n            fused.setdefault(vllm_sfx, []).append((hf_sfx, shard_id))\n        for name, shape in params:\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and shape and len(shape) == 2:\n                base = name[:-len(\".weight\")]\n                hit = None\n                for vllm_sfx, entries in fused.items():\n                    if base.endswith(vllm_sfx):\n                        hit = (base[:-len(vllm_sfx)], entries)\n                        break\n                if hit:\n                    stem, entries = hit\n                    total_rows = shape[0]\n                    for hf_sfx, shard_id in entries:\n                        rows = total_rows // len(entries)\n                        sub = (rows, shape[1])\n                        hname = f\"{stem}{hf_sfx}\"\n                        if \".mlp.experts.\" in hname:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(sub))\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(sub)))\n                        else:\n                            tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(sub))\n                    continue\n                if \".mlp.experts.\" in name and \"scale\" not in name:\n                    tensors[name] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n                    tensors[name[:-len(\".weight\")] + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = \\\n                        _f32(torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n                    continue\n            if \"embed_tokens\" in name and len(shape) == 2:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.randn(*shape, generator=gen) * 0.02)\n                continue\n            if \"norm\" in name and len(shape) == 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.ones(shape[0]))\n                continue\n            if len(shape) >= 1 and \"scale\" not in name:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n    else:\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"curated-fallback\"\n        tensors = curated_weights(cfg)\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n\n    shard_files, scale_tensors = write_ple_shards(cfg, geom)\n    if scale_tensors:\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-ple-scales.safetensors\", scale_tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-ple-scales.safetensors\")\n    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ple_shard_files\"] = shard_files\n    validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom)\n\n    manifest_path = OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\"\n    manifest_path.write_text(json.dumps(MANIFEST, indent=1))\n    total_bytes = sum(f.stat().st_size for f in OUT.iterdir() if f.is_file())\n    n_files = len(list(OUT.glob(\"*.safetensors\")))\n    print(f\"make-proxy: checkpoint complete: {n_files} safetensors files, \"\n          f\"{total_bytes / 2**20:.1f} MiB, weight_source=\"\n          f\"{MANIFEST['weight_source']}, base={source}\")\n    if MANIFEST[\"warnings\"]:\n        print(f\"make-proxy: {len(MANIFEST['warnings'])} warning(s) recorded \"\n              \"in proxy-manifest.json\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ntry:\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993866251},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Also — I just noticed `try_fork_introspection(cfg)` is called before config.json gets updated by the ignore list — no problem, since it reads the config from the OUT directory (which is already written). However, `ModelConfig(model=str(OUT))` reads the tokenizer — it's staged ✓.\n\nOne problem: introspection builds the model with the shrunken config — if the config is malformed → caught by except → fallback ✓.\n\nAlright, let's replace the flow section from `introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)` up to the end of the `if introspected:` branch.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5f5869b4363a488ab32536da","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\nstart = src.index('    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\\n')\nend = src.index('    else:\\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"curated-fallback\"')\nnew = '''    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    ignore = None\n    if introspected:\n        # Literal non-expert weight prefixes: valid under BOTH the regex and\n        # the membership reading of modules_to_not_convert, so the skip-list\n        # needs no semantic probe. Non-expert linears stay unquantized —\n        # exactly the workload's shape — and every parameter the fork's class\n        # declares is provided below.\n        params, _stacked = introspected\n        ignore = sorted({n[:-len(\".weight\")] for n, s in params\n                         if n.endswith(\".weight\") and len(s) >= 1\n                         and \".mlp.experts.\" not in n and \"scale\" not in n})\n    elif probe_ignore_semantics():\n        # Regex semantics observed in the fork's Fp8Config: one negative-\n        # lookahead pattern skips every Linear except the routed experts.\n        ignore = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\\\.mlp\\\\.experts\\\\.).*$\"]\n    if ignore:\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = ignore\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(f\"modules_to_not_convert installed ({len(ignore)} entries) — \"\n             \"non-expert linears stay unquantized, experts stay block-FP8\")\n    else:\n        note(\"RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed — quantize-all mode; \"\n             \"any quantized Linear whose name the fallback writer does not \"\n             \"know is uninitialized fp8 memory and could poison the logits\")\n\n    if introspected:\n        # Exact names from the fork's own class. Fused params are split back\n        # into their HF-side names; batched expert tensors are split back into\n        # per-expert HF names; only experts weights are block-FP8 (the ignore\n        # list above keeps everything else unquantized).\n        params, stacked = introspected\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n        HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n        NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n        NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n        M = int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n        E = EXPERTS\n        tensors = {}\n        fused = {}  # vllm suffix -> [(hf suffix, shard id)]\n        for vllm_sfx, hf_sfx, shard_id in stacked:\n            fused.setdefault(vllm_sfx, []).append((hf_sfx, shard_id))\n\n        def write_linear(hname, shape):\n            if \".mlp.experts.\" in hname:\n                tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n                tensors[hname + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                    torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n            else:\n                tensors[hname + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n\n        for name, shape in params:\n            if \"scale\" in name:\n                continue  # block scales ride beside their weights below\n            if name.endswith(\".weight\") and len(shape) == 2:\n                # Batched or fused expert tensors: back to per-expert HF names.\n                mex = re.match(r\"^(.*\\\\.mlp\\\\.experts)(?:\\\\.(\\\\d+))?\\\\.\"\n                               r\"(w13|w2)_weight$\", name)\n                if mex:\n                    stem, eidx, w = mex.groups()\n                    es = [int(eidx)] if eidx is not None else range(E)\n                    for e in es:\n                        if w == \"w13\":\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.gate_proj\", (M, H))\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.up_proj\", (M, H))\n                        else:\n                            write_linear(f\"{stem}.{e}.down_proj\", (H, M))\n                    continue\n                base = name[:-len(\".weight\")]\n                hit = None\n                for vllm_sfx, entries in fused.items():\n                    if base.endswith(vllm_sfx):\n                        hit = (base[:-len(vllm_sfx)], entries)\n                        break\n                if hit:\n                    stem, entries = hit\n                    sids = {sid for _s, sid in entries}\n                    if sids == {\"q\", \"k\", \"v\"}:\n                        rows = {\"q\": NH * HD, \"k\": NKV * HD, \"v\": NKV * HD}\n                    else:  # gate/up and friends split evenly\n                        rows = {sid: shape[0] // len(entries)\n                                for _s, sid in entries}\n                    for hf_sfx, sid in entries:\n                        write_linear(f\"{stem}{hf_sfx}\",\n                                     (rows.get(sid, shape[0] // len(entries)),\n                                      shape[1]))\n                    continue\n                write_linear(name, shape)\n                continue\n            if \"embed_tokens\" in name and len(shape) == 2:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.randn(*shape, generator=gen) * 0.02)\n                continue\n            if \"norm\" in name and len(shape) == 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.ones(shape[0]))\n                continue\n            if len(shape) >= 1:\n                tensors[name] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n        save_safetensors(OUT / \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\", tensors)\n        MANIFEST[\"files\"].append(\"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\")\n'''\nopen(p, 'w').write(src[:start] + new + src[end:])\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && echo BASH-OK && awk '/<<.PY.$/{f=1;next} /^PY$/{f=0} f' scripts/make-proxy.sh > /tmp/mp.py && python3 -m py_compile /tmp/mp.py && echo PY-OK"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":5833,"output":1652,"cacheRead":130944,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":128,"totalTokens":138429,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993866256,"responseId":"chatcmpl-641bad49-d8d0-48aa-ac4e-62f1055894ea","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5f5869b4363a488ab32536da","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"BASH-OK\nPY-OK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993897059},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, let me dry-run the fallback generator logic locally to detect runtime bugs (torch may not be installed on this machine, so I'll check). Let's verify: does this host have python3 with torch? Probably not. Simulation is possible: run the generator with a stubbed torch? That's heavy. Instead, carefully re-review the generated python file and test the pure-logic parts (config shrinking, geometry, safetensors serializer) with numpy-less stubs... Actually, I could copy /tmp/mp.py and replace `import torch` with a fake minimal torch shim to smoke-test the non-torch logic. But the code is deeply coupled with torch.\n\nAlternative: check whether torch exists on this host.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0ae9362285e045f6a7a6b391","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"import torch; print(torch.__version__)\" 2>&1 | head -2; python3 -c \"import numpy; print(numpy.__version__)\" 2>&1 | head -1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":3282,"output":218,"cacheRead":135168,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":146,"totalTokens":138668,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993897066,"responseId":"chatcmpl-79533557-9f51-41a3-bfca-d1cd6b41b7fa","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0ae9362285e045f6a7a6b391","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n2.5.1\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993907845},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no torch on this host, but numpy exists. Let's make a minimal torch shim that mimics the API used by the generator, so we can smoke-test the generator's logic end-to-end (config shrinking, geometry, safetensors serialization, fallback writer, PLE writer). The shim only needs to be sufficient for the fallback path (the introspection path imports vllm and will fail gracefully → fallback, which is exactly what we want to test).\n\nAPIs used in the fallback path:\n- torch.randn(V,H,generator=gen)*0.02, torch.zeros(shape), torch.ones(x), torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n- t.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous().view(torch.int16).numpy().tobytes()\n- t.to(torch.float8_e4m3fn).contiguous().view(torch.uint8).numpy().tobytes()\n- t.to(torch.float32).contiguous().numpy().tobytes()\n- torch.device(\"meta\") (introspection path — fails at vllm import before this)\n- torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n\nWrite the shim on top of numpy: Tensor wrapper class. bfloat16 conversion: fake it — store as float32 but .view(int16) needs 2 bytes... implement bf16 as float32→bf16 uint16 conversion (truncate mantissa) ✓. float8_e4m3fn: implement a simple encoder (just zero-fill / clamp) — shim returns uint8 zero-fill (values are zero anyway). Also implement torch.device, Generator.\n\nAfter that, run the generator with MODELS pointed at a fake (empty) directory and OUT pointed at a temp directory, with the vllm import failing → fallback path. Then, parse the generated safetensors header with a real safetensors library? Might not be installed. Verify with my own parser (header json). That's enough.\n\nLet's proceed with this test.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"No torch here, but I can smoke-test the generator's fallback path with a numpy-backed torch shim:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c278d8ac30d549fd9d79439c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/proxytest && cat > /tmp/proxytest/torch.py <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\n\nclass dtype:\n    def __init__(self, name, itemsize): self.name, self.itemsize = name, itemsize\n    def __repr__(self): return f\"torch.{self.name}\"\n\nfloat32 = dtype(\"float32\", 4); bfloat16 = dtype(\"bfloat16\", 2)\nfloat8_e4m3fn = dtype(\"float8_e4m3fn\", 1); int16 = dtype(\"int16\", 2)\nuint8 = dtype(\"uint8\", 1)\n\nclass Generator:\n    def manual_seed(self, s): self.seed = s; self.rng = np.random.default_rng(s); return self\n\nclass Tensor:\n    def __init__(self, arr, dt=float32): self.arr = np.asarray(arr); self.dtype = dt\n    def to(self, dt):\n        if dt.name == \"bfloat16\":\n            u = (self.arr.astype(np.float32).view(np.uint32) >> 16).astype(np.uint16)\n            return Tensor(u, dt)\n        if dt.name == \"float8_e4m3fn\":\n            a = np.clip(self.arr.astype(np.float32), -448, 448)\n            return Tensor(np.zeros(a.shape, np.uint8), dt)  # zeros path is exact\n        if dt.name == \"float32\": return Tensor(self.arr.astype(np.float32), dt)\n        return Tensor(self.arr, dt)\n    def contiguous(self): return self\n    def view(self, dt):\n        if dt.name == \"int16\" and self.dtype.name == \"bfloat16\":\n            return Tensor(self.arr.view(np.int16), dt)\n        if dt.name == \"uint8\": return Tensor(self.arr.view(np.uint8), dt)\n        return Tensor(self.arr, dt)\n    def numpy(self): return self.arr\n    def __mul__(self, o): return Tensor(self.arr * o, self.dtype)\n    def __rmul__(self, o): return self.__mul__(o)\n    @property\n    def shape(self): return tuple(self.arr.shape)\n\ndef zeros(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.zeros(tuple(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\ndef ones(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.ones(tuple(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\ndef randn(*shape, generator=None):\n    rng = generator.rng if generator else np.random.default_rng()\n    return Tensor(rng.standard_normal(tuple(shape)).astype(np.float32))\ndef manual_seed(s): pass\nclass device:\n    def __init__(self, name): self.name = name\n    def __enter__(self): return self\n    def __exit__(self, *a): return False\nEOF\necho shim-ok"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2520,"output":1118,"cacheRead":136192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":417,"totalTokens":139830,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993907851,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3f2029e8-4c59-4059-95e6-0c8a3afc0a02","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c278d8ac30d549fd9d79439c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"shim-ok\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993932395},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — the shim's `ones(shape)` also accepts scalar shapes (H,) ✓; `torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape))` is a list ✓. `torch.zeros(shape)` inside `_fp8` — the curated linear uses `torch.zeros(shape)` with a tuple ✓. `torch.ones(H)` scalar int ✓ tuple(H) fails — with Tensor(np.ones(tuple(H))) when H is an int → tuple(2560) error! `np.ones(2560)` is OK but `tuple(2560)` is a TypeError. Fix the shim: normalizing shape: `tuple(shape) if isinstance(shape,(list,tuple)) else (int(shape),)`. Patch the shim, and also the `Tensor` created from `torch.zeros(shape)` in the introspection branch is similar.\n\nAlso, the generator script reads env vars and runs main; imports vllm (fails) → no problem; sys.path.insert(\"/opt/vllm/tests\") is harmless.\n\nRun: set OUT to /tmp/proxytest/out via a script? OUT is hardcoded as Path(\"/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\")... For local testing, either patch a copy of mp.py with sed to replace the OUT path, or use a bind-like trick to run it: easiest is to make a copy with OUT replaced. Also the MODELS path is /models → doesn't exist → template path ✓.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_acac34f44c674a9da9968b3e","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp/proxytest && python3 - <<'EOF'\n# patch shim shape handling\ns = open('torch.py').read()\ns = s.replace(\"def zeros(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.zeros(tuple(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\",\n\"\"\"def _shp(s): return tuple(s) if isinstance(s, (list, tuple)) else (int(s),)\ndef zeros(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.zeros(_shp(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"def ones(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.ones(tuple(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\",\n              \"def ones(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.ones(_shp(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\")\nopen('torch.py','w').write(s)\nEOF\nawk '/<<.PY.$/{f=1;next} /^PY$/{f=0} f' /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh > gen.py\nsed -i 's|/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy|/tmp/proxytest/out|; s|/models|/tmp/proxytest/nonexistent|' gen.py\nmkdir -p out && PYTHONPATH=/tmp/proxytest python3 gen.py; echo \"EXIT=$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1607,"output":637,"cacheRead":138240,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":291,"totalTokens":140484,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993932401,"responseId":"chatcmpl-dff3666c-980b-43a6-825f-6ce416c8ae41","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_acac34f44c674a9da9968b3e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"make-proxy: no staged workload tokenizer: synthesized a WordLevel pair (proxy output text quality is not the claim; finite logits are)\nmake-proxy: ple_mmap not importable (ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named 'vllm'\"), ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named 'vllm'\")); the serve itself remains the naming authority\nmake-proxy: fork model introspection unavailable (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'vllm'); using the curated fallback naming with its typed residual risks\nmake-proxy: Fp8Config source probe unavailable: ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named 'vllm'\")\nmake-proxy: RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed — quantize-all mode; any quantized Linear whose name the fallback writer does not know is uninitialized fp8 memory and could poison the logits\nmake-proxy: skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)\nmake-proxy: 6 warning(s) recorded in proxy-manifest.json\nmake-proxy: checkpoint complete: 18 safetensors files, 220.4 MiB, weight_source=curated-fallback, base=template:evidence-dotfiles-observed-3.3+moe-dispatch-5\nEXIT=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993949045},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fallback path was executed end-to-end. 18 files = main 1 + PLE scale 1 + shard files 16 (8 layers × split 2) ✓. 220 MiB ✓ as expected. Next, verify the generated safetensors structure: parse the headers and validate names, dtypes, shapes, offsets; check the config.json contents; validate the shard naming regexes against _SHARD_RE in the dossier.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The fallback path runs end-to-end. Now verify the generated artifacts structurally:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e511c2dc557f4d72988a1f8d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp/proxytest && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re, struct, pathlib\nout = pathlib.Path('out')\nSHARD_RE = re.compile(r\"layers\\.(\\d+)\\.ple\\.ple_embedding\\.ngram_embedding\\.shard_(\\d+)\\.weight$\")\n\ndef header(p):\n    raw = open(p,'rb').read(8)\n    n = struct.unpack('<Q', raw)[0]\n    h = json.loads(open(p,'rb').read()[8:8+n])\n    return h\n\nfiles = sorted(out.glob('*.safetensors'))\nprint(len(files), \"files\")\ncfg = json.load(open(out/'config.json'))\nprint(\"archs\", cfg[\"architectures\"], \"| layers\", cfg[\"num_hidden_layers\"], \"| experts\", cfg[\"num_experts\"], \"| block\", cfg[\"quantization_config\"])\nprint(\"layer_types\", cfg[\"layer_types\"])\nmain = header(out/'model-00001-of-00001.safetensors')\nnames = sorted(main)\nprint(len(names), \"main tensors\")\nfor n in names[:14]: print(\"  \", n, main[n][\"dtype\"], main[n][\"shape\"])\n# validate each file: offsets within file size, shard naming\nsizes_ok = True\nfor f in files:\n    h = header(f); data = f.stat().st_size\n    for k,v in h.items():\n        if 'data_offsets' in v:\n            assert v['data_offsets'][1] <= data, (f,k)\n# shards\nshards = {}\nfor f in files:\n    for k in header(f):\n        m = SHARD_RE.search(k)\n        if m: shards.setdefault(int(m.group(1)), {})[int(m.group(2))] = header(f)[k]\nprint(\"shard layers:\", sorted(shards), \"per-layer counts:\", {k:len(v) for k,v in shards.items()})\nprint(\"shard dtype/shape sample:\", next(iter(next(iter(shards.values())).values())))\nscales = [k for f in files for k in header(f) if k.endswith('weight_scale')]\nprint(len(scales), \"weight_scale tensors; sample:\", scales[0], header(out/'model-ple-scales.safetensors')[scales[0]])\nprint(\"ALL STRUCTURE CHECKS PASSED\")\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1486,"output":656,"cacheRead":139264,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":94,"totalTokens":141406,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993949052,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3ad27a73-2936-426d-87da-b61d9b78a521","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e511c2dc557f4d72988a1f8d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"18 files\narchs ['Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration'] | layers 8 | experts 8 | block {'quant_method': 'fp8', 'weight_block_size': [128, 128]}\nlayer_types ['linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'full_attention', 'linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'full_attention']\n487 main tensors\n   lm_head.weight BF16 [4096, 2560]\n   model.embed_tokens.weight BF16 [4096, 2560]\n   model.layers.0.input_layernorm.weight BF16 [2560]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.down_proj.weight F8_E4M3 [2560, 256]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.down_proj.weight_scale_inv F32 [20, 2]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.gate_proj.weight F8_E4M3 [256, 2560]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.gate_proj.weight_scale_inv F32 [2, 20]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.up_proj.weight F8_E4M3 [256, 2560]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.up_proj.weight_scale_inv F32 [2, 20]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.1.down_proj.weight F8_E4M3 [2560, 256]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.1.down_proj.weight_scale_inv F32 [20, 2]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.1.gate_proj.weight F8_E4M3 [256, 2560]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.1.gate_proj.weight_scale_inv F32 [2, 20]\n   model.layers.0.mlp.experts.1.up_proj.weight F8_E4M3 [256, 2560]\nshard layers: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] per-layer counts: {0: 2, 1: 2, 2: 2, 3: 2, 4: 2, 5: 2, 6: 2, 7: 2}\nshard dtype/shape sample: {'dtype': 'F8_E4M3', 'shape': [256], 'data_offsets': [0, 256]}\n8 weight_scale tensors; sample: model.layers.0.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.weight_scale {'dtype': 'F32', 'shape': [1], 'data_offsets': [0, 4]}\nALL STRUCTURE CHECKS PASSED\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993971530},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The structure is correct:\n- Block FP8 expert weights [128,128] scale_inv shapes are correct (ceil(256/128)=2, ceil(2560/128)=20 ✓).\n- Per-layer shards are 2 each, 256 rows × head_dim 256… wait, the sample shard shape is [256]?? Expected (rows_per_shard, head_dim) = (256, 256). It's showing [256] — it's 1-dimensional! Bug: rows_per_shard = 256 (base 512 × head 1, split 2), HD=256 → torch.zeros((256,256)) should be 2-dimensional. But my shim: `torch.zeros(shape)` in _shp → tuple ✓ … the shim's Tensor arr is OK. Hmm, in `_fp8(torch.zeros(rows, HD))` — write_ple_shards calls `torch.zeros(rows, HD)` with two positional arguments! My shim's zeros signature is `zeros(shape, dtype=None)` — the second positional argument HD=256 got passed as dtype! Real torch.zeros(256, 256) is fine (variadic dims). This is a shim bug, not a generator bug. However — let me check the generator's call sites: `torch.zeros(rows, HD)` — valid real torch ✓. Just to be safe, I'll fix the shim and re-run to verify the 2-dimensional shape.\n\nAlso, verify the full-attention tensors and the tokenizer files. Quickly re-run.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The shard shape \"[256]\" is a bug in my shim (\"torch.zeros(rows, HD)\" — the shim was treating the second argument as dtype). I'll fix the shim and re-verify:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f57ff27e0cc34290b70227b0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp/proxytest && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('torch.py').read()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"def zeros(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.zeros(_shp(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"def zeros(*shape, dtype=None):\n    if len(shape) == 1 and isinstance(shape[0], (list, tuple)): shape = tuple(shape[0])\n    return Tensor(np.zeros(_shp(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"def ones(shape, dtype=None): return Tensor(np.ones(_shp(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"def ones(*shape, dtype=None):\n    if len(shape) == 1 and isinstance(shape[0], (list, tuple)): shape = tuple(shape[0])\n    return Tensor(np.ones(_shp(shape), np.float32), dtype or float32)\"\"\")\nopen('torch.py','w').write(s)\nEOF\nrm -rf out && mkdir out && PYTHONPATH=/tmp/proxytest python3 gen.py >/dev/null 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, struct, pathlib\nout = pathlib.Path('out')\ndef header(p):\n    n = struct.unpack('<Q', open(p,'rb').read(8))[0]\n    return json.loads(open(p,'rb').read()[8:8+n])\nf = out/'model-ple-3-00001.safetensors'\nh = header(f)\nk = list(h)[0]\nprint(\"shard tensor:\", k, h[k][\"dtype\"], h[k][\"shape\"])\nassert h[k][\"shape\"] == [256, 256], h[k]\nm = header(out/'model-00001-of-00001.safetensors')\nattn = [n for n in m if \"self_attn\" in n]\nprint(len(attn), \"attention tensors:\", sorted(attn)[:6])\nimport os\nprint(sorted(x.name for x in out.iterdir() if not x.name.endswith('.safetensors')))\ntok = json.load(open(out/'tokenizer.json'))\nprint(\"tokenizer model:\", tok[\"model\"][\"type\"], \"vocab:\", len(tok[\"model\"][\"vocab\"]))\nprint(\"SHARD SHAPE OK\")\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1787,"output":956,"cacheRead":140288,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":354,"totalTokens":143031,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993971536,"responseId":"chatcmpl-d5727f83-9695-4852-9a24-0c44d5e3e5cb","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f57ff27e0cc34290b70227b0","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"EXIT=0\nshard tensor: model.layers.3.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_00001.weight F8_E4M3 [256, 256]\n20 attention tensors: ['model.layers.3.self_attn.k_norm.weight', 'model.layers.3.self_attn.k_proj.weight', 'model.layers.3.self_attn.k_proj.weight_scale_inv', 'model.layers.3.self_attn.o_proj.weight', 'model.layers.3.self_attn.o_proj.weight_scale_inv', 'model.layers.3.self_attn.q_norm.weight']\n['config.json', 'proxy-manifest.json', 'tokenizer.json', 'tokenizer_config.json']\ntokenizer model: WordLevel vocab: 113\nSHARD SHAPE OK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787993995817},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All confirmed: shard [256,256] F8_E4M3, attention is only in full_attention layers (3 and 7 → 20 tensors = 2 layers × (4 fp8 + 4 scale + 2 norms)), tokenizer is synthesized, manifest also exists.\n\nNext, should I simulate the shrink path of the workload config too? To test shrink() with a fake workload config, mount /models — let me test quickly: create a config that looks like a fake workload, point MODELS there, and verify the shrink behavior + tokenizer copy. Quick test: modify gen.py? gen.py has MODELS hard-coded to /tmp/proxytest/nonexistent. Let me make a variant: create /tmp/proxytest/models with config.json + tokenizer file, sed-replace the path in gen.py.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me also exercise the workload-shrink path (base config + tokenizer copy):\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_315997c5b942484198fd669a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp/proxytest && mkdir -p models out2 && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ncfg = {\n \"architectures\": [\"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\"],\n \"model_type\": \"qwen4_exp\",\n \"torch_dtype\": \"bfloat16\",\n \"hidden_size\": 2560, \"head_dim\": 256,\n \"num_attention_heads\": 16, \"num_key_value_heads\": 2,\n \"num_hidden_layers\": 48, \"full_attention_interval\": 4,\n \"vocab_size\": 151936, \"max_position_embeddings\": 262144,\n \"num_experts\": 512, \"num_experts_per_tok\": 10,\n \"moe_intermediate_size\": 768, \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\": 768,\n \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 25000000, \"heads_per_ngram\": 8,\n \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 4096,\n \"quantization_config\": {\"quant_method\": \"fp8\", \"weight_block_size\": [128,128], \"modules_to_not_convert\": [\"x\"*30]*10},\n}\nopen('models/config.json','w').write(json.dumps(cfg))\nopen('models/tokenizer.json','w').write('{\"version\":\"1.0\"}')\nopen('models/tokenizer_config.json','w').write('{\"tokenizer_class\":\"X\"}')\nopen('models/generation_config.json','w').write('{}')\nEOF\nsed 's|/tmp/proxytest/out|/tmp/proxytest/out2|; s|/tmp/proxytest/nonexistent|/tmp/proxytest/models|' gen.py > gen2.py\nrm -f out2/*; PYTHONPATH=/tmp/proxytest python3 gen2.py 2>&1 | grep -v warning; echo EXIT=$?\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, pathlib\ncfg = json.load(open('out2/config.json'))\nprint(\"layers\", cfg[\"num_hidden_layers\"], \"experts\", cfg[\"num_experts\"], \"topk\", cfg[\"num_experts_per_tok\"])\nprint(\"vocab\", cfg[\"vocab_size\"], \"maxpos\", cfg[\"max_position_embeddings\"])\nprint(\"ngram_base\", cfg.get(\"ngram_vocab_size_base\"), \"heads\", cfg.get(\"heads_per_ngram\"), \"div\", cfg.get(\"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\"))\nprint(\"quant\", cfg[\"quantization_config\"], \"ignore\", cfg.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\nprint(\"layer_types head\", cfg[\"layer_types\"][:5], \"... len\", len(cfg[\"layer_types\"]))\nm = json.load(open('out2/proxy-manifest.json'))\nprint(\"base:\", m[\"base_config_source\"], \"| tokenizer:\", m[\"tokenizer_source\"])\nprint(\"ngram geom:\", m[\"geometry\"][\"ngram\"])\nimport glob\nprint(\"files:\", len(glob.glob('out2/*.safetensors')))\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1898,"output":889,"cacheRead":141312,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":173,"totalTokens":144099,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787993995824,"responseId":"chatcmpl-2d006062-7d2b-42a3-bb0a-af2106765fa5","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_315997c5b942484198fd669a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"make-proxy: ple_mmap not importable (ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named 'vllm'\"), ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named 'vllm'\")); the serve itself remains the naming authority\nmake-proxy: fork model introspection unavailable (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'vllm'); using the curated fallback naming with its typed residual risks\nmake-proxy: Fp8Config source probe unavailable: ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named 'vllm'\")\nmake-proxy: RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed — quantize-all mode; any quantized Linear whose name the fallback writer does not know is uninitialized fp8 memory and could poison the logits\nmake-proxy: skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)\nmake-proxy: checkpoint complete: 4098 safetensors files, 1672.7 MiB, weight_source=curated-fallback, base=workload:/tmp/proxytest/models/config.json\nEXIT=0\nlayers 8 experts 8 topk 8\nvocab 151936 maxpos 4096\nngram_base 512 heads 8 div 512\nquant {'quant_method': 'fp8', 'weight_block_size': [128, 128]} ignore None\nlayer_types head ['linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'full_attention', 'linear_attention'] ... len 8\nbase: workload:/tmp/proxytest/models/config.json | tokenizer: workload:tokenizer.json,tokenizer_config.json,generation_config.json\nngram geom: {'base': 512, 'heads': 8, 'divisible_by': 512, 'split': 512, 'padded_rows': 4096, 'rows_per_shard': 8, 'note': 'mirror of (org + split - 1) // split; a mismatch is caught by the discover_shards validation below'}\nfiles: 4098\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994023558},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Findings from the workload-path test:\n\n1. `num_experts_per_tok`: actual config value is 10 → min(10, 8) = 8 ✓ (top-k 8 out of 8 experts — valid).\n2. ngram geometry: base shrunk to 512, heads 8 → total 4096, padded 4096, split 512 (no split key in the config → default 512) → rows_per_shard 8, 512 shards/layer × 8 layers = 4096 shard files, each 8×256 = 2 KB → total for table is ~1.6 GB including per-file overhead. Hmm — 4098 files, 1672 MiB. It works, but it's heavy in file count for \"a small lookup table\". The split default of 512 is the fork's hard default, and if the actual model has no split field in the config, this is the right behavior. 4096 small files on NVMe is fine, and discover_shards parses headers only. Acceptable, and honest to the mirror. However, note: row_bytes — head_dim 256 ✓ shape (8,256).\n\nHmm wait — one more important check: with heads_per_ngram=8, is the PLE table row width really head_dim=256, or heads×ple_embed_dim? MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim) — nvidia ple_layer.py:288-290 passes `self.head_dim`. But that head_dim is the PLE layer's head_dim attribute, which may equal heads_per_ngram × ple_embed_dim! In amd/ple_layer.py:195-200: `VocabParallelEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim, ...)`. So the embedding width = self.head_dim, whatever that is. The geometry fields include `ple_embed_dim` — probably head_dim = heads_per_ngram * ple_embed_dim. I'm using the config's `head_dim` (attention head dim 256) — possibly wrong! If the PLE layer's head_dim differs, `_validate_layer_shards` will reject the row bytes and the serve will loudly fail.\n\nImprove the row-bytes guess: if config has `ple_embed_dim`, row_bytes = heads_per_ngram × ple_embed_dim; otherwise head_dim. This better matches the \"heads × ple_embed_dim\" structure. Let me patch write_ple_shards and ngram_geometry to compute row_bytes = heads * ple_embed_dim if both present, else head_dim. Also log in the manifest.\n\n3. Also worth noting: the actual checkpoint has 943 modules_to_not_convert — since my shrink replaces quantization_config wholesale, ignore=None here (quantize