exit_code': 2}, 'engine': {'lane': 'container', 'image': 'flashnext:dev', 'fork_repo': 'https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm', 'fork_commit': 'bdb6f0420e797de9266de593326368091085cc3b', 'fork_branch': 'flashnext', 'torch': '2.13.0+rocm7.14.0', 'torchvision': '0.28.0+rocm7.14.0', 'triton': '3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0', 'rocm_sdk_core': '7.14.0', 'amd_torch_device_gfx1151': '2.13.0+rocm7.14.0', 'gpu_target': 'gfx1151', 'built_at': '2026-08-29T07:07:15+0000'}, 'checkpoint_manifest': {'built_by': 'scripts/make-proxy.sh', 'ts': '2026-08-29T11:01:27', 'geometry': {'layers': 8, 'experts': 8, 'weight_block_size': [128, 128], 'ngram': {'base': 512, 'heads': 1, 'divisible_by': 128, 'split': 2, 'padded_rows': 512, 'rows_per_shard': 256, 'note': 'mirror of (org + split - 1) // split; a mismatch is caught by the discover_shards validation below', 'row_bytes': 256}, 'ple_shard_files': 16}, 'base_config_source': 'template:evidence-dotfiles-observed-3.3+moe-dispatch-5', 'config_edits': {'num_hidden_layers': [8, 8], 'layer_types': [[], ['linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'full_attention', 'linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'linear_attention', 'full_attention']], 'num_experts': [8, 8], 'num_experts_per_tok': [2, 2], 'decoder_sparse_step': [1, 1], 'moe_intermediate_size': [256, 256], 'shared_expert_intermediate_size': [256, 256], 'max_position_embeddings': [4096, 4096], 'vocab_size': [4096, 4096], 'quantization_config': [None, {'quant_method': 'fp8', 'weight_block_size': [128, 128]}], 'split_ngram_parts': [2, 2]}, 'tokenizer_source': 'synthetic-wordlevel', 'scaffold': {'fork_modules_probed': [{'module': 'models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap', 'import': \"FAIL ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'models.qwen4_exp'\"}, {'module': 'models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap_amd', 'import': \"FAIL ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'models.qwen4_exp'\"}, {'module': 'models.qwen4_exp.test_ple', 'import': \"FAIL ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'models.qwen4_exp'\"}], 'reused': [], 'validation': []}, 'weight_source': 'curated-fallback', 'files': ['model-00001-of-00001.safetensors', 'model-ple-scales.safetensors'], 'warnings': ['no staged workload tokenizer: synthesized a WordLevel pair (proxy output text quality is not the claim; finite logits are)', 'ple_mmap not importable (ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named \\'vllm\\'\"), ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named \\'vllm\\'\")); the serve itself remains the naming authority', \"fork model introspection unavailable (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'vllm'); using the curated fallback naming with its typed residual risks\", 'Fp8Config source probe unavailable: ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named \\'vllm\\'\")', 'RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed — quantize-all mode; any quantized Linear whose name the fallback writer does not know is uninitialized fp8 memory and could poison the logits', 'skipping discover_shards validation (module not importable)']}, 'error': 'serve container died during boot | unclean shutdown (stop rc=0, exit=2)', 'serve_log_tail': ['WARNING 08-29 09:02:03 [rocm.py:43] Failed to import from amdsmi with ModuleNotFoundError(\"No module named \\'amdsmi\\'\")', 'usage: vllm [-h] [-v]', '            {chat,complete,serve,launch,bench,collect-env,run-batch} ...', 'vllm: error: unrecognized arguments: --disable-log-requests'], 'mmap': {'log_mentions': 0, 'engaged': False}}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994148036},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent — the image exists on this host (flashnext:dev is already built!), and the script actually launched a real container with the real fork engine! The serve failed with:\n\n`vllm: error: unrecognized arguments: --disable-log-requests`\n\nSo this vLLM version doesn't accept --disable-log-requests. What's interesting is that it did manage to get through platform detection (\"Failed to import amdsmi\" warning → the fallback of patch 0003's KFD topology detection works). Also, this machine apparently has no visible GPU? The container actually ran vllm and exited with code 2 due to argument parsing — a fast failure, good.\n\nWait — but hold on, did I just launch a container on a host that might not have a GPU? The serve died at the argument parsing stage before GPU initialization. No problem.\n\nFix: remove --disable-log-requests from run-proxy.sh (or use the new name --log-requests-level? In recent vLLM it's `--log-requests-level` or the default). Simplest: remove the flag entirely.\n\nBut wait — even better, this means we can actually test the real serve locally… but this machine (the agent host) — is this a coordinator with a GPU? The container got past argument parsing… but the amdsmi import failed; KFD topology fallback. If /dev/kfd exists on this host, we might be able to fully launch the proxy! This is actually the first-light machine (campaigns run here). Let's check: ls /dev/kfd.\n\nNote: the python heredoc receipt writer worked, the container was cleaned up, and the ERR trap bug: `KeyError: 'FN_LINE'` — was on_error called with $1 unset? trap 'on_error $LINENO' — in bash, LINENO inside trap is expanded at trap definition time… it should have a value. Error: FN_LINE KeyError — meaning `python3 -c` was executed in an environment without FN_LINE… I wrote `FN_TAIL=\"$tailtxt\" FN_LINE=\"$line\" write_receipt ...` — write_receipt is a function; when you put environment variable assignments in front of a function call, the variables get set in the shell's environment for that command… in bash, `VAR=x funcname` — if funcname is a shell function, the variable assignment gets applied in the function's scope, but is it exported? Function calls: prefixed variable assignments get set in the function's local scope, but they are not exported to the child process unless they were already exported! That's the bug: FN_LINE/FN_TAIL aren't exported → python3 -c can't see them. Note however that write_receipt itself does `FN_STATUS=\"$1\" FN_DATA=\"$2\" FN_OUT=\"$OUT\" python3` — those are prefixed directly onto the python3 command → exported ✓. Fix: use export inside on_error:\n\n```\nexport FN_TAIL=\"$tailtxt\" FN_LINE=\"$line\"\nwrite_receipt \"fail\" \"$(python3 -c '...')\"\n```\nFirst the substitution — python3 -c is executed after the export ✓.\n\nAlso note: in this failure, the python stage's receipt correctly wrote \"serve container died during boot\" + log tail, and the trap preserved it ✓ — the never-overwrite design worked exactly as intended.\n\nAlso: boot_seconds 25.2 — the polling loop detected the container's death quickly ✓ (died at argument parsing; no /v1/models).\n\nFixes to run-proxy.sh:\n1. Remove --disable-log-requests.\n2. Fix the FN_LINE/FN_TAIL export inside on_error.\n\nThen retest — since this host actually has an image and (probably) a GPU, we might get a real serve attempt. First check /dev/kfd.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Two actual findings: this host **does indeed** have the `flashnext:dev` image — the runner actually launched the real engine — and (a) `--disable-log-requests` is not a valid argument in this vLLM version, (b) my trap isn't exporting `FN_LINE`/`FN_TAIL` (function-scope variables aren't exported). Let me check whether there's a GPU here, then fix both:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_888297c7a27e4af99dfead9b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /dev/kfd 2>&1; ls /sys/class/kfd 2>&1 | head -3"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_62a5321905354bb4ac8284f9","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"on_error() {\n    local line=\"$1\"\n    log \"FAILED at line $line — recording a fail receipt and cleaning up\"\n    local tailtxt=\"\"\n    tailtxt=\"$(podman logs --tail 40 \"$CTR\" 2>&1 || true)\"\n    export FN_TAIL=\"$tailtxt\" FN_LINE=\"$line\"\n    write_receipt \"fail\" \\\n        \"$(python3 -c 'import json,os; print(json.dumps({\"aborted_at_line\": int(os.environ[\"FN_LINE\"]), \"serve_log_tail\": os.environ[\"FN_T