m_experts_per_tok = 10\n  num_hidden_layers = 48\n  num_key_value_heads = 2\n  output_gate_type = sigmoid\n  output_router_logits = False\n  pad_token_id = None\n  partial_rotary_factor = 0.25\n  ple_conv_kernel_size = 4\n  ple_embed_dim = 2560\n  ple_layer_ids = [2]\n  rms_norm_eps = 1e-06\n  rope_parameters: <dict>\n    mrope_interleaved = True\n    mrope_section = [11, 11, 10]\n    partial_rotary_factor = 0.25\n    rope_theta = 10000000\n    rope_type = default\n  router_aux_loss_coef = 0.001\n  shared_expert_intermediate_size = 640\n  split_ngram_parts = 128\n  tie_word_embeddings = False\n  use_cache = True\n  vocab_size = 248320\ntie_word_embeddings = False\ntransformers_version = 5.8.0.dev0\nvideo_token_id = 248057\nvision_config: <dict>\n  deepstack_visual_indexes = []\n  depth = 27\n  hidden_act = gelu_pytorch_tanh\n  hidden_size = 1152\n  in_channels = 3\n  initializer_range = 0.02\n  intermediate_size = 4304\n  model_type = qwen4_exp\n  num_heads = 16\n  num_position_embeddings = 2304\n  out_hidden_size = 2560\n  patch_size = 16\n  spatial_merge_size = 2\n  temporal_patch_size = 2\nvision_end_token_id = 248054\nvision_start_token_id = 248053\nquantization_config: <dict>\n  quant_method = fp8\n  activation_scheme = dynamic\n  weight_per_tensor = False\n  act_per_tensor = False\n  weight_block_size = [128, 128]\n  modules_to_not_convert = ['lm_head', 'model.language_model.embed_tokens', 'model.language_model.hyper_con...\n\nlayer_types len: 0\nquantization_config keys: ['quant_method', 'activation_scheme', 'weight_per_tensor', 'act_per_tensor', 'weight_block_size', 'modules_to_not_convert']\nactivation_scheme: dynamic | block: [128, 128] | ignore entries: 943\nignore sample: ['lm_head', 'model.language_model.embed_tokens', 'model.language_model.hyper_connection_mixer.input_mix_weight_down', 'model.language_model.hyper_connection_mixer.input_mix_weight_up', 'model.language_model.layers.0.attn_hyper_connection.block_inject_weight']\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994356310},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"now the actual structure is coming into view:\n\n1. **The config is nested**: text_config holds all the fields; top-level is multimodal (vision_config + language_model). Module prefixes have `model.language_model.` on them (not `model.layers`). embed = `model.language_model.embed_tokens`, lm_head is at top level.\n\n2. **`ple_layer_ids = [2]`** — PLE only exists in layer 2!! Not in every layer. My assumption of \"per-layer PLE\" was wrong for this model. The proxy should respect ple_layer_ids: shrink to fewer layers → keep ple_layer_ids within range (e.g., 8 layers → [2] is still valid ✓).\n\n3. `split_ngram_parts = 128` exists as a config field ✓; `ngram_vocab_size_base = 20000000`, heads 8 → total 160M, divisor 128. Proxy: shrink base to 512 → total 4096, split 128 → shard_size 32, 128 shards for the single PLE layer.\n\n4. `modules_to_not_convert` = literal module names, 943 entries ('lm_head', 'model.language_model.embed_tokens', ...) — i.e., membership semantics by literal prefix. My probe said membership ✓ consistent.\n\n5. quantization_config needs activation_scheme (dynamic) + weight_per_tensor/act_per_tensor fields — merge instead of replace.\n\n6. Weight names carry the `model.language_model.` prefix; the multimodal architecture builds the vision tower too — shrink vision or drop it? Can I set `language_model_only: true`? There's a config flag \"language_model_only\": False — if I set it to true the vision tower won't be built! That shrinks things dramatically. But does vLLM respect this? Probably the model class checks this. If it exists, set language_model_only=true in the proxy. Hmm, risk: unknown semantics. In fact, the log showed \"Model ... is treated as multimodal but has no registered multimodal processor; running in text-only mode\" — vLLM is already demoting to text-only. Keep the vision config but it will still be built (vision tower weights will be needed!). If I