bed_dim = 8×2560 = 20480 → 51.2e9 params ✓ exact match to \"51.2-billion-parameter hash-lookup embedding\".\n\nSo org_rows = ngram_vocab_size_base // heads_per_ngram, then padded to make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by, row_bytes = heads × ple_embed_dim. Shard mapping: shard_size = ceil(org/split), shards = ceil(org/shard_size) = split (when divisible).\n\nFix to ngram_geometry: total = base // heads (if heads>1), else base*heads?? Hmm — which one? The 51.2B arithmetic nails it: rows = base/heads = 2.5M. Check divisibility: padded 2.5M is divisible by 128 ✓. So: rows = base // heads (when heads>1 and divisible). Encode that formula with a note; when base/heads isn't integral, fall back to base*heads… choice: if base % heads == 0 then total = base // heads, else base. Document the derivation in a comment (from the spec's 51.2B number).\n\nProxy numbers: base 512, heads 8 → rows 64, div 128 → padded 128; split 2 → shard_size 64, shards 2, row_bytes 20480 → table = 128 rows × 20480 = 2.6 MB ✓ small.\n\nHmm wait, let me double-check that padding is applied after the division: 2.5M is already divisible by 128. Proxy: 64 → pad to 128 ✓ shard rows 64 each.\n\nE. Curated fallback naming: for a nested config, prefixes are model.language_model.layers.* — my curated writer writes names in the model.layers.* form, which is wrong. But on this machine introspection should succeed and the fallback should remain unused. Still, cheaply improve the curated writer: derive the layer prefix from the ignore-list entries of the real config? Overkill. Instead: make the curated writer prefix-aware: prefix = \"model.language_model\" if cfg has text_config else \"model\". embed_tokens → f\"{prefix}.embed_tokens\". Also, the real model has hyperconnection modules, etc. — the curated fallback remains best-effort, the typed risks are documented. Keep it simple: implement prefix detection.\n\nF. Probe ignore semantics: observed membership. Then in membership mode, without introspection, we can't enumerate → quantize-all risk remains as documented. But introspection will likely succeed here. Also my regex probe: to be sure of the semantics, let me actually grep the fork's fp8.py — I'll verify quickly in the container.\n\nG. VllmConfig validation also needs activation_scheme in the quantization config → merge fix (A/B) covers this.\n\nH. try_fork_introspection: after construction, enumerate parameters — the model contains the language_model subtree + possibly vision (language_model_only=true strips vision). Also MTP? params might include mtp layers — the names will tell us.\n\nAdditionally, the duplicate op registration RuntimeError I saw earlier on import of amd/ops/hc.py during registry resolution — it appeared in the ERROR log but ModelConfig continued (registry resolution retried?). Occurred inside my introspection's ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls — did the import error out? After the \"Duplicate registration\" error, logs continued with WARNING about multimodal etc — that was my own introspection's ModelConfig construction (scheduler/config logs). resolve_model_cls hit the duplicate op at import time and… the reported introspection failure was a ValidationError from VllmConfig (activation_scheme) — so resolve_model_cls didn't even get there; the ERROR block came from ModelConfig init?? No — registry resolution happens inside ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls… order: ERROR from registry.py:1072, then WARNINGs from model.py/scheduler.py (ModelConfig). Hmm, actually maybe ModelConfig init resolves architectures for mm check → triggers the import → duplicate op error logged (was it swallowed?), then VllmConfig validation failed. Duplicate registration: ops/hc.py registers the op; something imported it twice (once via a previous import path during probe_fork_scaffolds? importing models.qwen4_exp.test_ple* module → importing vllm.models.qwen4_exp.amd.model → registering op; then resolve_model_cls's import path `from .amd.model import ...` via the package __getattr__ — same module object shouldn't be re-executed…). Duplicate at the same line 1038 → module was executed twice → two distinct module instances (e.g., `vllm.models.qwen4_exp.amd.ops.hc` and something aliased). Did my scaffold probe import `models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap` from the /opt/vllm/tests rootdir?? That FAILed (in this run ModuleNotFoundError: models.qwen4_exp not found — because tests/models has no __init__.py? in-container the import failed — good, so that wasn't the cause). The double import: registry resolves \"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\" → vllm.models.qwen4_exp __getattr__ → `from .amd.model import` … and earlier my try_fork_introspection's own ModelConfig init had already triggered the architecture resolution for the mm check (imported once)… the second import via a different module path (`vllm.models.qwen4_exp.amd.model` cached in sys.modules → no re-run). Hmm, direct_register_custom_op is supposed to be idempotent via a library check… direct_register_custom_op in vllm's torch_utils handles duplicates with `if my_lib is None`… whatever — this is fork-side behavior at serve time too. But serving goes through the same import once. In my introspection, the ERROR didn't raise (it was logged via the registry error handler, then… actually the registry error handler logs and re-raises). Did resolve raise? The exception caught was ValidationError — from the VllmConfig(...) call. So the registry ERROR lines came after resolve — meaning they were from ModelConfig?? No… order in stderr: ERROR block, then WARNING multimodal (ModelConfig), then my note about introspection failure (ValidationError). VllmConfig() runs after ModelConfig — resolve_model_cls is called inside my code after VllmConfig… my code order: mc = ModelConfig(...) → logs WARNING/INFO ✓; vc = VllmConfig(model_config=mc) → ValidationError raised ✓. So where did the registry ERROR come from? Probably from the probe_fork_scaffolds import of tests.models… (import failed). Or from ModelRegistry inside ModelConfig's mm check… anyway — not fatal to my flow; the serve has its own single import path.\n\nWait, actually — that ERROR block could affect the serve too if it's triggered by the same double-import path… serving is fresh single-process import → fine.\n\nSo let's apply the fixes. Restructure shrink to be text_config-aware, merge quantization, ple layer ids, geometry fix, template ple_layer_ids + activation_scheme, prefix-aware curated writer, write PLE only for ple layers.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The actual configuration revealed a nested multimodal structure, PLE only for layer 2 (`ple_layer_ids: [2]`), `activation_scheme: dynamic`, literal membership ignore semantics, and accurate table arithmetic (rows = base/heads, row width = heads×ple_embed_dim → 2.5M rows × 20480 B = 51.2B params ✓). Rewriting shrink/geometry/PLE writer accordingly:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c41dbfde43cf4247b102529c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\n\n# --- 1. shrink(): nested text_config, quant merge, ple layer ids, lm-only ---\nstart = src.index('def shrink(cfg):')\nend = src.index('# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Stage 2')\nnew_shrink = '''def shrink(cfg):\n    # Multimodal workload configs nest the language model under text_config;\n    # the template config is flat. Edit whichever level carries the fields.\n    tc = cfg.get(\"text_config\", cfg)\n    edits = {}\n\n    def set_(key, val):\n        edits[key] = [tc.get(key), val]\n        tc[key] = val\n\n    archs = cfg.get(\"architectures\") or []\n    if not any(\"Qwen4Exp\" in a for a in archs):\n        die(f\"base config architectures {archs} carry no Qwen4Exp identifier; \"\n            \"refusing to relabel a foreign model as the proxy\")\n    if \"language_model_only\" in cfg:\n        cfg[\"language_model_only\"] = True  # the proxy has no vision bytes\n        edits[\"language_model_only\"] = [False, True]\n    set_(\"num_hidden_layers\", LAYERS)\n    interval = int(tc.get(\"full_attention_interval\", 4))\n    pattern = [\"linear_attention\"] * max(1, interval - 1) + [\"full_attention\"]\n    set_(\"layer_types\", [pattern[i % len(pattern)] for i in range(LAYERS)])\n    set_(\"num_experts\", EXPERTS)\n    set_(\"num_experts_per_tok\",\n         min(int(tc.get(\"num_experts_per_tok\", TOPK)), EXPERTS))\n    # Every layer routed-MoE, so the admitted block-FP8 kernel runs on every\n    # decode step of the proxy serve.\n    set_(\"decoder_sparse_step\", 1)\n    set_(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"shared_expert_intermediate_size\" in tc:\n        set_(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER)\n    if \"intermediate_size\" in tc:\n        set_(\"intermediate_size\", 2 * BLOCK)\n    set_(\"max_position_embeddings\",\n         min(int(tc.get(\"max_position_embeddings\", 4096)), 4096))\n    if not (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file():\n        set_(\"vocab_size\", 4096)  # template tokenizer is paired with 4096\n    # PLE layers survive the layer shrink; the mmap claim needs at least one.\n    ple_ids = [i for i in tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\", range(LAYERS))\n               if i < LAYERS]\n    if not ple_ids:\n        ple_ids = [LAYERS - 1]\n    set_(\"ple_layer_ids\", ple_ids)\n    # Block-FP8 quantization: MERGE with the workload's quantization_config\n    # (activation_scheme and friends are required by the fork's Fp8Config —\n    # a wholesale replacement fails VllmConfig validation), and drop the\n    # workload's 943-entry ignore list: it names modules by layer index and\n    # cannot survive the shrink; the builder reinstalls its own below.\n    qc = dict(cfg.get(\"quantization_config\") or {})\n    qc.update({\"quant_method\": \"fp8\", \"weight_block_size\": [BLOCK, BLOCK]})\n    qc.setdefault(\"activation_scheme\", \"dynamic\")\n    qc.pop(\"modules_to_not_convert\", None)\n    edits[\"quantization_config\"] = \"merged; see manifest geometry\"\n    cfg[\"quantization_config\"] = qc\n    # Small PLE table: shrink every large ngram-size field; keep heads/dims.\n    for key in list(tc):\n        if \"ngram\" in key.lower() and re.search(r\"(size|base|vocab)\",\n                                                key.lower()):\n            val = tc[key]\n            if isinstance(val, int) and val > 512:\n                set_(key, 512)\n    split_key = next((k for k in tc\n                      if \"split\" in k.lower() and \"ngram\" in k.lower()), None)\n    if split_key is not None:\n        set_(split_key, 2)\n    return edits\n\n\n'''\nsrc = src[:start] + new_shrink + src[end:]\n\n# --- 2. template additions: ple_layer_ids, activation_scheme via flat cfg ---\nsrc = src.replace('''        \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 512,\n        \"heads_per_ngram\": 1,\n        \"ple_embed_dim\": 256,\n        \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 128,\n        \"split_ngram_parts\": 2,\n    }''', '''        \"ngram_vocab_size_base\": 512,\n        \"heads_per_ngram\": 1,\n        \"ple_embed_dim\": 256,\n        \"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\": 128,\n        \"split_ngram_parts\": 2,\n        \"ple_layer_ids\": [2],\n    }''')\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(src)\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && echo BASH-OK"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":5933,"output":4469,"cacheRead":152064,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3131,"totalTokens":162466,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787994356317,"responseId":"chatcmpl-09a65a48-39df-4870-a764-a0ed6b91880a","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c41dbfde43cf4247b102529c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"BASH-OK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994461171},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait a sec — template mode: flat cfg, text_config doesn't exist → tc = cfg ✓. But the template's quantization_config goes through the merge ✓ (no existing qc → create a new one with activation_scheme dynamic attached ✓).\n\nBut there's one problem: in template mode, the fields are at the flat top level, and stage_tokenizer reads cfg[\"vocab_size\"] ✓; curated_weights reads things like cfg[\"hidden_size\"] — but in WORKLOAD mode (nested), the curated fallback reads cfg[\"hidden_size\"] → KeyError (this is the crash that occurred). We need a helper that reads geometry from tc. Fix: curated_weights and write_ple_shards and ngram_geometry must use the text_config level. Add a module-level helper `_tc(cfg)` that returns cfg.get(\"text_config\", cfg), and use it in these functions and in main.\n\nAlso ngram_geometry/ngram_row_bytes fix (rows = base//heads; row_bytes = heads×ple_embed_dim). And write_ple_shards: only the ple layers, and use tc.\n\nFurther, the curated writer's prefix: if nested, \"model.language_model\".","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_be515eca98d14a78a1944483","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\n\n# --- text_config accessor + geometry fixes ---\nold_geom = src[src.index('def ngram_row_bytes(cfg):'):src.index('def probe_fork_scaffolds():')]\nnew_geom = '''def text_cfg(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Multimodal workload configs nest the language model under text_config;\n    the template config is flat.\"\"\"\n    return cfg.get(\"text_config\", cfg)\n\n\ndef ngram_row_bytes(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Row width of the mmap table, in fp8 elements. The PLE layer builds its\n    embedding at (padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim); the workload arithmetic\n    (specs/flashnext/spec.md \"engram table\": 51.2 B params = 2.5 M rows x\n    20480 B) shows head_dim = heads_per_ngram x ple_embed_dim there.\"\"\"\n    tc = text_cfg(cfg)\n    heads = tc.get(\"heads_per_ngram\")\n    dim = tc.get(\"ple_embed_dim\")\n    if isinstance(heads, int) and isinstance(dim, int):\n        return heads * dim\n    return int(tc.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n\n\ndef ngram_geometry(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Mirror the loader's shard mapping (specs/flashnext/evidence/\n    ple-54129.md section 3): shard_size = ceil(org / split); the checkpoint\n    carries ceil(org / shard_size) row-block tensors per PLE layer. The row\n    count arithmetic is pinned to the workload's 51.2 B-parameter table:\n    rows = ngram_vocab_size_base // heads_per_ngram, then padded to\n    make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by.\"\"\"\n    tc = text_cfg(cfg)\n    base = int(tc.get(\"ngram_vocab_size_base\", 512))\n    heads = int(tc.get(\"heads_per_ngram\", 1))\n    div = int(tc.get(\"make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by\", 1) or 1)\n    split = int(tc.get(\"split_ngram_parts\", 512))\n    total = base // heads if heads > 1 and base % heads == 0 else base\n    padded = math.ceil(total / div) * div if div > 1 else total\n    return {\"base\": base, \"heads\": heads, \"divisible_by\": div,\n            \"split\": split, \"rows_total\": padded,\n            \"rows_per_shard\": math.ceil(padded / split) if split else padded,\n            \"note\": \"rows = base // heads per the 51.2B-param arithmetic; \"\n                    \"shard_size mirror of (org + split - 1) // split; a \"\n                    \"mismatch is caught by the discover_shards validation\"}\n\n\n'''\nsrc = src.replace(old_geom, new_geom)\n\n# --- curated_weights: tc-aware + prefix-aware ---\ncw_start = src.index('def curated_weights(cfg):')\ncw_end = src.index('def write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):')\nnew_cw = '''def curated_weights(cfg):\n    \"\"\"qwen3-next-family HF naming; the fallback path. Residual risks, typed:\n    (a) linear-attention and hyperconnection module tensors are left to the\n    fork's own init — safe only when an ignore-list keeps them unquantized;\n    (b) PLE shards are written only for the config's ple_layer_ids.\"\"\"\n    tc = text_cfg(cfg)\n    # Multimodal configs nest weights under model.language_model.\n    prefix = \"model.language_model\" if \"text_config\" in cfg else \"model\"\n    H = int(tc[\"hidden_size\"])\n    HD = int(tc.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n    NH = int(tc.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n    NKV = int(tc.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n    V = int(tc[\"vocab_size\"])\n    E, M = EXPERTS, int(tc.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n    S = int(tc.get(\"shared_expert_intermediate_size\", 0) or 0)\n    quantize_linears = not bool(cfg.get(\"quantization_config\", {})\n                                .get(\"modules_to_not_convert\"))\n    gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n    tensors = {}\n    emb = torch.randn(V, H, generator=gen) * 0.02\n    tensors[f\"{prefix}.embed_tokens.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)\n    tensors[\"lm_head.weight\"] = _bf16(emb)  # tied content keeps logits finite\n    tensors[f\"{prefix}.norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n\n    def linear(name, shape, quantized):\n        if quantized:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _fp8(torch.zeros(shape))\n            tensors[name + \".weight_scale_inv\"] = _f32(\n                torch.ones(scale_inv_shape(shape)))\n        else:\n            tensors[name + \".weight\"] = _bf16(torch.zeros(shape))\n\n    for i, lt in enumerate(tc[\"layer_types\"]):\n        p = f\"{prefix}.layers.{i}\"\n        tensors[f\"{p}.input_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        tensors[f\"{p}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(H))\n        if lt == \"full_attention\":\n            a = f\"{p}.self_attn\"\n            linear(f\"{a}.q_proj\", (NH * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.k_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.v_proj\", (NKV * HD, H), quantize_linears)\n            linear(f\"{a}.o_proj\", (H, NH * HD), quantize_linears)\n            tensors[f\"{a}.q_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n            tensors[f\"{a}.k_norm.weight\"] = _bf16(torch.ones(HD))\n        # linear_attention layers: no checkpoint tensors are written — the\n        # fork's own init covers them when they stay unquantized (see above).\n        m = f\"{p}.mlp\"\n        # The router is a Linear too: without an ignore list the Fp8 config\n        # would claim it, so its bytes follow the same rule as the linears.\n        linear(f\"{m}.gate\", (E, H), quantize_linears)\n        for e in range(E):\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (M, H)), (\"up_proj\", (M, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, M))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.experts.{e}.{proj}\", shape, True)\n        if S > 0:\n            for proj, shape in ((\"gate_proj\", (S, H)), (\"up_proj\", (S, H)),\n                                (\"down_proj\", (H, S))):\n                linear(f\"{m}.shared_experts.{proj}\", shape, quantize_linears)\n    return tensors\n\n\n'''\nsrc = src[:cw_start] + new_cw + src[cw_end:]\n\n# --- write_ple_shards: only ple layers, tc-aware ---\nws_start = src.index('def write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):')\nws_end = src.index('def validate_ple(ple_mmap, geom):')\nnew_ws = '''def write_ple_shards(cfg, geom):\n    \"\"\"One row-block tensor per shard under the discover_shards naming, plus\n    the per-layer global weight_scale the load_weights interception keeps.\n    Shards are written only for the config's ple_layer_ids. Values are fp8\n    zeros at scale 1.0: the PLE contribution is exactly zero, which is\n    finite by construction.\"\"\"\n    tc = text_cfg(cfg)\n    prefix = \"model.language_model\" if \"text_config\" in cfg else \"model\"\n    rb = ngram_row_bytes(cfg)\n    rows, split = geom[\"rows_per_shard\"], geom[\"split\"]\n    ple_layers = tc.get(\"ple_layer_ids\") or range(int(tc[\"num_hidden_layers\"]))\n    files = 0\n    scale = _f32(torch.ones(1))\n    main = {}\n    for layer in ple_layers:\n        for s in range(split):\n            name = (f\"{prefix}.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n                    f\"ngram_embedding.shard_{s:05d}.weight\")\n            save_safetensors(\n                OUT / f\"model-ple-{layer}-{s:05d}.safetensors\",\n                {name: _fp8(torch.zeros(rows, rb))})\n            files += 1\n        main[f\"{prefix}.layers.{layer}.ple.ple_embedding.\"\n             f\"ngram_embedding.weight_scale\"] = scale\n    return files, main\n\n\n'''\nsrc = src[:ws_start] + new_ws + src[ws_end:]\n\n# main(): geometry row_bytes via ngram_row_bytes unchanged; curated writer's\n# quantize_linears now reads the merged qc — also fix the ignore install check\n# and the introspection writer's config reads (nested).\nsrc = src.replace('''        params, _stacked = introspected\n        ignore = sorted({n[:-len(\".weight\")] for n, s in params\n                         if n.endswith(\".weight\") and len(s) >= 1\n                         and \".mlp.experts.\" not in n and \"scale\" not in n})''',\n'''        params, _stacked = introspected\n        ignore = sorted({n[:-len(\".weight\")] for n, s in params\n                         if n.endswith(\".weight\") and len(s) >= 1\n                         and \".mlp.experts.\" not in n and \"scale\" not in n})\n        # lm_head lives at the top level and is never quantized.\n        ignore.append(\"lm_head\")''')\nsrc = src.replace('''        ignore = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\\\.mlp\\\\.experts\\\\.).*$\"]''',\n'''        ignore = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\\\.mlp\\\\.experts\\\\.).*$\"]''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    if ignore:\n        cfg[\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = ignore''',\n'''    if ignore:\n        cfg[\"quantization_config\"][\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = ignore''')\n# introspection writer config reads -> tc-aware\nsrc = src.replace('''        params, stacked = introspected\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        H = int(cfg[\"hidden_size\"])\n        HD = int(cfg.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n        NH = int(cfg.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n        NKV = int(cfg.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n        M = int(cfg.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n        E = EXPERTS''',\n'''        params, stacked = introspected\n        MANIFEST[\"weight_source\"] = \"fork-introspection\"\n        gen = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n        tc = text_cfg(cfg)\n        H = int(tc[\"hidden_size\"])\n        HD = int(tc.get(\"head_dim\", 256))\n        NH = int(tc.get(\"num_attention_heads\", 16))\n        NKV = int(tc.get(\"num_key_value_heads\", 2))\n        M = int(tc.get(\"moe_intermediate_size\", MOE_INTER))\n        E = EXPERTS''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    manifest_path = OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\"''',\n'''    MANIFEST[\"geometry\"][\"ple_layers\"] = list(\n        text_cfg(cfg).get(\"ple_layer_ids\", range(LAYERS)))\n    manifest_path = OUT / \"proxy-manifest.json\"''')\nopen(p, 'w').write(src)\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && awk '/<<.PY.$/{f=1;next} /^PY$/{f=0} f' scripts/make-proxy.sh > /tmp/mp.py && python3 -m py_compile /tmp/mp.py && echo OK"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":4789,"output":3019,"cacheRead":157696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":238,"totalTokens":165504,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787994461178,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e3a2dd31-6e12-4342-85ad-b7e873db2d3e","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_be515eca98d14a78a1944483","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 51, in <module>\nValueError: substring not found\nOK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994517664},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The outer python failed midw