uning_knobs_from_the_environment\",\n                    \"test_forward_raises_named_error_when_streamed_but_build_tables_never_ran\",\n                    \"test_model_load_weights_calls_build_tables_exactly_once_when_enabled\",\n--\n    \"weight_source\": \"curated-fallback\",\n    \"files\": [\n        \"model-00001-of-00001.safetensors\",\n        \"model-ple-scales.safetensors\"\n    ],\n    \"warnings\": [\n        \"fork model introspection unavailable (TypeError: _ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls() missing 1 required positional argument: 'model_config'); using the curated fallback naming with its typed residual risks\",\n        \"Fp8Config appears to consume modules_to_not_convert by literal membership; skipping the ignore-list (quantize-all mode)\",\n        \"RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed \\u2014 quantize-all mode; any quantized Linear whose name the fallback writer does not know is uninitialized fp8 memory and could poison the logits\"\n    ]\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994762681},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Big discovery! This time the test module import succeeded (models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap — tests must be in a different location, or the import path was resolved…). And my \"callable writer\" regex matched a ton of TEST functions (`test_build_tables_*`) — my regex `(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|...)` matched `test_build_tables_...`! One of them may have been called with fn(str(OUT)) — e.g., `test_build_tables_raises_when_a_ple_layer_has_no_shards_on_disk` — a pytest test function taking one argument… could it have run with a monkeypatch fixture?? With one positional arg it should fail… but some test taking a single `tmp_path`-like arg might have run and done something. More importantly: one of these test functions likely called discover_shards against the checkpoint directory (before the shard was written) → functools.cache got poisoned with an empty result → validate saw zero!\n\nAlso check the \"invoked\" entry — look at the entire scaffold block of the manifest. Fix for both problems:\n\n1. In probe_fork_scaffolds, don't call anything starting with `test_` — those are pytest tests, not fixture writers. Restrict to names not starting with \"test\" and not starting with \"test_\". The actual fixture writers inside the test file are typically private helpers (e.g., `_write_shard_file`) or pytest fixtures (FixtureFunctionMarker objects — not plain callables with a clean signature… in fact, pytest fixture functions are plain functions decorated with @pytest.fixture; if called directly they need fixture arguments). Realistically, no safe generic invocation exists → remove blind invocation entirely; limit to import-probing + recording candidates, plus reuse ple_mmap as the naming authority. That's the honest line: blind test invocation is dangerous (just polluted the cache!).\n\nActually — better targeted reuse: the fixture helper the dossier cited (test_ple_mmap.py:112-124 writes `model-ple-{layer_idx}-{shard_index:05d}.safetensors`) — probably a module-level helper function without the test_ prefix. If it exists, list it; only invoke non-test callables with a single path-like argument. Keep the invocation, but strictly exclude test_* names.\n\n2. validate_ple: bypass the cache with `getattr(ple_mmap.discover_shards, \"__wrapped__\", ple_mmap.discover_shards)`.\n\n3. Introspection API: `ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures, mc)` — the signature is (architectures, model_config) → returns (cls, arch). Fix the call: `cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures, mc)[0]`.\n\nFurthermore, from the list of test names, I learned something about the semantics of build_tables (\"build_tables attaches a table per PLE layer\", \"skips layers without an mmap placeholder\") — consistent with ple_layer_ids.\n\nLet me check the entire scaffold invocation record to see which test got invoked.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"My scaffold probe called a pytest test function (matching `build_tables`) and contaminated the cached `discover_shards`. Three fixes: exclude `test_*` callables, bypass the cache during verification, and the correct registry signature:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0d74107d80d644168fad10ad","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"python3 -m json.tool ~/.local/state/flashnext/proxy-checkpoint/proxy-manifest.json | grep -B2 -A4 '\"invoked\"\\|_error' | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2023,"output":759,"cacheRead":176128,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":643,"totalTokens":178910,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787994762688,"responseId":"chatcmpl-0f283d74-21db-4749-a867-a3260d69398e","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0d74107d80d644168fad10ad","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"                    \"test_build_tables_second_call_skips_the_discover_shards_header_scan\",\n                    \"test_build_tables_wires_the_tuning_knobs_from_the_environment\",\n                    \"test_forward_raises_named_error_when_streamed_but_build_tables_never_ran\",\n                    \"test_model_load_weights_calls_build_tables_exactly_once_when_enabled\",\n                    \"test_model_load_weights_never_calls_build_tables_when_disabled\"\n                ],\n                \"test_build_tables_attaches_a_table_per_ple_layer_without_cross_contamination_error\": \"TypeError\",\n                \"test_build_tables_ignores_layers_without_an_mmap_placeholder_error\": \"TypeError\",\n                \"test_build_tables_is_idempotent_and_reuses_an_already_attached_table_error\": \"TypeError\",\n                \"test_build_tables_raises_on_missing_shard_file_error\": \"TypeError\",\n                \"test_build_tables_raises_on_scale_mismatch_between_streamed_and_header_error\": \"TypeError\",\n                \"test_build_tables_raises_on_shard_width_mismatch_error\": \"TypeError\",\n                \"invoked\": \"test_build_tables_raises_when_a_ple_layer_has_no_shards_on_disk\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"module\": \"models.qwen4_exp.test_ple_mmap_amd\",\n                \"import\": \"FAIL RuntimeError: Tried to register an operator (vllm::qwen4_exp_grouped_gemma_rmsnorm(Tensor x, Tensor weight, float eps, SymInt num_groups) -> Tensor) with the same name and overload name multiple times. Each overload's schema should only be registered with a single call to def(). Duplicate registration: registered at /opt/vllm/vllm/utils/torch_utils.py:1038. Original registration: registered at /opt/vllm/vllm/utils/torch_utils.py:1038\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994784871},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed: `test_build_tables_raises_when_a_ple_layer_has_no_shards_on_disk` was invoked (a single positional argument — a pytest fixture function with a default value?), and the discover_shards cache against our directory got polluted... in fact, \"raises_when_a_ple_layer_has_no_shards\" runs discover against an empty table → the cache now holds empty results keyed by our model path. This also explains the duplicate op registration on the second import (test_ple_mmap_amd re-imported ops.hc via a different path — a fork-internal test artifact, unrelated).\n\nFixes:\n1. probe_fork_scaffolds: never invoke test_* functions; record them as candidates only. Invoke only non-test helpers, and maintain the signature guard.\n2. validate_ple: use __wrapped__ to bypass the functools.cache.\n3. Signature of resolve_model_cls: pass (mc.architectures, mc).\n\nApply these three edits.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_704040881acc488d93e5d0d0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\n\ndef rep(old, new, label):\n    global src\n    assert old in src and src.count(old) == 1, f\"BAD: {label}\"\n    src = src.replace(old, new)\n    print(\"ok:\", label)\n\n# 1. never invoke test_* functions: they are pytest tests, not fixture writers\nrep('''            writers = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                       if callable(getattr(mod, n, None)) and re.search(\n                           r\"(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|ckpt|\"\n                           r\"checkpoint|fixture)\", n, re.I)]\n            entry[\"callable_writers\"] = writers\n            for wname in writers:''',\n'''            # test_* names are pytest tests — invoking them runs fixture\n            # contracts we do not control (one polluted discover_shards'\n            # functools.cache in review); record them, never call them.\n            tests = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                     if n.startswith(\"test_\") and re.search(\n                         r\"(shard|table|ckpt|checkpoint|fixture)\", n, re.I)]\n            entry[\"test_contracts_present\"] = len(tests)\n            writers = [n for n in dir(mod)\n                       if callable(getattr(mod, n, None))\n                       and not n.startswith(\"test_\") and re.search(\n                           r\"(write|build|make|create).*(shard|table|ckpt|\"\n                           r\"checkpoint|fixture)\", n, re.I)]\n            entry[\"callable_writers\"] = writers\n            for wname in writers:''', \"scaffold test guard\")\n\n# 2. resolve_model_cls signature: (architectures, model_config)\nrep('''            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]''',\n'''            cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures, mc)[0]''',\n\"registry signature\")\n\n# 3. discover_shards is functools.cached — bypass any poisoned cache entry\nrep('''    found = ple_mmap.discover_shards(str(OUT))''',\n'''    # discover_shards is @functools.cache'd; bypass any cache a scaffold\n    # probe may have populated against this directory.\n    disc = getattr(ple_mmap.discover_shards, \"__wrapped__\",\n                   ple_mmap.discover_shards)\n    found = disc(str(OUT))''', \"cache bypass\")\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(src)\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && awk '/<<.PY.$/{f=1;next} /^PY$/{f=0} f' scripts/make-proxy.sh > /tmp/mp.py && python3 -m py_compile /tmp/mp.py && echo OK"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1895,"output":885,"cacheRead":177408,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":200,"totalTokens":180188,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787994784878,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7e5d2030-e9cf-47b8-8bab-75d4362f5ad0","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_704040881acc488d93e5d0d0","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok: scaffold test guard\nok: registry signature\nok: cache bypass\nOK\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787994804669},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — the old text of edit 2: did my try_fork_introspection have `ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]`? Originally I wrote `cls = ModelRegistry.resolve_model_cls(mc.architectures)[0]` — yes, matched ✓.\n\nAlso, the signature of ModelConfig(...) — it worked without issues in the run (no complaint about missing args was emitted).\n\nRe-run make-proxy for real.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0e9c3d8ef6c941a4b1db1f29","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && time bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -20","timeout":1200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1019,"output":186,"cacheRead":179200,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":93,"to