eated on the default device?). Using the `torch.device(\"meta\")` context should keep parameters on meta, but some code explicitly creates tensors on `torch.cuda` (e.g., ViT position embeddings?). On a ROCm container with GPU, \"cuda\" works.\n\n(b) Set the default device to meta and use `torch.set_default_device(\"meta\")`? Some code explicitly calls .cuda().\n\nSimplest: add device mounts + group-add/ulimit to make-proxy's podman run, just like run-proxy. Since this container has a GPU, the build will have GPU access. Weight construction via torch.zeros stays on CPU ✓; meta-context model parameters are on meta ✓.\n\nAdd to podman run: `--device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host --group-add keep-groups --ulimit memlock=-1:-1`.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Model construction reached kernel selection but needs GPU device access. Add the device flags to the builder container:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c715121b277e4e019383d93e","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"# -i keeps stdin attached: without it podman closes stdin and `python3 -`\n# silently executes an empty program (the bug latent in run-smoke.sh).\n# GPU devices are attached because the fork's model construction touches\n# device tensors even under the meta-device introspection path.\npodman run -i --rm \\\n    --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri \\\n    --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host \\\n    --group-add keep-groups --ulimit memlock=-1:-1 \\","oldText":"# -i keeps stdin attached: without it podman closes stdin and `python3 -`\n# silently executes an empty program (the bug latent in run-smoke.sh).\npodman run -i --rm \\"}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling/scripts/make-proxy.sh"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1732,"output":591,"cacheRead":190464,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":315,"t