ses a literal prefix, which works for both semantics if it's membership, and also works if it's regex (as a self-matching pattern). OK, no change needed.\n\nHowever note: the literal prefix from introspection includes all non-expert weights — including PLE-related ones (ngram embeddings don't exist as parameters when mmap is on… in the mmap-disabled builder env, ngram_embedding is a VocabParallelEmbedding parameter named something like model.language_model.layers.2.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.weight). Hmm! Introspection is done with VLLM_PLE_MMAP unset → ngram_embedding is a real parameter → it goes into the ignore list as a literal prefix \"model.language_model.layers.2.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding\" ✓ good (unquantized). And my checkpoint provides shard tensors instead of a .weight — the loader W5 interception handles this: shard names get discarded (weights_streamed), and the scale is retained. Since mmap is enabled at serve time, the loader branch differs: the MmapNgramEmbedding path expects shard names + weight_scale ✓.\n\nAlso the ignore list from introspection contains vision tower weights → they get written as bf16 zeros ✓ consistent.\n\nRe-run make-proxy.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4e3f91b0e0bd4fffab79779b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && time bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -10","timeout":1800}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1454,"output":446,"cacheRead":193536,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":344,"totalTokens":195436,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787995238829,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8669e2e2-ad11-4a80-90b6-7f57840cf48e","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4e3f91b0e0bd4fffab79779b","toolName":"bash",