bigger problem. Let me check what \"FlashAttention version None\" means on ROCm in this fork, and whether the serve-time backend selection is different. No, better: just run run-proxy.sh right now — it's the ground truth of claim 4.1. If serve also fails on QSA/FA, then the proxy needs full_attention layers = 0 (a linear-attention-only proxy) — since the mmap table + MoE admission doesn't depend on full attention, it's a legitimate proxy reduction.\n\nNo wait — think about P10/piecewise: serving requires compilation. Just run it. Use the real script from the repo, but keep the receipts in... run-proxy writes to REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/proxy.json — this worktree. If I run it here the receipt file will be created. Delete it after testing (since it would be generated during the campaign's own run). This is a verification run.\n\nLet me run with a generous timeout (cold compile; proxy is small — probably 5-15 minutes).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Introspection still can't construct the FA backend — the question of whether QSA works on serve is ultimately one that only serve itself can answer. Let's run the real `run-proxy.sh` end-to-end (receipts get deleted after verification):\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8f2e53970ed144be80cb1c04","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && FN_PROXY_BOOT_TIMEOUT=2400 bash scripts/run-proxy.sh; echo \"RUNNER-EXIT=$?\"","timeout":3000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1669,"output":429,"cacheRead":194304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":279,"totalTokens":196402,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787995290357,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b9a017d7-69f1-44f4-b945-b18e91c76b47","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8f2e53970ed144be80cb1c04","toolName":"bash"