ould affect the actual TP2 first-light too (a campaign-level problem that probably needs an upstream issue / fork fix — but that's for the fork lane, not my task).\n\nFor the PROXY (my task), the purpose is to execute the permitted MoE kernel + mmap table path. The full-attention/QSA layers are orthogonal. Proxy-side mitigation: set all layer_types to \"linear_attention\" — i.e., no full_attention layers → no QSA → no FA requirement. Would the model function? GDN linear attention works via Triton (the logs showed the GDN kernel was selected). PLE is at layer 1 (linear_attention type) — the PLE module is independent of attention type ✓. MoE is per-layer ✓.\n\nBut wait — does config validation allow layer_types that are all linear? full_attention_interval is 4… just set layer_types explicitly; remove it… hmm, the QSA indexer also has config parameters (indexer_budget etc.) — they just go unused.\n\nWait a sec — the real workload's initial light also faces this QSA-FA problem… unless the FA ROCm backend becomes available at serve time on the pair node (the same image). This is the same image on the same host. If FA is unavailable here, then the pair's first-light should fail likewise — that's a typed blocker for a different lane (fork/overseer). My proxy's task: deliver the proxy tooling that proves the permitted kernel + table path. Running without full-attention layers still satisfies claim 4.1 (proxy serves, mmap enabled, finite outputs, clean shutdown) — and, importantly, delivers the campaign behavior: \"the permitted kernel path and the ported table path execute on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded.\"\n\nHmm, but is layer_types=all-linear legitimate given \"same architecture identifier as workload\"? Architecture identifier = Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration ✓ unchanged. The spec says \"same architecture identifier and expert format\" — layer pattern is not included in the contract. The proxy is a \"small synthetic checkpoint\" — a layer-pattern reduction is in the spirit of \"a handful of layers.\"\n\nBut — wait. Reconsider: perhaps FlashAttention is available but the backend wasn't selected because… \"Using FlashAttention version None\" — in ROCm vllm, the FLASH_ATTN backend maps to AOTriton/CK flash-attn via the `flash_attn` package? The container may not have flash-attn (rocm). Check: does the image have flash_attn / vllm's ROCm FA? Look at qsa.py:100-110 to check which check raises, and see what the serve environment requires (probably `vllm.attention.backends.flash_attn` availability via `FlashAttentionBackend.get_name()`… let's read the qsa.py check.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The true serve-time blocker: QSA needs FlashAttention. Check what the fork's QSA actually requires:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_acfcd2366dad43899ed7a904","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"podman run --rm --entrypoint bash flashnext:dev -c \"sed -n '85,115p' /opt/vllm/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/amd/qsa.py; echo ====; grep -rn 'FlashAttention version' /opt/vllm/vllm/v1/attention/backends/ 2>/dev/null | head -3\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"^WARNING\\|^INFO\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1614,"output":800,"cacheRead":218112,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":650,"totalTokens":220526,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787996059447,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3ddd4e05-b788-4e25-8974-ebe8240fb287","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_acfcd2366dad43899ed7a904","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n    @staticmethod\n    def get_builder_cls() -> type[Qwen4ExpQSAMetadataBuilder]:\n        return Qwen4ExpQSAMetadataBuilder\n\n    @classmethod\n    def is_sparse(cls) -> bool:\n        return True\n\n    @classmethod\n    def supports_kv_connector(cls) -> bool:\n        return False\n\n\nclass Qwen4ExpQSAFlashAttentionImpl(FlashAttentionImpl):\n    \"\"\"Run paged sparse GQA with the QSA Triton kernel.\"\"\"\n\n    supports_dcp: bool = False\n    supports_pcp: bool = False\n\n    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs) -> None:\n        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)\n        if not is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available():\n            raise NotImplementedError(\"Qwen4Exp QSA requires FlashAttention\")\n        if self.dcp_world_size != 1:\n            raise NotImplementedError(\n                \"Qwen4Exp QSA does not support decode context parallelism\"\n            )\n        if self.kv_cache_dtype not in (\"auto\", \"bfloat16\"):\n            raise NotImplementedError(\"Qwen4Exp QSA requires a BF16 main KV cache\")\n        self.supports_quant_query_input = False\n====\n/opt/vllm/vllm/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py:898:            \"Using FlashAttention version %s\",\n/opt/vllm/vllm/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py:975:            \"FlashAttention version not detected.\"\n/opt/vllm/vllm/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py:1269:            \"FlashAttention version not detected.\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787996082952},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available()` is False — flash-attn's varlen function isn't available in this image (ROCm without flash-attn). So any configuration with full attention layers fails to serve in this container. The actual pair-first-light task hits this too — that's a separate lane's problem (probably needs an upstream issue / fork fix, or aiter). Doesn't block my deliverable: the proxy can fulfill its purpose (the accepted MoE + mmap table) even with linear_attention-only layers.\n\nJudgment: shrink() forces layer_types. For the proxy, all layers should be linear_attention, but… hmm, wait, P10/claim 4.1 doesn't require full attention. However — there's one thing to consider: piecewise cudagraph capture + mmap's splitting op: those don't depend on attention type ✓.\n\nBut — if all layers are