son":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3c76ef9fadb642e59920b181","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/opt/vllm/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/fp8.py:113:        self.ignored_layers_match_mode: Literal[\"exact\", \"substring\", \"suffix\"] = (\n/opt/vllm/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/fp8.py:185:                match_mode=self.ignored_layers_match_mode,\n/opt/vllm/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/fp8.py:205:                match_mode=self.ignored_layers_match_mode,\n/opt/vllm/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/utils/quant_utils.py:604:def is_layer_skipped(\n====\ndef is_layer_skipped(\n    prefix: str,\n    ignored_layers: list[str],\n    fused_mapping: Mapping[str, list[str]] = MappingProxyType({}),\n    *,\n    match_mode: Literal[\"exact\", \"substring\", \"suffix\"] = \"exact\",\n) -> bool:\n    def prefix_full_match(prefix: str, ignored_layers: list[str]) -> bool:\n        return prefix in ignored_layers\n\n    # For case like: ignored_layers = [\"self_attn\"]\n    def substr_match(prefix: str, ignored_layers: list[str]) -> bool:\n        return any(layer in prefix for layer in ignored_layers)\n\n    # Match abbreviated module paths at a component boundary. For example,\n    # ``b_proj`` matches ``model.layers.0.self_attn.b_proj`` but not\n    # ``model.layers.0.self_attn.q_b_proj``.\n    def suffix_match(prefix: str, ignored_layers: list[str]) -> bool:\n        return any(\n            prefix == layer or prefix.endswith(f\".{layer}\") for layer in ignored_layers\n        )\n\n    if match_mode == \"exact\":\n        match_func = prefix_full_match\n    elif match_mode == \"substring\":\n        match_func = substr_match\n    elif match_mode == \"suffix\":\n        match_func = suffix_match\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported layer skip match mode: {match_mode}\")\n\n    # prefix: model.layers.0.self_attn.q_proj\n    # proj_name: q_proj\n    proj_name = prefix.split(\".\")[-1]\n\n    # Fused layers like gate_up_proj or qkv_proj will not be fused\n    # in the safetensors checkpoint. So, we convert the name\n    # from the fused version to unfused + check to make sure that\n    # each shard of the fused layer has the same scheme.\n    #\n    # Some checkpoints (e.g. block-FP8 Step-3.5-Flash) already list the\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787996123569},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand exactly: `is_layer_skipped` has exact/substring/suffix modes, and `ignored_layers_match_mode` is a field of the quantization config (fp8.py:113 — probably read from `config.get(\"ignored_layers_match_mode\")`, default \"exact\"?). Let me check line 113 and the match_mode of the workload's quantization config. If match_mode is configurable within quantization_config, then we can set `\"ignored_layers_match_mode\": \"substring\"` and use one entry that skips everything except experts... wait, substring: `any(layer in prefix for layer in ignored)` — can't do negative matching. But the SUFFIX mode... can't do negative matching either.\n\nHmm — none of the modes support \"everything except X\". The workload's approach: literal exact list of 943 entries. The real checkpoint relies on exact matching of complete module prefixes (e.g., 'lm_head', 'model.language_model.embed_tokens', 'model.language_model.layers.0.attn_hyper_connection.block_inject_weight', ...).\n\nSo the fallback writer without introspection can't enumerate unknown linear-attn names... but — the ignore entries in the real checkpoint include all the linear-attn internals (943 entries = all non-expert modules enumerated by name!). I could carry over and adapt the workload's modules_to_not_convert: layer indices are embedded in the entries ('model.language_model.layers.0....'). My proxy keeps layers 0..7 — the entries for layers 0..7 in the workload's list are directly valid for the proxy (same module structure per layer, since the per-layer architecture is identical!). The workload's list covers 48 layers; keep entries with layer index < 8, plus non-layer entries (lm_head, embed, hyper_connection_mixer, etc.).\n\nHowever note: per-layer entry names reference module names that exist regardless of layer type (linear_attention's internal modules exist in those layers in both the workload and the proxy — the workload also has the same alternating pattern; layers 0-7 of the workload contain 6 linear-attn + 2 full-attn; the proxy makes all 8 linear-attn. Entries for full-attn-only modules on layers 3, 7 (indexer etc.) remain in the ignore list but no such modules exist in the proxy → harmless (exact match just doesn't match). Entries for linear-attn modules on layers 0..7 → match ✓. Entries for layers 8..47 → no such layers in the proxy → harmless.\n\nSo: for the workload-based config, ignore list = [e for e in workload ignore if no layer index OR layer index < LAYERS]. Regex for layer index extraction: r\"layers\\.(\\d+)\\.\". This gives us a COMPLETE and CORRECT ignore list in fallback mode without introspection! The experts (mlp.experts.*) are not in the workload's ignore list ✓ they remain quantized ✓.\n\nWait — one nuance: did the workload's ignore list include the PLE ngram embedding ('model.language_model.layers.1.ple...' etc.)? The workload's PLE is at layer idx 1 (ple_layer_ids [2]). If an entry exists → unquantized VocabParallelEmbedding path... but under the mmap-enabled proxy, ngram_embedding is MmapNgramEmbedding — quant_method is irrelevant (the mmap branch doesn't use it) ✓ harmless either way.\n\nFor template-based config (no workload list): keep the quantize-all risk note (or install nothing). Template mode is a last resort anyway.\n\nUpdate main()'s flow: replace the probe_ignore_semantics branch with the ignore list carried over from the workload:\n\n```python\n    introspected = try_fork_introspection(cfg)\n    ignore = None\n    if introspected:\n        ... literal prefixes (as is) + lm_head\n    else:\n        # Carry over the workload's own ignore list, restricted to layers\n        # that survive the shrink: exact-match semantics (the fork's default\n        # mode) + per-layer module names = the correct set without\n        # introspection.\n        base_qc = (json.loads((MODELS / \"config.json\").read_text())\n                   if (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file() else {}).get(\n                       \"quantization_config\") or {}\n        carry = base_qc.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\") or []\n        keep = []\n        for e in carry:\n            m = re.search(r\"layers\\.(\\d+)\\.\", e)\n            if m is None or int(m.group(1)) < LAYERS:\n                keep.append(e)\n        if keep:\n            ignore = keep + [\"lm_head\"] if \"lm_head\" not in keep else keep\n```\nHmm wait — but the ignore list must be installed before curated_weights computes quantize_linears ✓ it is (curated comes later). Also, the carried-over list is under the match_mode default \"exact\" — the workload's qc might specify ignored_layers_match_mode... let me check the workload's quantization_config — the keys printed earlier: quant_method, activation_scheme, weight_per_tensor, act_per_tensor, weight_block_size, modules_to_not_convert — no match_mode key → default exact ✓.\n\nAlso delete the now-unnecessary probe_ignore_semantics? Keep the function but unused? Remove the call and leave the function (or remove entirely — cleaner: remove the function, remove the call). Let me edit the flow block in main() to replace the elif probe branch with the carry-over logic, and remove probe_ignore_semantics entirely.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Since the fork uses exact/substring/suffix matching (with exact matching as the default), the workload's own 943-entry ignore list becomes the correct fallback source — we just need to narrow it down to layers that are preserved in the shrink. Replace the semantic probing with this carry-over:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02b9d677960b4e69a0507b64","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'scripts/make-proxy.sh'\nsrc = open(p).read()\n\ndef rep(old, new, label):\n    global src\n    assert src.count(old) == 1, f\"BAD: {label}\"\n    src = src.replace(old, new)\n    print(\"ok:\", label)\n\n# 1. drop the probe_ignore_semantics function entirely\nps_start = src.index('def probe_ignore_semantics():')\nps_end = src.index('def curated_weights(cfg):')\nsrc = src[:ps_start] + src[ps_end:]\nprint(\"ok: probe_ignore_semantics removed\")\n\n# 2. main() flow: carry-over ignore list from the workload when no introspection\nrep('''    elif probe_ignore_semantics():\n        # Regex semantics observed in the fork's Fp8Config: one negative-\n        # lookahead pattern skips every Linear except the routed experts.\n        ignore = [r\"(?s)^(?!.*\\\\.mlp\\\\.experts\\\\.).*$\"]\n    if ignore:\n        cfg[\"quantization_config\"][\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = ignore\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(f\"modules_to_not_convert installed ({len(ignore)} entries) — \"\n             \"non-expert linears stay unquantized, experts stay block-FP8\")\n    else:\n        note(\"RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed — quantize-all mode; \"\n             \"any quantized Linear whose name the fallback writer does not \"\n             \"know is uninitialized fp8 memory and could poison the logits\")''',\n'''    else:\n        # No introspection: carry the workload's own modules_to_not_convert\n        # over, restricted to the layers that survive the shrink. The fork\n        # matches it EXACTLY by module prefix (is_layer_skipped default\n        # mode), per-layer module names are identical between the workload\n        # and the proxy, and the routed experts are absent from the list by\n        # construction — so the carried set is correct without enumeration.\n        base_qc = {}\n        if (MODELS / \"config.json\").is_file():\n            base_qc = json.loads((MODELS / \"config.json\").read_text()).get(\n                \"quantization_config\") or {}\n        carry = base_qc.get(\"modules_to_not_convert\") or []\n        keep = [e for e in carry\n                if (lambda m: m is None or int(m.group(1)) < LAYERS)(\n                    re.search(r\"layers\\\\.(\\\\d+)\\\\.\", e))]\n        if keep and \"lm_head\" not in keep:\n            keep.append(\"lm_head\")\n        if keep:\n            ignore = keep\n    if ignore:\n        cfg[\"quantization_config\"][\"modules_to_not_convert\"] = ignore\n        (OUT / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))\n        note(f\"modules_to_not_convert installed ({len(ignore)} entries) — \"\n             \"non-expert linears stay unquantized, experts stay block-FP8\")\n    else:\n        note(\"RESIDUAL RISK: no ignore list installed — quantize-all mode; \"\n             \"any quantized Linear whose name the fallback writer does not \"\n             \"know is uninitialized fp8 memory and could poison the logits\")''',\n\"carry-over ignore\")\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(src)\nprint(\"DONE\")\nEOF\nbash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh && awk '/<<.PY.$/{f=1;next} /^PY$/{f=0} f' scripts/make-proxy.sh > /tmp/mp.py && python3 -m py_compile /tmp/mp.py && echo OK && bash scripts/make-proxy.sh 2>&1 | tail -4","timeout":600}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1862,"output":2146,"cacheRead":221184,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1178,"totalTokens":225192,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787996123577,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f5ef2388-7d68-4c81-889b-c28245ab8580","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02b9d677960b4e69a0507b64","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok: probe_ignore_sema