(vllm_sfx=\"in_proj_ba\") ✓ → stem = base[:-10] = \"...linear_attn.\"; then name = stem + \"a\" = \"...linear_attn.a\"?? That would be 'a', not 'baa'.\n\nHmm, the 'in_proj_baa' that the loader sees... the loader's mapper: checkpoint name → vllm name is via hf_to_vllm_mapper, probably {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\", ...}? Or the model's hf_to_vllm_mapper maps HF→vLLM, and I wrote the vLLM name, but the mapper was applied to it anyway: mapper orig_to_new_substr {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\"?}... my checkpoint name \"...in_proj_ba.weight\" → substring \"in_proj_b\" was found → replaced with \"in_proj_ba\"?? → \"...in_proj_baa.weight\"! Yes — the mapper contains something like {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\"} (HF stores them separately, in_proj_b? no...). The actual HF checkpoint probably has in_proj_b and in_proj_a tensors; mapper {\"in_proj_b\": \"in_proj_ba\", \"in_proj_a\": \"in_proj_ba\"}? Hmm.\n\nKey insight: checkpoint names must be the HF-side names (before the mapper is applied). My introspection wrote the vLLM-side names; the loader applies hf_to_vllm_mapper to checkpoint names → collision/duplication. The fused split via stacked_params_mapping produced HF names for qkv and such, but even those pass through the mapper again (for qkv, the mapper probably doesn't contain those substrings, so they survived).\n\nThe cleanest fix: apply the inverse mapping myself — better yet: read the model's hf_to_vllm_mapper (WeightsMapper) inside the introspection, and write the checkpoint names as the preimage: for each vLLM parameter name, compute hf_name = the inverse of the mapper. WeightsMapper has orig_to_new_substr etc. Inversion: for each vllm param name, apply the reverse substitution new→orig (if the substitution is unambiguous). Let me look at the model's mapper: model.hf_to_vllm_mapper (does Qwen4ExpModel define it?). During introspection, grab `getattr(model, 'hf_to_vllm_mapper', None)` and dump its contents — then decide. Let me run a simple container probe that i