e=0,video=0` to serve. In newer vLLM, the syntax accepts JSON or key=value pairs: `--limit-mm-per-prompt image=0,video=0`? In the new version, `--mm-processor-kwargs`... is the flag `--limit-mm-per-prompt` (the older one) or `--limit-mm-per-prompt` + `--limit-mm-per-...`? Let me quickly check the CLI help inside the container.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The OOM is the **vision encoder** profiled with multimodal dummies. Disable mm inputs via CLI limit. Check the exact flag name in this vLLM:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_36847428398f4eb9ae8893a5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"podman run --rm --entrypoint bash flashnext:dev -c \"vllm serve --help 2>/dev/null | grep -i 'limit-mm\\|mm-per-prompt' | head -6\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v WARNING","timeout":180}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":4414,"output":515,"cacheRead":272384,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":380,"totalTokens":277313,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787997896159,"responseId":"chatcmpl-0a254c2d-1801-4899-ad62-8c9419b59d29","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_36847428398f4eb9ae8893a5","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1787997928175},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`vllm serve --help` produced no output? Let's grab the complete help and try grepping for the multimodal (mm) limit options.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The vision encoder's dummy profile allocates 256 GiB. The proxy is text-only; cap mm inputs to zero. Find the exact flag:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d2cab4ba7c8f45abb42116c2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"podman run --rm --entrypoint bash flashnext:dev -c \"vllm serve --help 2>&1 | grep -B2 -A8 'limit_m